    {
        "title" : "bicep-deploy vs bicep-action: A Tool or a Workflow?",
        "date_published" : "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2026-11-16T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow/",
        "summary": " Azure/bicep-deploy vs bicep-action: A Tool or a Workflow? I maintain innofactororg/bicep-action, so I should say up front that I am not a neutral party. I am also the person who most needs this comparison to be honest, because every time someone evaluates bicep-action for a new estate, the first question is the obvious one: why not just use Microsoft\u0026rsquo;s?\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azurebicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azurebicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure/bicep-deploy vs bicep-action: A Tool or a Workflow?'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azurebicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure/bicep-deploy vs bicep-action: A Tool or a Workflow?\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action/hero.png\" alt=\"A tool versus a workflow\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI maintain \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003einnofactororg/bicep-action\u003c/a\u003e, so I should say up front that I am not a neutral party. I am also the person who most needs this comparison to be honest, because every time someone evaluates bicep-action for a new estate, the first question is the obvious one: why not just use Microsoft\u0026rsquo;s?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft\u0026rsquo;s answer to \u0026ldquo;how do I deploy Bicep from a pipeline\u0026rdquo; is \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Azure/bicep-deploy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/a\u003e, published as the \u003ccode\u003eazure/bicep-deploy@v2\u003c/code\u003e GitHub Action, with the same engine shipped to Azure DevOps as the \u003ccode\u003eBicepDeploy@0\u003c/code\u003e task. It is official, MIT-licensed, actively developed, and its latest release, v2.5.0 at the end of October 2026, added what-if support for deployment stacks. If you need to deploy a Bicep file to Azure from CI, it does that, cleanly and with Microsoft behind it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebicep-action answers a different question. It is not a deploy step; it is a deployment workflow. It plans every change in the pull request, posts the plan as a comment for people to review, runs quality gates, and deploys only the plan that was approved, on GitHub and Azure DevOps alike.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat distinction, a tool versus a workflow, explains almost every row in the grids below. Most of the time the right choice is obvious once you know which one you need. This post sets out what each does, where each is stronger, and where each falls short, using the current releases of both: \u003ccode\u003eazure/bicep-deploy\u003c/code\u003e v2.5.0 and \u003ccode\u003eBicepDeploy@0\u003c/code\u003e, and bicep-action \u003ccode\u003ev2026.11.13\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"two-different-shapes\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Two different shapes\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action/layers.png\" alt=\"The workflow sits on the primitive\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy is a primitive.\u003c/strong\u003e One step, one operation. You give it a \u003ccode\u003etype\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003edeployment\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003edeploymentStack\u003c/code\u003e), an \u003ccode\u003eoperation\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003ecreate\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003evalidate\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ewhatIf\u003c/code\u003e, and for stacks \u003ccode\u003edelete\u003c/code\u003e), a \u003ccode\u003escope\u003c/code\u003e, and your template and parameters. It compiles the Bicep, calls Azure Resource Manager through the Azure SDK for JavaScript, and writes the result to the log. Everything else about your pipeline, when it runs, who approves it, what happens to the what-if output, is yours to build around it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the hood it is a TypeScript Node 24 action. The engine lives in a shared package, \u003ccode\u003e@azure/bicep-deploy-common\u003c/code\u003e, which the Azure Pipelines \u003ccode\u003eBicepDeploy@0\u003c/code\u003e task also consumes, so both platforms get the same behaviour and the same input set. Authentication is separate: on GitHub you run \u003ccode\u003eazure/login\u003c/code\u003e first, and the action picks up the credential through a chained Azure credential; on Azure DevOps you pass a service connection.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ebicep-action is a workflow.\u003c/strong\u003e A plan action and a deploy action on GitHub, and a pipeline plus reusable stage templates on Azure DevOps, all running the same Bash scripts over the Azure CLI. The plan job builds, validates, runs the what-if, the delete gate, PSRule, a cost estimate and a snapshot check, then posts one comment on the pull request. The deploy job waits for an environment approval, deploys with the Bicep version and stack settings the plan used, and comments the result. Sign-in, provider registration and auto merge are part of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"at-a-glance\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  At a glance\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ebicep-action\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat it is\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eA deploy/validate/what-if step\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eA plan, review and deploy workflow\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMaintainer\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMicrosoft\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eInnofactor (open source)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLicence\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMIT\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBSD 3-Clause\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eGitHub\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eazure/bicep-deploy@v2\u003c/code\u003e action\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eplan\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003edeploy\u003c/code\u003e composite actions\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure DevOps\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eBicepDeploy@0\u003c/code\u003e task (same engine)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eFull pipeline and stage templates (same scripts)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eImplementation\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTypeScript, Node 24, Azure SDK for JS\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBash scripts over Azure CLI, Bicep CLI, jq\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRunner OS\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAny runner that runs Node actions\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLinux (Bash) runners\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAuthentication\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eazure/login\u003c/code\u003e (GitHub), service connection (Azure DevOps)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuilt in: OpenID Connect or secret (GitHub), service connection (Azure DevOps)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhere the what-if goes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eJob log, colour-formatted\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePull request comment, logs artifact, and \u003ccode\u003ewhatif-summary.json\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRelease model\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSemantic versions, \u003ccode\u003ev2\u003c/code\u003e major tag\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDated releases, \u003ccode\u003ev1\u003c/code\u003e tag\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"feature-coverage\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Feature coverage\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the grid most people want. \u0026ldquo;Build it yourself\u0026rdquo; means the capability is not in the tool but you can assemble it from the platform and your own scripts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eCapability\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ebicep-action\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eStandard deployments: resource group, subscription, management group, tenant\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeployment stacks: resource group, subscription, management group\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat-if for standard deployments\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat-if for stacks\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (since v2.5.0)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eValidate\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, with \u003ccode\u003evalidation-level\u003c/code\u003e (\u003ccode\u003eprovider\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003etemplate\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eproviderNoRbac\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (validate step)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003e.bicepparam\u003c/code\u003e and JSON parameter files\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eInline parameters\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (\u003ccode\u003eparameters\u003c/code\u003e input)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eExclude change types from what-if\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (\u003ccode\u003ewhat-if-exclude-change-types\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo input; ignore and no-change results are left out of the comment\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePin the Bicep version\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (\u003ccode\u003ebicep-version\u003c/code\u003e input)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAutomatic: the deploy uses the version the plan recorded\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTemplate outputs as step outputs\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, with \u003ccode\u003emasked-outputs\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo; the deploy action has no outputs\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSovereign clouds\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (\u003ccode\u003eenvironment\u003c/code\u003e input)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo input\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDelete a stack\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (\u003ccode\u003eoperation: delete\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat-if posted to the pull request\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, one comment per plan\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeploy result posted to the pull request\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eApproval before deploy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself with environments\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuilt in, through environments\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeploy exactly what was planned\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself (pass the same version and settings)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes: Bicep version, mode and stack settings enforced\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eApproval list for stack deletes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, delete gate with approved resource IDs\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eFail on non-deterministic deletes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, in delete modes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePolicy and best-practice checks\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePSRule for Azure, optional\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eCost estimate and budget gate\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure Cost Estimator, optional failing threshold\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSnapshot drift check\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAutomatic when a snapshot file is committed\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMachine-readable what-if summary\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003ewhatif-summary.json\u003c/code\u003e (counts, IDs, deterministic, blocked)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWait for a new subscription to become visible\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, retries that one error up to 30 minutes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRegister resource providers before deploy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, from the providers the plan found\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eKeep existing tag values (such as \u003ccode\u003ecreatedOn\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, scoped to resource groups you name\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAuto merge after deploy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes (GitHub)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eOne run at a time per target\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild it yourself\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDocumented concurrency pattern in every example\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMulti-environment examples\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSingle-environment examples\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTest → production examples for both platforms\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"deployment-stacks-side-by-side\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Deployment stacks, side by side\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStacks are where both projects have invested most, and where they differ in philosophy rather than coverage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eStack option\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ebicep-action\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAction on unmanaged resources\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSeparate settings for resources, resource groups and management groups (\u003ccode\u003edelete\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003edetach\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eOne setting: \u003ccode\u003edetachAll\u003c/code\u003e (default), \u003ccode\u003edeleteResources\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edeleteAll\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeny settings mode\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003enone\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edenyDelete\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edenyWriteAndDelete\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003enone\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edenyDelete\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003edenyWriteAndDelete\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeny settings excluded actions and principals\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeny settings on child scopes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBypass the stack out-of-sync error\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eStack description and tags\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeletes require an approval list\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRe-check deletes immediately before deploy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes, in delete modes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eStack settings must match the plan\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eYes\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft exposes more of the stack API, and if you need deny-setting exclusions for a break-glass principal, or per-scope control of what gets deleted, bicep-action cannot express that today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebicep-action, on the other hand, treats deletion as something that needs a reviewed commit. With \u003ccode\u003eaction-on-unmanage-resources: delete\u003c/code\u003e in Microsoft\u0026rsquo;s action, removing a resource from the template deletes it on the next \u003ccode\u003ecreate\u003c/code\u003e. That is the documented, intended behaviour of a stack. Whether a human saw the what-if first depends entirely on how you built the pipeline around it. In bicep-action, a delete mode fails the plan unless every resource the stack would delete is listed by ID in an approved-deletes file, and fails it outright if Azure cannot determine every resource that might be deleted. The deploy job then runs that check again against the current state, because the plan may be hours old.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"strengths-and-weaknesses-honestly\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Strengths and weaknesses, honestly\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action-a-tool-or-a-workflow/bicep-deploy-vs-bicep-action/choose.png\" alt=\"Choosing between composing and adopting\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"azurebicep-deploy\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azurebicep-deploy\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure/bicep-deploy'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Azure/bicep-deploy\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it is stronger\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt is Microsoft\u0026rsquo;s.\u003c/strong\u003e Official support, the Bicep team\u0026rsquo;s own contributors, a Contributor Licence Agreement process, CodeQL and dependency automation. For organisations that only adopt vendor-supported tooling, that ends the discussion.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt is light and portable.\u003c/strong\u003e A single Node step with no Azure CLI dependency, running on Linux, Windows or macOS runners, with the Bicep binary kept in the runner\u0026rsquo;s tool cache, so a self-hosted runner downloads each version once.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt exposes more of the API.\u003c/strong\u003e Validation levels, what-if change-type filters, inline parameters, sovereign clouds, stack delete, and the full set of stack and deny-setting options.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOutputs flow on.\u003c/strong\u003e Template outputs become step outputs, with masking for sensitive ones, so a later step can use the endpoint or resource ID the deployment produced.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSame engine on both platforms.\u003c/strong\u003e The GitHub Action and the \u003ccode\u003eBicepDeploy@0\u003c/code\u003e task share one package, so behaviour matches.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt composes.\u003c/strong\u003e Because it does one thing, it fits into whatever pipeline design you already have.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it falls short\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt is not a review workflow.\u003c/strong\u003e The what-if goes to the job log. Getting it in front of a reviewer, gating the deploy on that review, and posting the result back are all left to you.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlan and deploy are separate, unrelated runs.\u003c/strong\u003e The examples validate on pull requests and create on push to main. Nothing records what the what-if run used, so nothing guarantees the deployment matches what anyone looked at, unless you pin the Bicep version and settings yourself in both places.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeletes are not gated.\u003c/strong\u003e Stacks will delete what you tell them to, with no approval list and no check for hidden deletes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo quality gates.\u003c/strong\u003e Policy checks, cost estimates and drift checks are outside its scope.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eYoung in places.\u003c/strong\u003e Stack what-if arrived in v2.5.0 in October 2026, and the Azure DevOps task is still on major version 0.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"bicep-action\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#bicep-action\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'bicep-action'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    bicep-action\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it is stronger\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe workflow is the product.\u003c/strong\u003e Plan in the pull request, one comment with everything a reviewer needs, approval through the platform\u0026rsquo;s own environments, deployment of the approved plan, result posted back. Nothing to assemble.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeploy matches plan as closely as ARM allows.\u003c/strong\u003e The deploy installs the plan\u0026rsquo;s Bicep version, refuses different stack settings, and re-runs the delete gate. ARM has no saved plan file, so this is not a guarantee in the way Terraform\u0026rsquo;s is, but it closes the gaps a pipeline can close.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSafety by default.\u003c/strong\u003e Deletes need a reviewed list of IDs, non-deterministic deletes fail, PSRule and a cost budget can fail the plan, and a committed snapshot catches template drift, including drift caused by a Bicep release.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBuilt for the details that break real pipelines.\u003c/strong\u003e New subscriptions that are not visible yet, providers that are not registered, \u003ccode\u003ecreatedOn\u003c/code\u003e tags that should not be overwritten, masked values that garble a comment. Each feature exists because a production pipeline hit it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAutomation-ready.\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ccode\u003ewhatif-summary.json\u003c/code\u003e lets you auto-approve plans that are provably safe and route the rest to a person.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSame comments on GitHub and Azure DevOps,\u003c/strong\u003e including multi-environment stage templates for Azure DevOps.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere it falls short\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eIt is not Microsoft\u0026rsquo;s.\u003c/strong\u003e It is maintained by a partner team, and its priorities follow the production estates it runs in.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eLinux and Bash only.\u003c/strong\u003e It shells out to the Azure CLI, Bicep CLI, jq and Perl, so it needs a Linux runner and is slower to start than a single Node step.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNarrower API surface.\u003c/strong\u003e No sovereign-cloud input, no inline parameters, no validation-level or what-if filters, no stack delete operation, and fewer stack and deny-setting options.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo deployment outputs.\u003c/strong\u003e If a later step needs a value the template produced, you query Azure for it.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOpinionated.\u003c/strong\u003e It assumes pull requests, environments and approvals. If your process deploys on push without review, most of what it does is in the way.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAzure DevOps downloads the scripts at run time\u003c/strong\u003e from GitHub at the pinned release, so agents need to reach GitHub, and the template repository is referenced through a GitHub service connection.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"which-one-should-you-use\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Which one should you use?\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse \u003cstrong\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/strong\u003e when you need a deployment step inside a pipeline you already own: a release pipeline with its own gates, a tool that consumes deployment outputs, a sovereign cloud, Windows runners, stack options bicep-action does not expose, or a policy that only vendor-supported tooling is allowed. It is also the right building block if you want to design your own review workflow from scratch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse \u003cstrong\u003ebicep-action\u003c/strong\u003e when what you want is the workflow: changes reviewed as plans in pull requests, deletes approved in commits, cost and policy checked before anyone deploys, and the same experience on GitHub and Azure DevOps. It is the one to pick when the question is not \u0026ldquo;how do I deploy this file\u0026rdquo; but \u0026ldquo;how do I stop anyone deploying something nobody looked at\u0026rdquo;.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey are not really competitors. bicep-deploy is a good primitive, and bicep-action is a workflow that today happens to be built on the Azure CLI rather than on that primitive. The gaps in the grids above run in opposite directions, which is usually a sign that two tools are solving different problems well. If you are standing at that fork, start from the question you are actually trying to answer, and the grid will tell you the rest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"sources\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Sources\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/Azure/bicep-deploy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure/bicep-deploy\u003c/a\u003e: README, \u003ccode\u003eaction.yml\u003c/code\u003e, examples and release notes for v2.4.0 and v2.5.0\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/microsoft/azure-pipelines-tasks/tree/master/Tasks/BicepDeployV0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003eBicepDeployV0\u003c/code\u003e task\u003c/a\u003e in microsoft/azure-pipelines-tasks\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003einnofactororg/bicep-action\u003c/a\u003e: README, how it works, configuration reference and examples at \u003ccode\u003ev2026.11.13\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "bicep-action: Plan, Review and Deploy Bicep from Pull Requests",
        "date_published" : "2026-11-09T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2026-11-09T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/bicep-action-plan-review-and-deploy-bicep-from-pull-requests/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/bicep-action-plan-review-and-deploy-bicep-from-pull-requests/",
        "summary": " Terraform teams stopped deploying blind years ago. They open a pull request, a bot runs terraform plan and posts the result as a comment, a colleague reads exactly what will be created, changed and destroyed, and only then does anyone type atlantis apply. Most Bicep teams still merge and find out. The pipeline runs, the deployment succeeds or fails, and the first time anyone sees what Azure actually did is in the activity log afterwards.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/v1/docs/images/hero.png\" alt=\"Plan, review, deploy\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTerraform teams stopped deploying blind years ago. They open a pull request, a bot runs \u003ccode\u003eterraform plan\u003c/code\u003e and posts the result as a comment, a colleague reads exactly what will be created, changed and destroyed, and only then does anyone type \u003ccode\u003eatlantis apply\u003c/code\u003e. Most Bicep teams still merge and find out. The pipeline runs, the deployment succeeds or fails, and the first time anyone sees what Azure actually did is in the activity log afterwards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat gap is why we built \u003cstrong\u003ebicep-action\u003c/strong\u003e. It is a pair of GitHub actions and an Azure DevOps pipeline that run Bicep the way Atlantis runs Terraform. Every change is planned in the pull request, the plan is reviewed by people, and only the approved plan is deployed. GitHub and Azure DevOps run the same shell scripts and post the same pull request comments, so a team can move between the two platforms without relearning anything.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is free. The code and documentation are published under the BSD 3-Clause licence in a public repository, \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003einnofactororg/bicep-action\u003c/a\u003e, and you can pin it, fork it or read every line of it. It is also not a weekend project. The first commit was in November 2023, it has shipped fifteen releases since, and it is the mandated pipeline for every Bicep workload repository in one of the larger managed Azure estates we run, on Azure DevOps, as well as the pipeline behind the workloads our subscription-vending engine creates. Every fix in this week\u0026rsquo;s release, \u003ccode\u003ev2026.11.13\u003c/code\u003e, came from something a production pipeline hit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis post walks through what it does, how it compares with Atlantis, and how to run it for one environment or for several.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"what-happens-when-you-open-a-pull-request\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  What happens when you open a pull request\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe flow has two jobs and a person in between.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"mermaid-diagram my-8\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"mermaid pele\" hidden\u003esequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Dev as Engineer\n    participant PR as Pull request\n    participant Plan as Plan job\n    participant Rev as Reviewer\n    participant Dep as Deploy job\n    participant Az as Azure\n    Dev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Push a branch, open a pull request\n    PR-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Plan: Trigger the workflow or pipeline\n    Plan-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Az: Build, validate, what-if (read only)\n    Plan-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: One comment: what-if, rules, cost, snapshot\n    Rev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Read the plan\n    Rev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Dep: Approve the environment\n    Dep-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Az: Deploy with the plan\u0026#39;s Bicep version and settings\n    Dep-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Comment the result (and auto merge on GitHub)\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdetails class=\"mermaid-source\"\u003e\u003csummary\u003eDiagram source\u003c/summary\u003e\u003cpre\u003esequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Dev as Engineer\n    participant PR as Pull request\n    participant Plan as Plan job\n    participant Rev as Reviewer\n    participant Dep as Deploy job\n    participant Az as Azure\n    Dev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Push a branch, open a pull request\n    PR-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Plan: Trigger the workflow or pipeline\n    Plan-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Az: Build, validate, what-if (read only)\n    Plan-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: One comment: what-if, rules, cost, snapshot\n    Rev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Read the plan\n    Rev-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Dep: Approve the environment\n    Dep-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;Az: Deploy with the plan\u0026#39;s Bicep version and settings\n    Dep-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;PR: Comment the result (and auto merge on GitHub)\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cfigcaption data-mermaid-auto-caption\u003eFigure 3\u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eplan job\u003c/strong\u003e only reads from Azure. It compiles the template, validates it, asks Azure what the deployment would change, runs the quality checks, and posts everything as \u003cstrong\u003eone comment\u003c/strong\u003e on the pull request. Any failed check fails the plan, and the deployment never starts.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe approval step uses what each platform already has. On GitHub it is an environment with required reviewers; on Azure DevOps it is an environment with an approval check. There is no bespoke approval mechanism to learn or secure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003edeploy job\u003c/strong\u003e runs only after a successful plan and an approval. It deploys, comments the result on the same pull request, and on GitHub can turn on auto merge, so the branch is merged the moment the deployment succeeds. Main stays a record of what is actually deployed, which is the same property Atlantis users rely on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"what-the-plan-checks\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  What the plan checks\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/v1/docs/images/plan-gates.png\" alt=\"The checks in the plan job\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA plan is more than a what-if. The plan job runs a sequence of gates, each of which can fail the plan:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eStep\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eWhat it checks\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eFails the plan when\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBicep build\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThe template and \u003ccode\u003e.bicepparam\u003c/code\u003e compile with the latest Bicep release\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eIt does not compile\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eValidate\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eaz deployment \u0026lt;scope\u0026gt; validate\u003c/code\u003e, and which resource providers the template needs\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure rejects the template\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat-if\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhat Azure would create, modify or delete; with stacks, what it would detach or delete\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThe what-if fails, or a stack would delete something not approved\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePSRule \u003cem\u003e(opt-in)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePSRule for Azure against the Well-Architected rules\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eA rule fails\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eCost estimate\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThe monthly cost of the compiled template\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eIt exceeds your threshold\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBicep snapshot \u003cem\u003e(automatic)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThe template against a committed snapshot of every resource it produces\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThe template no longer matches the snapshot\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe what-if is the heart of the comment. It is posted as a coloured diff, \u003ccode\u003e+\u003c/code\u003e for create, \u003ccode\u003e-\u003c/code\u003e for delete, \u003ccode\u003e!\u003c/code\u003e for modify, with property-level changes listed under each resource and long results folded away. Reviewers read infrastructure changes the way they read code changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"deletes-are-approved-in-a-commit-not-discovered-afterwards\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#deletes-are-approved-in-a-commit-not-discovered-afterwards\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Deletes are approved in a commit, not discovered afterwards'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Deletes are approved in a commit, not discovered afterwards\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe single most valuable thing bicep-action does is make deletes visible and deliberate. With \u003ccode\u003edeployment_mode: stack\u003c/code\u003e, the template is deployed as an Azure \u003cstrong\u003edeployment stack\u003c/strong\u003e, which means Azure knows which resources belong to the template. When you remove something from the code, the stack what-if shows exactly what would be detached or deleted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/v1/docs/images/stacks.png\" alt=\"A stack creates, detaches, and deletes only when approved\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe default behaviour for removed resources, \u003ccode\u003edetachAll\u003c/code\u003e, never deletes anything; the resource is simply released from the stack. If you choose \u003ccode\u003edeleteResources\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003edeleteAll\u003c/code\u003e, a \u003cstrong\u003edelete gate\u003c/strong\u003e applies: the plan fails unless every resource the stack would delete is listed, by resource ID, in an approved-deletes file in the repository. Deleting a production resource therefore needs a reviewed commit that names it. If Azure cannot determine every resource that might be deleted, because some names are only known at deploy time, the plan fails rather than risk a hidden delete.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"a-snapshot-that-puts-the-real-change-in-the-diff\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#a-snapshot-that-puts-the-real-change-in-the-diff\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'A snapshot that puts the real change in the diff'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    A snapshot that puts the real change in the diff\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eBicep can now produce a \u003cstrong\u003esnapshot\u003c/strong\u003e: a fully expanded list of every resource the template produces, computed offline. Commit it next to your parameters file and the plan compares the template with it. If the template\u0026rsquo;s output changes, the plan fails until you regenerate and commit the snapshot, at which point the exact resource-level change sits in the pull request diff. A refactor that claims to change nothing can prove it. A Bicep release that silently changes compiled output gets reviewed like any other change.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"cost-before-you-spend-it\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#cost-before-you-spend-it\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Cost before you spend it'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Cost before you spend it\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe plan runs the Azure Cost Estimator against the compiled template and puts the monthly estimate in the comment. Set a \u003ccode\u003ecost_threshold\u003c/code\u003e and the plan fails when the estimate exceeds it, or when the estimate cannot be made, because a budget you cannot check is not a budget. Leave it at the default and the estimate is report-only.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"deploy-exactly-what-was-planned\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Deploy exactly what was planned\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/v1/docs/images/plan-equals-deploy.png\" alt=\"The deployment matches the plan\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA reviewer approves a specific plan. If the deployment can drift from that plan, the review is worth very little. bicep-action closes the obvious gaps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe same Bicep version.\u003c/strong\u003e The plan records the Bicep CLI version it compiled with. The deploy job installs that version, even if a newer one shipped while the plan waited for approval.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe same mode and stack settings.\u003c/strong\u003e The plan records its deployment mode and stack settings, and a deployment with different settings fails and asks for a new plan.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeletes checked again.\u003c/strong\u003e With a delete mode, the deploy job runs the delete gate again against the current state, immediately before deploying, because a plan can be hours old.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFresh state where it matters.\u003c/strong\u003e Values read from Azure during planning, such as existing tag values, are read again at deploy time rather than reused.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Azure DevOps the deploy stage picks these values up from the plan stage automatically. On GitHub you pass the plan action\u0026rsquo;s outputs to the deploy action, which every example in the repository already does.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"how-it-compares-with-atlantis\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  How it compares with Atlantis\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ebicep-action exists because Atlantis is right about the workflow. The comparison is worth making honestly, because the platforms are different in ways that matter.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003e\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eAtlantis\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ebicep-action\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLanguage\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTerraform and OpenTofu\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure Bicep (and ARM JSON)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWhere it runs\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eA self-hosted server that receives webhooks\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eInside your existing GitHub Actions or Azure DevOps runners; nothing to host\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePlan\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e\u003ccode\u003eterraform plan\u003c/code\u003e, posted as a comment\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuild, validate, what-if, PSRule, cost and snapshot, posted as one comment\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eApply trigger\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAn \u003ccode\u003eatlantis apply\u003c/code\u003e comment, subject to apply requirements\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAn environment approval in the platform\u0026rsquo;s own UI\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePlan equals apply\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eApplies the saved plan file\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNo saved plan exists in ARM; the Bicep version and settings are pinned and deletes are re-checked\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLocking\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePer project or directory, held until the pull request merges or is unlocked\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eA concurrency group per Azure target on GitHub; one run at a time, deployments never cancelled\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePolicy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eConftest/OPA policy checks\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePSRule for Azure, with your own baseline and rules\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eCost\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eNot built in\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure Cost Estimator, with an optional failing threshold\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDeletes\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eShown as destroys in the plan\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eStack what-if plus a delete gate that requires approved IDs\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLicence\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eApache 2.0\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBSD 3-Clause\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo rows deserve a closer look.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003ePlan equals apply.\u003c/strong\u003e Atlantis applies the exact plan file it showed you, which is the strongest guarantee available. ARM has no equivalent: a what-if is a preview, not a contract, and Azure re-evaluates the template at deployment time. bicep-action gets as close as the platform allows by pinning the compiler and settings and re-running the delete gate, but if something in Azure changes between plan and deploy, the deployment acts on the new state. Treat an old plan with suspicion, and re-plan when in doubt.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNo server.\u003c/strong\u003e Atlantis is a long-running service with credentials, a webhook endpoint and its own user interface, and it has to be patched, scaled and secured like any other. bicep-action has no running component. Credentials are your platform\u0026rsquo;s own workload identity federation or service connection, approvals are your platform\u0026rsquo;s environments, logs are your platform\u0026rsquo;s artifacts. The attack surface is the one you already have.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe lock deserves a note too. On GitHub, each example puts the workflow in a concurrency group per Azure target with \u003ccode\u003ecancel-in-progress: false\u003c/code\u003e. A second pull request waits until the first is deployed or rejected, so a deployment never runs over changes it did not plan. GitHub keeps one waiting run per group, so a newer waiting run replaces an older one, which is usually what you want.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-details-that-usually-break-pipelines\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The details that usually break pipelines\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA few features exist because production pipelines kept tripping over the same things.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNew subscriptions.\u003c/strong\u003e A pipeline that runs against a subscription created minutes earlier, which is exactly what subscription vending produces, often cannot see it yet, or its role assignments have not propagated. The scripts retry that one error, the subscription not being visible, for up to \u003ccode\u003esubscription_wait_minutes\u003c/code\u003e (30 by default), logging what the identity can see on each attempt. Any other error, such as a missing permission, still fails at once. In real runs we have watched that window last more than an hour.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTags that should keep their first value.\u003c/strong\u003e Tags such as \u003ccode\u003ecreatedOn\u003c/code\u003e are meant to record when a resource was first deployed, but a template that sets them overwrites them on every run. The existing tags feature reads chosen tag values from the resources already in Azure, scoped to the resource groups you name, and passes them into the template so they survive redeployment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAutomation on top of the plan.\u003c/strong\u003e Every plan writes \u003ccode\u003ewhatif-summary.json\u003c/code\u003e: counts of creates, modifies, deletes, detaches and unsupported changes, the IDs involved, and whether the result was deterministic. One of the examples uses it to auto-approve plans that are provably safe, such as a plan with no deletes, no detaches, no unsupported changes and a deterministic result, and routes everything else to a human.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSecrets in the comment.\u003c/strong\u003e Azure masks secret values in the what-if. This week\u0026rsquo;s release makes sure those masked values render correctly in Azure DevOps comments, where a run of asterisks used to turn the rest of the what-if into an unreadable block of comment colouring. It is a small fix, and a good example of why the project moves the way it does: it came from a reviewer struggling to read a real production plan.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"one-environment\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  One environment\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn GitHub, a single-environment setup is a plan job and a deploy job. The plan:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 12 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003euses\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eactions/checkout@v7\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eplan\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003euses\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einnofactororg/bicep-action/.github/actions/plan@v1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ewith\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eazure_client_id\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e${{ env.azure_client_id }}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eazure_subscription_id\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e${{ env.azure_subscription_id }}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eazure_tenant_id\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e${{ env.azure_tenant_id }}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edeployment_mode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003estack\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003elocation\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ewesteurope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003escope\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003esub\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etemplate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einfra/main.bicep\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etemplate_parameters\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einfra/main.bicepparam\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe deploy job runs in a GitHub environment with required reviewers and passes the plan\u0026rsquo;s outputs, \u003ccode\u003eproviders\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ebicep_version\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003estack_settings\u003c/code\u003e, to the deploy action. The \u003ccode\u003erecommended.yml\u003c/code\u003e example in the repository is the complete version, with OpenID Connect sign-in, the concurrency lock, auto merge and the optional checks turned on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Azure DevOps, copy \u003ccode\u003ems.azure.deploy.yml\u003c/code\u003e into the repository, set its variables, point an environment with an approval check at it, and add a build validation branch policy so it runs on every pull request. Every step is inline, so the single-environment pipeline needs no template repository. The pipeline downloads the scripts at the release you pin in \u003ccode\u003eWORKFLOW_VERSION\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"many-environments\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Many environments\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReal workloads have test and production, often more, each in its own subscription. bicep-action handles that by repeating the plan-and-deploy pair per environment and chaining them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn GitHub, the multi-environment example runs test first and production second, all from one pull request:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eplan_test → deploy_test (environment: test) → plan_prod → deploy_prod (environment: production)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach environment has its own subscription, parameters file (\u003ccode\u003emain.test.bicepparam\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003emain.prod.bicepparam\u003c/code\u003e), stack name, cost threshold, GitHub environment with its own reviewers and federated credential, and \u003ccode\u003eartifact_identifier\u003c/code\u003e, so the logs of the two runs do not collide. Production is planned only after test has deployed, so the production plan reflects a change that has already been proven once, and only the production deploy merges the pull request.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn Azure DevOps, the repository ships reusable \u003cstrong\u003estage templates\u003c/strong\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eplan-stage.yml\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003edeploy-stage.yml\u003c/code\u003e. A multi-environment pipeline references the bicep-action repository as a resource, pinned to a release tag, and calls the templates once per environment with that environment\u0026rsquo;s variables:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 33 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0178041d16e852b9168ffe8cf474f007-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eresources\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003erepositories\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003erepository\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ebicep_action\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003egithub\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einnofactororg/bicep-action\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eref\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003erefs/tags/v1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eendpoint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003egithub_connection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estages\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etemplate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e.azuredevops/templates/plan-stage.yml@bicep_action\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eparameters\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estageName\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ePlan_test\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eserviceConnection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest_arm_connection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003evariables\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eARTIFACT_IDENTIFIER\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSUBSCRIPTION_ID\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eIN_TEMPLATE_PARAMS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einfra/main.test.bicepparam\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSTACK_NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eapp-test\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etemplate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e.azuredevops/templates/deploy-stage.yml@bicep_action\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eparameters\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estageName\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eDeploy_test\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edependsOn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ePlan_test]\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eplanStageName\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ePlan_test\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eenvironmentName\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eserviceConnection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest_arm_connection\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003evariables\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eARTIFACT_IDENTIFIER\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSUBSCRIPTION_ID\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eIN_TEMPLATE_PARAMS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003einfra/main.test.bicepparam\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e        \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSTACK_NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eapp-test\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e# ...then Plan_prod and Deploy_prod the same way, with the production values\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eShared settings live in pipeline variables or a variable group, and per-environment values in each stage\u0026rsquo;s \u003ccode\u003evariables\u003c/code\u003e, which take precedence. Each environment gets its own service connection and its own approval check, so production reviewers approve production and nobody else.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"getting-started\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Getting started\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe repository has everything needed to adopt it, written to be copied rather than interpreted:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/blob/main/docs/how-it-works.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eHow it works\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: the plan and deploy jobs step by step, stacks and the delete gate, the snapshot, cost, PSRule and the summary file.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/blob/main/docs/configuration.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eConfiguration reference\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: every GitHub input and its Azure DevOps variable side by side, with defaults and recommended settings.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSetup guides\u003c/strong\u003e for \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/blob/main/docs/setup-github.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eGitHub\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/blob/main/docs/setup-azure-devops.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure DevOps\u003c/a\u003e: environments, federated credentials, roles and branch policies.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/tree/main/docs/examples\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eExamples\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: recommended, minimal, multi-environment and auto-approval workflows for GitHub, and multi-environment and variable-group pipelines for Azure DevOps.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/bicep-action/blob/main/docs/troubleshooting.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eTroubleshooting\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e: the messages you might see and what to do about them.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePin a release: \u003ccode\u003e@v1\u003c/code\u003e on GitHub and \u003ccode\u003eWORKFLOW_VERSION: v1\u003c/code\u003e on Azure DevOps follow the latest release, or pin a dated tag such as \u003ccode\u003ev2026.11.13\u003c/code\u003e if you want to choose when to move.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you run Bicep in production and nobody reads what it will do before it does it, this is the cheapest fix you will find. It costs nothing, it runs in the CI you already have, and the first pull request it plans will show you something you did not know your template was about to change.\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Quota Groups: Recycling Capacity You Already Own",
        "date_published" : "2026-11-02T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2026-11-02T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-quota-groups-recycling-capacity-you-already-own/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-quota-groups-recycling-capacity-you-already-own/",
        "summary": "The most expensive vCPU in Azure is the one you already had approved, gave back by accident, and now have to ask for again. That is exactly what happens every time an old subscription is cancelled. Years of quota increases, each one a support ticket, a business justification and a few days of waiting, disappear with the subscription. Meanwhile the brand-new subscription that replaces it starts life with default limits, in a region where capacity is tight, and the first deployment into it fails with a quota error the platform team then has to chase.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eThe most expensive vCPU in Azure is the one you already had approved, gave back by accident, and now have to ask for again. That is exactly what happens every time an old subscription is cancelled. Years of quota increases, each one a support ticket, a business justification and a few days of waiting, disappear with the subscription. Meanwhile the brand-new subscription that replaces it starts life with default limits, in a region where capacity is tight, and the first deployment into it fails with a quota error the platform team then has to chase.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor most of Azure\u0026rsquo;s history there was no way around this. Quota was a property of the subscription: granted to it, enforced on it, and lost with it. Azure Quota Groups change that. They lift compute quota from the subscription to a group object, so quota can be pooled across subscriptions, handed back to the pool when a workload shrinks or is retired, and handed out again to a new subscription without a ticket.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI spend a lot of my time on landing zones and on subscription vending, the automated process that creates a subscription, places it in the management group hierarchy, wires it to the network and hands it to a team with a working deployment pipeline. In our case that engine is called Concierge. When a reviewer asked recently whether we should be putting every new subscription into a quota group as part of vending, especially as older subscriptions are being decommissioned, it was the right question, and working through the answer properly is what this post is about.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuota Groups fit the problem well. They are also more subtle than the announcement suggests, and three limits decide whether you can use them at all. They only accept Enterprise Agreement and Microsoft Customer Agreement subscriptions, which rules out anything bought through a Cloud Solution Provider. They only cover IaaS compute quota, the vCPU limits per VM family. And they do nothing for region or zone access, which is a separate gate that fails in a confusingly similar way. If you run vending through a CSP partner, the first of those ends the conversation before it starts, and you need a different design.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, what quota actually is, because everything after depends on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"quota-capacity-and-access-are-three-different-gates\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Quota, capacity and access are three different gates\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a deployment fails to get compute in Azure, it is usually one of three things, and they are often confused.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuota\u003c/strong\u003e is a limit Azure enforces on your subscription: how many vCPUs of a given VM family you may run in a given region, plus a total regional vCPU limit across families. It is a number on your subscription, it is checked at deployment time, and exceeding it fails the deployment with a quota error such as \u003ccode\u003eQuotaExceeded\u003c/code\u003e or an \u003ccode\u003eOperationNotAllowed\u003c/code\u003e that names the family and the limit. Quota is not capacity. A high limit does not mean the hardware is free; it means Azure has agreed you may use up to that much.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCapacity\u003c/strong\u003e is whether the region actually has the hardware to place your VM right now. When it does not, you get an allocation failure such as \u003ccode\u003eAllocationFailed\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eZonalAllocationFailed\u003c/code\u003e, even with plenty of quota. Quota increase requests are themselves checked against capacity, which is why increases in busy regions can be rejected or take a long time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAccess\u003c/strong\u003e is whether your subscription may use a region, a zone or a VM size at all. Some regions are reserved and need an explicit access request. Within an open region, a specific size can be restricted for a specific subscription, which you can see in the SKU list: \u003ccode\u003eaz vm list-skus --location \u0026lt;region\u0026gt; --size \u0026lt;size\u0026gt; --all\u003c/code\u003e returns a \u003ccode\u003erestrictions\u003c/code\u003e block, with a \u003ccode\u003etype\u003c/code\u003e of \u003ccode\u003eLocation\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eZone\u003c/code\u003e and a \u003ccode\u003ereasonCode\u003c/code\u003e of \u003ccode\u003eNotAvailableForSubscription\u003c/code\u003e. A deployment that hits it fails with \u003ccode\u003eSkuNotAvailable\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuota Groups address the first gate only. Microsoft says so plainly in the documentation: \u0026ldquo;Quota Groups addresses the quota management pain point, it does not address the regional and or zonal access pain point.\u0026rdquo; Keep that sentence in mind, because it comes back when we get to automation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"what-a-quota-group-actually-is\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  What a quota group actually is\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA quota group is an Azure Resource Manager object of type \u003ccode\u003eMicrosoft.Quota/groupQuotas\u003c/code\u003e. It is created at a \u003cstrong\u003emanagement group\u003c/strong\u003e scope and inherits its permissions from that management group, but it is not tied to the hierarchy beneath it. Membership is explicit: you add subscriptions to it through the API, from any management group, and nothing is synchronised automatically. A subscription can belong to one quota group at a time.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreating one is a single \u003ccode\u003ePUT\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ehttp\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003ePUT https://management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Management/managementGroups/{mgId}/providers/Microsoft.Quota/groupQuotas/{groupName}?api-version=2025-03-01\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e{\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e  \u0026#34;properties\u0026#34;: {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e    \u0026#34;displayName\u0026#34;: \u0026#34;platform-compute-pool\u0026#34;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdding a subscription is another \u003ccode\u003ePUT\u003c/code\u003e, with no body:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ehttp\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003ePUT https://management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Management/managementGroups/{mgId}/providers/Microsoft.Quota/groupQuotas/{groupName}/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}?api-version=2025-03-01\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth return \u003ccode\u003eprovisioningState: ACCEPTED\u003c/code\u003e and complete asynchronously, so any automation has to poll before it moves on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo prerequisites catch people out. Every member subscription needs the \u003ccode\u003eMicrosoft.Quota\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eMicrosoft.Compute\u003c/code\u003e resource providers registered before it is added. And the roles are split across two scopes: \u003cem\u003eGroupQuota Request Operator\u003c/em\u003e on the management group that holds the group, to create it and manage its limit, and \u003cem\u003eQuota Request Operator\u003c/em\u003e on each participating subscription, to move quota in and out of it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-group-limit-starts-at-zero\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-group-limit-starts-at-zero\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The group limit starts at zero'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The group limit starts at zero\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA new quota group has a limit of \u003cstrong\u003ezero\u003c/strong\u003e, and that surprises most people. Adding subscriptions does not change that. The documentation is explicit: \u0026ldquo;When added to the group, subscriptions carry their existing quota and usage. The subscriptions\u0026rsquo; quota isn\u0026rsquo;t manipulated when added to a group. Subscription quota remains separate from the group limit.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the group limit is its own pot, separate from the members\u0026rsquo; limits, and you fill it in one of two ways:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeallocation.\u003c/strong\u003e You move unused quota from a member subscription into the group.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eA group limit increase.\u003c/strong\u003e You ask Microsoft for more quota at the group level, for one region and one VM family at a time. It goes through the same capacity checks as a subscription request, and if it is rejected you fall back to a support ticket raised from the quota group blade. If it is approved, the quota is stamped on the group rather than on any one subscription.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"deployments-still-check-the-subscription\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#deployments-still-check-the-subscription\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Deployments still check the subscription'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Deployments still check the subscription\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe other thing to internalise is where the check happens. The documentation says: \u0026ldquo;When deploying resources the quota check at runtime is done against the subscription quota.\u0026rdquo; The group is never consulted when you deploy. Quota in the group is inventory; it does nothing until you \u003cstrong\u003eallocate\u003c/strong\u003e it to a subscription.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat single fact shapes every automated flow. Putting a new subscription into a group gives it nothing. Somebody, or something, has to move quota from the group to the subscription before the first deployment, or that deployment fails exactly as it would have without a group.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"allocation-and-deallocation-are-absolute-not-deltas\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Allocation and deallocation are absolute, not deltas\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMoving quota in either direction uses the same call, and the semantics are easy to get wrong. You \u003ccode\u003ePATCH\u003c/code\u003e the subscription\u0026rsquo;s \u003cstrong\u003eallocation\u003c/strong\u003e for a region, and you set the \u003cstrong\u003enew absolute limit\u003c/strong\u003e you want the subscription to have, not the amount to move.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ehttp\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 14 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-e8d867dcb5c0ec7661b6e9082b398e76-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003ePATCH https://management.azure.com/providers/Microsoft.Management/managementGroups/{mgId}/subscriptions/{subscriptionId}/providers/Microsoft.Quota/groupQuotas/{groupName}/resourceProviders/Microsoft.Compute/quotaAllocations/{location}?api-version=2025-03-01\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e{\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e  \u0026#34;properties\u0026#34;: {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e    \u0026#34;value\u0026#34;: [\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e      {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e        \u0026#34;properties\u0026#34;: {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e          \u0026#34;resourceName\u0026#34;: \u0026#34;standardddv4family\u0026#34;,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e          \u0026#34;limit\u0026#34;: 50\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e        }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e      }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e    ]\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the subscription currently has 60 vCPUs of that family, setting 50 \u003cstrong\u003edeallocates\u003c/strong\u003e 10 to the group. If it has 40, setting 50 \u003cstrong\u003eallocates\u003c/strong\u003e 10 from the group. The direction is implied by the difference between the current limit and the one you send.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo constraints follow from that. You cannot deallocate below what the subscription is using, so quota is only reclaimable once the VMs consuming it are gone. And you cannot allocate more than the group has available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReading the state back is where the vocabulary matters. The allocation snapshot for a subscription returns its \u003ccode\u003elimit\u003c/code\u003e and a \u003ccode\u003eshareableQuota\u003c/code\u003e; a value of \u003ccode\u003e-10\u003c/code\u003e means that subscription has given 10 vCPUs to the group. The group\u0026rsquo;s own view, from \u003ccode\u003egroupQuotaLimits/{location}\u003c/code\u003e, returns three numbers that are easy to conflate:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003elimit\u003c/code\u003e is what has been \u003cstrong\u003estamped\u003c/strong\u003e on the group by approved increase requests.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eavailableLimit\u003c/code\u003e is what the group can \u003cstrong\u003ehand out right now\u003c/strong\u003e, including quota deallocated from members.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003eallocatedToSubscriptions\u003c/code\u003e lists each member\u0026rsquo;s net movement, negative for subscriptions that have given quota back.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the documentation\u0026rsquo;s own example, a group with a stamped \u003ccode\u003elimit\u003c/code\u003e of 40 shows an \u003ccode\u003eavailableLimit\u003c/code\u003e of 50, because a member had already deallocated 10. If you build reporting or automation on top of this API, \u003ccode\u003eavailableLimit\u003c/code\u003e is the number that answers \u0026ldquo;can I allocate this?\u0026rdquo;.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"recycling-quota-from-decommissioned-environments\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Recycling quota from decommissioned environments\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDecommissioning is the scenario that prompted the question, and it is where Quota Groups pay for themselves. Most estates that have been in Azure for a while are carrying subscriptions that are being consolidated or retired: old per-environment subscriptions, a previous generation of landing zone, workloads moving to a new hierarchy. Each one holds quota that somebody fought for.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe decommissioning flow with a quota group looks like this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"mermaid-diagram my-8\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"mermaid pele\" hidden\u003eflowchart LR\n    A[Old subscription\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;in the group] --\u0026gt;|1. Remove workloads| B[Usage falls]\n    B --\u0026gt;|2. PATCH allocation\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;limit = usage| C[Unused quota\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;moves to group]\n    C --\u0026gt;|3. DELETE membership| D[Subscription leaves group]\n    D --\u0026gt;|4. Cancel| E[Subscription gone]\n    C --\u0026gt; P[(Group pool\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;availableLimit)]\n    P --\u0026gt;|5. PATCH allocation\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;on new subscription| N[New subscription\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;ready to deploy]\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdetails class=\"mermaid-source\"\u003e\u003csummary\u003eDiagram source\u003c/summary\u003e\u003cpre\u003eflowchart LR\n    A[Old subscription\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;in the group] --\u0026gt;|1. Remove workloads| B[Usage falls]\n    B --\u0026gt;|2. PATCH allocation\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;limit = usage| C[Unused quota\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;moves to group]\n    C --\u0026gt;|3. DELETE membership| D[Subscription leaves group]\n    D --\u0026gt;|4. Cancel| E[Subscription gone]\n    C --\u0026gt; P[(Group pool\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;availableLimit)]\n    P --\u0026gt;|5. PATCH allocation\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;on new subscription| N[New subscription\u0026lt;br/\u0026gt;ready to deploy]\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cfigcaption data-mermaid-auto-caption\u003eFigure 5\u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe order matters, and it is the order most decommissioning runbooks get wrong if they were written before quota groups existed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJoin the old subscription to the group first.\u003c/strong\u003e A subscription that is not a member cannot deallocate into it. If your retiring subscriptions predate the group, adding them is step zero.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRemove the workloads.\u003c/strong\u003e Deallocation cannot go below usage, so the VMs, scale sets and anything else consuming the family have to be gone first.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eDeallocate per region and per family.\u003c/strong\u003e Set each allocation to the remaining usage, normally zero. This is one \u003ccode\u003ePATCH\u003c/code\u003e per region, with one entry per family in the body. Check \u003ccode\u003eshareableQuota\u003c/code\u003e afterwards.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRemove the subscription from the group.\u003c/strong\u003e On removal, \u0026ldquo;subscriptions carry their existing quota and usage. The group limit isn\u0026rsquo;t manipulated based on subscription removal.\u0026rdquo; Quota already deallocated stays in the pool.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOnly then cancel the subscription.\u003c/strong\u003e Cancel first and the quota goes with it, which is exactly what you were trying to avoid.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDone in this order, a retirement programme becomes a quota source rather than a quota sink. Every subscription you close tops up the pool that the next one draws from, and the support tickets you raised years ago keep paying out.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne governance point is easy to miss. Deleting the management group that holds a quota group loses access to its limit, recoverable only by recreating a management group with the same ID. If you are reshaping your hierarchy at the same time as retiring subscriptions, which is common, put the quota group on a management group that is not going anywhere. A dedicated platform management group near the root is a better home than a landing-zone group that might be renamed or collapsed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"how-it-would-fit-an-automated-vending-flow\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  How it would fit an automated vending flow\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA subscription-vending engine like Concierge runs a fixed sequence for every order: create the subscription, place it in the right management group, allocate its address space, create its repository and pipeline, give its deployment identity the access it needs, and hand over. The first deployment is the workload\u0026rsquo;s own pipeline, running as its own identity. That is deliberate, because the first run is the proof that the pipeline works. It also means that if the subscription lacks the quota the workload needs, the order is reported as complete and then the very first thing the team does fails.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith a quota group available, the vending flow gains one step between placement and handover:\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"mermaid-diagram my-8\"\u003e\n\u003cpre class=\"mermaid pele\" hidden\u003esequenceDiagram\n    participant O as Order\n    participant V as Vending engine\n    participant S as New subscription\n    participant G as Quota group\n    participant P as Workload pipeline\n    O-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;V: request (architype, region, quota needs)\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: create, place in management group\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: register Microsoft.Quota, Microsoft.Compute\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: PUT groupQuotas/{g}/subscriptions/{sub}\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: GET groupQuotaLimits/{region} (availableLimit)\n    alt pool has enough\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: PATCH quotaAllocations/{region} (absolute limit)\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: GET allocation, confirm limit\n    else pool is short\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: PATCH groupQuotaLimits/{region} (increase request)\n        V--\u0026gt;\u0026gt;O: report \u0026#34;quota pending\u0026#34; with request ID\n    end\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;P: hand over\n    P-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: first deploy\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003cdetails class=\"mermaid-source\"\u003e\u003csummary\u003eDiagram source\u003c/summary\u003e\u003cpre\u003esequenceDiagram\n    participant O as Order\n    participant V as Vending engine\n    participant S as New subscription\n    participant G as Quota group\n    participant P as Workload pipeline\n    O-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;V: request (architype, region, quota needs)\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: create, place in management group\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: register Microsoft.Quota, Microsoft.Compute\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: PUT groupQuotas/{g}/subscriptions/{sub}\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: GET groupQuotaLimits/{region} (availableLimit)\n    alt pool has enough\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: PATCH quotaAllocations/{region} (absolute limit)\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: GET allocation, confirm limit\n    else pool is short\n        V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;G: PATCH groupQuotaLimits/{region} (increase request)\n        V--\u0026gt;\u0026gt;O: report \u0026#34;quota pending\u0026#34; with request ID\n    end\n    V-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;P: hand over\n    P-\u0026gt;\u0026gt;S: first deploy\u003c/pre\u003e\u003c/details\u003e\n\u003cfigcaption data-mermaid-auto-caption\u003eFigure 6\u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA few design decisions fall out of building this rather than drawing it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe order has to say what quota it needs.\u003c/strong\u003e The engine cannot guess. The cleanest place for that is the architype, the template a workload is built from, which already knows its VM families and sizes. The order then carries region, family and vCPU count, with the architype supplying defaults.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe engine allocates; it does not manage the pool.\u003c/strong\u003e Allocating from the group on behalf of a new subscription is a vending concern. Raising the group limit, deciding how much headroom to hold, and deallocating from retiring subscriptions are platform-ownership concerns. Mixing them gives an automated service the power to drain a pool that other teams depend on. In our design, the engine reads \u003ccode\u003eavailableLimit\u003c/code\u003e, allocates if it can, and otherwise reports the shortfall rather than escalating on its own.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u0026ldquo;Done, quota pending\u0026rdquo; is a real state.\u003c/strong\u003e Increase requests are asynchronous and can be rejected. The order should be able to complete with an explicit warning and the request ID, so nobody runs the first deployment into a known shortfall and nobody believes a subscription is ready when it is not.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe roles are a real expansion of trust.\u003c/strong\u003e The vending identity needs \u003cem\u003eQuota Request Operator\u003c/em\u003e on each subscription it creates, which is modest because it usually owns those subscriptions anyway. It also needs \u003cem\u003eGroupQuota Request Operator\u003c/em\u003e on the management group that holds the group, which is a standing grant at management-group scope in the customer\u0026rsquo;s tenant. That deserves the same scrutiny as any other privileged grant, and it is another argument for a dedicated management group.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOne group per tenant, configured per customer.\u003c/strong\u003e The group lives under a management group in one tenant. A vending engine that serves several customers from one deployment needs the group ID as customer configuration, not as a global setting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhether you can build any of it depends on three limits.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-three-limits-that-decide-whether-you-can-use-it\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The three limits that decide whether you can use it\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"billing-no-csp\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#billing-no-csp\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Billing: no CSP'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Billing: no CSP\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe documentation lists it as the first limitation: \u0026ldquo;Available only for Enterprise Agreement, Microsoft Customer Agreement (MCA), and Internal subscriptions.\u0026rdquo;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSubscriptions bought through a Cloud Solution Provider, the partner-led Azure Plan billed under a Microsoft Partner Agreement, are none of those. They cannot be added to a quota group. That is not a configuration gap you can engineer around; the API will not accept them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis matters more than it sounds, because a large share of managed estates are CSP. A managed service provider vending subscriptions for customers through its partner tenant is creating exactly the subscriptions Quota Groups exclude. Concierge supports all three agreement types, EA, MCA and MPA, but where a customer is billed through CSP, the vending engine has nothing to join the new subscription to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe useful nuance is that an estate can be mixed. If the subscriptions being retired are EA or MCA, a quota group can still pool quota \u003cem\u003ebetween them\u003c/em\u003e while they are wound down, and allocate it to other EA or MCA subscriptions. What it cannot do is carry that quota across the billing boundary into new CSP subscriptions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"scope-iaas-compute-only\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#scope-iaas-compute-only\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Scope: IaaS compute only'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Scope: IaaS compute only\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe second limitation is \u0026ldquo;Supports IaaS compute resources only.\u0026rdquo; The group APIs live under \u003ccode\u003eresourceProviders/Microsoft.Compute\u003c/code\u003e, and the unit is the VM family vCPU limit. That covers virtual machines and scale sets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt does not cover the quota that, in my experience, blocks new workloads most often today: Azure OpenAI tokens per minute, App Service and Functions plans, Container Apps environments, database vCores, public IP addresses. Each of those has its own quota and its own request process, usually per subscription. A platform built on PaaS and AI services can adopt quota groups and still find that most of its first-deploy failures are untouched by them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"access-not-a-quota-problem\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#access-not-a-quota-problem\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Access: not a quota problem'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Access: not a quota problem\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe third limitation causes the most confusion, because it fails in a way that looks like quota. Quota transfers and deployments \u0026ldquo;will fail unless regional and or zonal access is provided on the subscription.\u0026rdquo; A new subscription can be denied a reserved region, a zone, or a specific VM size, and no amount of quota in a group changes that. You can allocate 200 vCPUs of a family to a subscription and still have every deployment fail with \u003ccode\u003eSkuNotAvailable\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccess is fixed through the region access request process, which is a support request, not an API call. For reserved regions it is an \u0026ldquo;Other Requests\u0026rdquo; ticket listing the subscriptions, region and planned usage. An automated flow can detect the restriction up front by reading the SKU restrictions for the target region and sizes, and it should, because it is far cheaper to report \u0026ldquo;this subscription cannot use this size here\u0026rdquo; at vending time than to let the workload team discover it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"what-we-do-instead-when-the-subscriptions-are-csp\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  What we do instead when the subscriptions are CSP\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause Concierge vends CSP subscriptions for some customers, we recorded the decision in an architecture decision record rather than leaving it in a review thread. It comes down to the same three gates, handled without a pool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuota is part of the order.\u003c/strong\u003e After placement, the engine registers the providers it needs, reads current usage and limits through the \u003ccode\u003eMicrosoft.Quota\u003c/code\u003e API at subscription scope, and raises a \u003cstrong\u003eper-subscription\u003c/strong\u003e increase for any shortfall, for whatever resource type the architype declares, not only compute. The quota API addresses a subscription\u0026rsquo;s limits by scope, along the lines of \u003ccode\u003e/subscriptions/{id}/providers/Microsoft.Compute/locations/{region}/providers/Microsoft.Quota/quotas/{family}\u003c/code\u003e, and the same pattern covers other providers that publish their limits through it. Whether every provider accepts API increase requests on a CSP subscription, or some still need a ticket, is something we are verifying on a test subscription before we rely on it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAccess is checked, not assumed.\u003c/strong\u003e The engine reads SKU restrictions for the target region and sizes and reports any \u003ccode\u003eNotAvailableForSubscription\u003c/code\u003e before handover, with the region access request listed as an action rather than buried in a failed pipeline run.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThe outcome is recorded on the order.\u003c/strong\u003e Granted, pending with a request ID, or rejected. The order can finish as \u0026ldquo;done, quota pending\u0026rdquo;, and the ticket that tracks it says so.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eQuota groups stay as an option for EA and MCA customers.\u003c/strong\u003e Where the customer\u0026rsquo;s configuration names a group, the engine joins the subscription and allocates compute from it instead of raising a per-subscription compute request. Everything that is not compute still goes through the per-subscription path.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is less elegant than a single pool. It still turns a failed first deployment into a known state at vending time, which is the outcome that actually matters to the team receiving the subscription.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"where-this-leaves-you\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Where this leaves you\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eQuota Groups solve a real and old problem: quota you paid for in time and tickets no longer has to die with the subscription that held it. For EA and MCA estates, especially ones in the middle of consolidating or retiring subscriptions, the flow is worth building now. Join the retiring subscriptions, deallocate before you cancel, keep the group on a management group that will outlive your current hierarchy, and let vending allocate from the pool rather than raise tickets.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGo in with the boundaries clear, though. The group is inventory, not entitlement: the subscription is what gets checked, so allocation is a step, not a side effect. It covers VM families, not the PaaS and AI quota that increasingly gates new workloads. It does nothing for region or zone access. And if your subscriptions come through CSP, it is not available to you at all, so the design has to treat quota, capacity and access as explicit, per-subscription parts of every order.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat last point is the one I would carry into any vending design, pool or no pool. A subscription is not ready because it exists. It is ready when the first deployment of the workload it was built for can succeed, and quota and access are part of that definition.\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure DevOps Wiki to a Corporate PDF",
        "date_published" : "2026-10-05T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2026-10-05T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-devops-wiki-to-a-corporate-pdf/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-devops-wiki-to-a-corporate-pdf/",
        "summary": "The project documentation is in good shape. The team has been maintaining an Azure DevOps wiki, the architecture pages link to the detailed design, and the deployment instructions sit alongside the decisions that explain them.\nThen comes the handover request: “Can you send us the design document as a PDF? Please use the company template.”\nThat is a reasonable request. The recipient might not have access to Azure DevOps. An architecture board may need a fixed version to review, or the customer may need to file the document in a records system. A wiki is useful for the people doing the work; a controlled document is useful for the people accepting it.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eThe project documentation is in good shape. The team has been maintaining an Azure DevOps wiki, the architecture pages link to the detailed design, and the deployment instructions sit alongside the decisions that explain them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen comes the handover request: “Can you send us the design document as a PDF? Please use the company template.”\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat is a reasonable request. The recipient might not have access to Azure DevOps. An architecture board may need a fixed version to review, or the customer may need to file the document in a records system. A wiki is useful for the people doing the work; a controlled document is useful for the people accepting it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCopying the pages into Word gets the first document out of the door. It also creates another copy to maintain. At the next revision, someone has to work out what changed, paste it again, repair the formatting and check the page numbers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI wanted to keep the Markdown as the source and make the formatted document a build output. The implementation is available in \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003einnofactororg/markdown2pdf\u003c/a\u003e. It includes an Azure DevOps pipeline and a GitHub Action, both using Pandoc and a LaTeX template to produce a PDF artifact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis post walks through the Azure DevOps route, explains where the corporate formatting belongs, and shows how the underlying Pandoc commands fit together.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"give-the-wiki-a-publishing-process\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Give the wiki a publishing process\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConsider a design document spread across several wiki pages: an overview, requirements, architecture, security and an operational handover. The team wants to keep editing those pages normally. At agreed points, it needs to publish those sections as one document with a cover, version history, contents page and consistent branding.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are two separate decisions here: which content belongs in the document, and how that content should look. The workflow keeps them separate:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 10 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eMarkdown pages + explicit document order\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  |\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  v\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eMerge content and resolve supported asset paths\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  |\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  v\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eApply document metadata, history and replacements\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  |\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  v\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ePandoc + corporate LaTeX template -\u0026gt; PDF artifact\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe order file defines the publication. The template defines its presentation. Authors can change the design without adjusting headers and footers on every page, while template changes can be reviewed independently of technical content.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe output is a snapshot of the source used by that build. Generating it does not approve it: the organisation\u0026rsquo;s review, sign-off and records process still applies.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"start-with-the-git-repository-behind-the-wiki\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Start with the Git repository behind the wiki\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn Azure DevOps wiki is backed by Git, but the type of wiki matters when arranging the build.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003eproject wiki\u003c/strong\u003e has its own wiki repository. Use the wiki\u0026rsquo;s \u003cstrong\u003eClone wiki\u003c/strong\u003e option to obtain the repository URL, then clone it using your normal authenticated Git setup:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egit clone \u0026lt;wiki-clone-url\u0026gt; wiki-source\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReplace the placeholder; don\u0026rsquo;t put a personal access token into a command that will be saved in a script or build log.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003ecode wiki\u003c/strong\u003e publishes Markdown from a normal repository and branch. That is a convenient arrangement when you want documentation changes reviewed through pull requests and built by a pipeline in the same repository.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe supplied conversion pipeline checks out \u003ccode\u003eself\u003c/code\u003e. It does not automatically discover or export a separate project wiki. For a project wiki, add an authenticated checkout or staging step to bring its Markdown and attachments into the build workspace, or deliberately move to a code-wiki arrangement. Keep that acquisition step explicit so that a successful build cannot quietly publish an outdated copy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the rest of this example, assume the Markdown is available in the pipeline\u0026rsquo;s source repository under \u003ccode\u003edocs/design\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"choose-the-documents-reading-order\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Choose the document\u0026rsquo;s reading order\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA wiki\u0026rsquo;s navigation tree is not necessarily a good printed document. It may include working notes, obsolete pages or several audiences\u0026rsquo; material. Alphabetical file order is rarely what a design reviewer needs either.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe converter uses a \u003ccode\u003edocument.order\u003c/code\u003e file to select the pages and their sequence:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 10 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003edocs/\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  design/\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    document.order\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Overview.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Requirements.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Architecture.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Security.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Operations.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    images/\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      architecture.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor this document, \u003ccode\u003edocs/design/document.order\u003c/code\u003e contains:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 6 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# Customer design and handover\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eOverview.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eRequirements.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eArchitecture.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eSecurity.md\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eOperations.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach entry names a file relative to the document folder, including its extension. Lines beginning with \u003ccode\u003e#\u003c/code\u003e are comments. Nested paths can be listed explicitly when the content spans subfolders.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAzure DevOps also uses \u003ccode\u003e.order\u003c/code\u003e files for wiki navigation. Those are not interchangeable with \u003ccode\u003edocument.order\u003c/code\u003e: the converter expects an explicit list of Markdown paths, not a recursive walk of the wiki\u0026rsquo;s navigation files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy early experiments used PowerShell helpers named \u003ccode\u003eGet-DocfxFolderItems\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eGet-DocfxItem\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eInvoke-DocfxTocProcessing\u003c/code\u003e to inspect the wiki hierarchy and its \u003ccode\u003e.order\u003c/code\u003e files. That was useful for exploring the source structure. The implementation shared here uses the simpler publication manifest instead; you don\u0026rsquo;t need those helpers or DocFX to run it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis gives the author an editorial decision to review in Git. A new wiki page doesn\u0026rsquo;t become part of the customer deliverable merely because it exists.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"add-the-azure-devops-pipeline\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Add the Azure DevOps pipeline\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCopy the repository\u0026rsquo;s \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf/blob/main/.azuredevops/markdown2pdf.yml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure DevOps pipeline\u003c/a\u003e into the source repository, for example as:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e.pipelines/docs.design.yml\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse the full supplied pipeline, not just the variable block below. For this scenario, its variables would look like this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 14 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003evariables\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eFIRST_CHANGE_DESCRIPTION\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eInitial design draft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eFOLDER\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003edocs/design\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eGIT_LOG_LIMIT\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e15\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eHISTORY_FILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ehistory.txt\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eMAIN_AUTHOR\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eArchitecture Team\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eORDER_FILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003edocument.order\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eOUT_FILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003esolution-design.pdf\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ePROJECT\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eCUSTOMER-001\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eREPLACE_FILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ereplace.json\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSKIP_GIT_COMMIT_HISTORY\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eSUBTITLE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eSolution Design and Operational Handover\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eTITLE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eCustomer Platform\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eWORKFLOW_VERSION\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ev3\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe next sections define the optional \u003ccode\u003ehistory.txt\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003ereplace.json\u003c/code\u003e used here. Leave their variables empty if you don\u0026rsquo;t want those features.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eFOLDER\u003c/code\u003e tells the converter where the content lives. \u003ccode\u003eORDER_FILE\u003c/code\u003e selects the publication manifest. \u003ccode\u003eTITLE\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eSUBTITLE\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003ePROJECT\u003c/code\u003e provide document metadata, while \u003ccode\u003eOUT_FILE\u003c/code\u003e names the PDF published as a pipeline artifact.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eWORKFLOW_VERSION\u003c/code\u003e selects the converter scripts and template assets fetched from GitHub. The repository\u0026rsquo;s example uses \u003ccode\u003ev3\u003c/code\u003e. For a controlled publishing process, choose and review a specific version; use an immutable commit reference where your standards require it. A template change can alter the deliverable even when none of its Markdown changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe supplied pipeline performs these jobs:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChecks out the source with \u003ccode\u003efetchDepth: 0\u003c/code\u003e, making Git history available for the document history feature.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCaches TeX Live and installs the conversion dependencies.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFetches the converter, LaTeX template and branding images from the selected implementation version.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRuns the conversion with the configured inputs.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePublishes the resulting PDF with \u003ccode\u003ePublishPipelineArtifact@1\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreate a pipeline in Azure DevOps using \u003cstrong\u003eExisting Azure Pipelines YAML file\u003c/strong\u003e, select the copied file, and run it manually for the first test. The agent needs access both to the source content and to the external locations used to download the tools and template.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor Azure Repos Git, configure \u003cstrong\u003ebuild validation in the branch policies\u003c/strong\u003e if you want the PDF generated during pull-request review. Don\u0026rsquo;t rely on the sample YAML\u0026rsquo;s \u003ccode\u003epr:\u003c/code\u003e block to configure Azure Repos PR validation; the branch policy is the relevant control there. Configure a normal CI trigger separately if you also want builds after merges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe finished PDF is a downloadable artifact on the run. Publishing it to SharePoint, a customer portal or a records system is a separate delivery step, with its own access and approval requirements.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"make-the-template-match-the-document-standard\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Make the template match the document standard\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe implementation has three main presentation assets:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf/blob/main/tools/designdoc.tex\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003etools/designdoc.tex\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e: the LaTeX document template.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003etools/designdoc-cover.png\u003c/code\u003e: the cover image.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003etools/designdoc-logo.png\u003c/code\u003e: the page-header logo.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe template provides a title page, version history, table of contents and styled content pages. Headers carry the logo and document context; footers provide page numbering. The converter supplies metadata such as title, project, authors and date.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat is the place to implement the approved fonts, colours, margins and page furniture. Keep those choices out of individual Markdown pages so authors aren\u0026rsquo;t maintaining formatting instructions alongside the design.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe supplied assets are Innofactor-specific. To publish under another organisation\u0026rsquo;s standard, maintain a reviewed customisation or fork, and update the pipeline\u0026rsquo;s download locations to use it. Copying a different template into the documentation folder is not enough if the pipeline still fetches the upstream assets on every run.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlso inspect \u003ccode\u003etools/convert.sh\u003c/code\u003e. Some presentation and policy values are supplied there rather than in the \u003ccode\u003e.tex\u003c/code\u003e file, including an Innofactor-specific confidentiality statement. Changing the logo alone does not make the document appropriate for another company or for public distribution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA template can reproduce a corporate layout, but that does not automatically make a document compliant. If the standard requires a document identifier, classification, approver table or specific revision fields, add and review those explicitly. Check the generated PDF against an approved sample before treating the template as ready for formal use.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"decide-what-version-history-means\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Decide what “version history” means\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe converter supports three sources for the history page, in priority order:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAn explicit history file, when supplied and found.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe fallback author and initial change description when Git history is deliberately skipped.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGit commit history for the documentation folder, falling back to the initial entry when no history is available.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGit history is useful during drafting, but commit messages are not always suitable for a customer-facing revision table. “Fix typo” and “move diagram again” record the work without describing a formal issue of the document.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a controlled deliverable, I would use \u003ccode\u003edocs/design/history.txt\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e1.0|Oct 26, 2023|Architecture Team|Initial design issued for review\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e1.1|Oct 28, 2023|Architecture Team|Updated network design following review\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe format is \u003ccode\u003eVersion|Date|Author|Description\u003c/code\u003e, one entry per line, without a header row. These are illustrative entries, not dates generated by the pipeline.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSet \u003ccode\u003eHISTORY_FILE: history.txt\u003c/code\u003e to use it. If you prefer Git-derived history during development, leave that setting empty, keep \u003ccode\u003eSKIP_GIT_COMMIT_HISTORY: false\u003c/code\u003e, and use \u003ccode\u003eGIT_LOG_LIMIT\u003c/code\u003e to bound the number of entries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNeither option proves that a revision was approved. Record approval through the process your organisation actually uses, and retain the issued PDF with its source revision and build reference.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"reuse-content-without-maintaining-customer-specific-copies\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Reuse content without maintaining customer-specific copies\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA common documentation problem is a largely reusable design with a few customer-specific names. The converter\u0026rsquo;s replacement file lets the publishing step substitute those values.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor example, a Markdown paragraph might contain:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003emarkdown\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eThe primary services for {organization name} run in {data center name}.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith \u003ccode\u003edocs/design/replace.json\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;{organization name}\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Contoso\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;{data center name}\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;WE1\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSet \u003ccode\u003eREPLACE_FILE: replace.json\u003c/code\u003e to apply the replacements to the merged content before conversion. Keep that configuration with the publication so reviewers can see which values were used.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is simple text substitution, not a full document templating language. The implementation uses shell and \u003ccode\u003esed\u003c/code\u003e processing, so test values containing slashes, ampersands or other special characters before relying on them. Don\u0026rsquo;t use the file as a secret store; the substituted text is going into a distributed document.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"write-markdown-that-survives-the-move-to-paper\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Write Markdown that survives the move to paper\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA browser can scroll horizontally. A portrait A4 page cannot. A few authoring habits make the generated PDF much more useful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eKeep tables narrow, give diagrams readable labels, and split large comparison matrices into smaller sections. Use proper Markdown headings rather than formatting ordinary paragraphs to resemble headings. Let the generated contents page describe the document instead of carrying a wiki-specific contents widget into print.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse explicit relative image paths where possible:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003emarkdown\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e![\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ePlatform architecture\u003c/span\u003e](\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e./images/architecture.png\u003c/span\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe converter rewrites supported relative paths as it merges pages, and the repository specifically recommends paths starting with \u003ccode\u003e./\u003c/code\u003e. It is not a complete Azure DevOps wiki-rendering engine. Check attachments, page links, anchors and any wiki-specific syntax against the output. Turning a path into an absolute build-agent path does not make it a useful link for the recipient of a PDF.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe implementation also supports fenced admonitions through its Pandoc filter:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003emarkdown\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e::: warning\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eConfirm the recovery procedure before scheduling the production cutover.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e:::\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe supported classes are \u003ccode\u003ewarning\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eimportant\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003enote\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003ecaution\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003etip\u003c/code\u003e. Check how these appear in both your wiki and PDF; support in the converter does not guarantee identical rendering in every Markdown viewer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe supplied template is designed for portrait A4 and does not offer a per-page landscape switch. Wide tables and diagrams need an editorial decision, not just a smaller font. Section numbering is not enabled automatically by the supplied conversion command either; agree a consistent approach before numbering headings manually.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"where-the-original-pandoc-commands-fit\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Where the original Pandoc commands fit\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe pipeline wraps tools that can also be used directly. These commands are useful for understanding the conversion or testing a formatting change without first wiring up a complete publishing process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"combine-pages-in-an-explicit-order\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#combine-pages-in-an-explicit-order\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Combine pages in an explicit order'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Combine pages in an explicit order\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003ePandoc can read an ordered list of inputs from a defaults file. For example, save this as \u003ccode\u003edefaults.yaml\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003einput-files\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eOverview.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eRequirements.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eArchitecture.md\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003everbosity\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eINFO\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen run Pandoc from the folder containing those files:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --defaults defaults.yaml -o output.docx\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis illustrates the same principle as \u003ccode\u003edocument.order\u003c/code\u003e, but the formats are different. \u003ccode\u003edefaults.yaml\u003c/code\u003e is Pandoc configuration; \u003ccode\u003edocument.order\u003c/code\u003e is input to the repository\u0026rsquo;s merge script. They are not two files you must maintain for the supplied pipeline.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDefaults files can also hold resource paths and other conversion settings. Pandoc supports \u003ccode\u003e${.}\u003c/code\u003e in path-valued fields to refer to the defaults file\u0026rsquo;s directory, which helps when keeping configuration and supporting assets together. See the \u003ca href=\"https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#defaults-files\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ePandoc defaults documentation\u003c/a\u003e for the available fields.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"use-a-word-reference-document-when-word-is-the-deliverable\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#use-a-word-reference-document-when-word-is-the-deliverable\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Use a Word reference document when Word is the deliverable'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Use a Word reference document when Word is the deliverable\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes the official handover format is DOCX, or the recipient needs to make tracked edits. Pandoc\u0026rsquo;s Word route uses a reference document:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --defaults defaults.yaml --reference-doc\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ereference.docx -o output.docx\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSave the approved template as a \u003ccode\u003e.docx\u003c/code\u003e, rather than passing a \u003ccode\u003e.dotx\u003c/code\u003e directly. Put \u003ccode\u003ereference.docx\u003c/code\u003e in the working folder or pass its explicit path.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePandoc uses the reference document\u0026rsquo;s styles and document properties; it does not fill an arbitrary existing Word document as though it were a mail-merge template. Check the result against the corporate standard, especially when it contains custom cover content or mandatory tables.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a separate output route. The \u003ccode\u003emarkdown2pdf\u003c/code\u003e implementation described above renders through LaTeX and XeLaTeX; it does not take a corporate Word template and automatically turn that into its PDF layout.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"apply-latex-settings-to-the-pdf-route\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#apply-latex-settings-to-the-pdf-route\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Apply LaTeX settings to the PDF route'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Apply LaTeX settings to the PDF route\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor local PDF experiments, a header include such as \u003ccode\u003ehead.tex\u003c/code\u003e can hold page and link settings:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etex\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 9 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e\\usepackage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003efancyvrb,newverbs\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e\\usepackage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e[top=2cm, bottom=1.5cm, left=2cm, right=2cm]\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003egeometry\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e\\hypersetup\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    bookmarksopen=true,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    colorlinks=true,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    linkcolor=blue,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    filecolor=magenta,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    urlcolor=blue\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApply it when generating a PDF:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-15\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-15\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --defaults defaults.yaml --pdf-engine\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003exelatex -H head.tex -o output.pdf\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis requires Pandoc and a suitable TeX installation. A LaTeX header does not style DOCX output; use the reference document for that. In the automated implementation, make the equivalent changes in the reviewed template and metadata rather than maintaining a competing set of local overrides.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"inspect-code-highlighting-and-link-colours\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#inspect-code-highlighting-and-link-colours\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Inspect code highlighting and link colours'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Inspect code highlighting and link colours\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003ePandoc can list its syntax-highlighting styles and recognised languages:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-16\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-16\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --list-highlight-styles\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --list-highlight-languages\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a standalone experiment using its built-in highlighting:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-17\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-17\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --pdf-engine\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003exelatex --highlight-style zenburn test.md -o test.pdf\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOr combine the defaults file with numbered sections and a different highlight style:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-18\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-18\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --defaults defaults.yaml --pdf-engine\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003exelatex -H head.tex \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  -N --highlight-style\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eespresso -V colorlinks -o output.pdf\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLanguage labels on fenced code blocks help Pandoc choose the right syntax rules. The shared converter uses \u003ccode\u003e--listings\u003c/code\u003e, so its code presentation is controlled through the LaTeX listings configuration; changing a \u003ccode\u003e--highlight-style\u003c/code\u003e example is not the same as changing that pipeline\u0026rsquo;s code styling.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLink colours can be tested independently too:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-19\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6f6a61dd55e0251acdd0cdce4da6c66d-19\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epandoc --pdf-engine\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003exelatex -V colorlinks -V \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eurlcolor\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eblue \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  -V \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003etoccolor\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ered test.md -o test.pdf\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe text must be recognised as a link. Use Markdown links or an explicit autolink such as \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;https://example.com\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e rather than assuming that every URL-looking string will become one.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese commands explain the building blocks. For repeated delivery, the versioned pipeline should remain the publishing route, so the document doesn\u0026rsquo;t depend on whichever combination of flags someone last used locally.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"review-the-artifact-before-issuing-it\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Review the artifact before issuing it\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the first run, choose a small but representative document: several pages, an image, a table and a code block. Inspect the PDF rather than treating a green pipeline result as evidence of document quality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck that the pages appear in the intended order, images resolve, table columns fit and code is legible. Confirm that the cover, history, confidentiality text and branding are appropriate for the recipient. Test links from the downloaded PDF, outside the build agent and ideally without access to the source wiki.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter that first review, the publishing loop becomes manageable: edit the Markdown, review the change, build the PDF and retain the version that was actually issued. If you want artifacts on every relevant change, include order files, history files, replacement files and pipeline configuration in your trigger or branch-policy path filters, not just \u003ccode\u003e.md\u003c/code\u003e files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"use-the-implementation\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Use the implementation\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe complete project is available at \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003einnofactororg/markdown2pdf\u003c/a\u003e, with \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf/tree/main/.azuredevops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure DevOps setup instructions\u003c/a\u003e and a \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf#usage\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eGitHub Action example\u003c/a\u003e for documentation hosted on GitHub. The code and documentation are released under the BSD 3-Clause License; retain the relevant notices when adapting them.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe useful starting point is one document, one explicit order file and one reviewed template. Keep the wiki as the place the team works, and publish a PDF from the reviewed source when someone needs a formal copy. The next revision can then follow the same process without rebuilding the document by hand in Word.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"references\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#references\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'References'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    References\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003emarkdown2pdf source and usage\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf/blob/main/.azuredevops/markdown2pdf.yml\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAzure DevOps pipeline implementation\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/innofactororg/markdown2pdf/blob/main/tools/convert.sh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eConversion script\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ePandoc user guide\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://jdhao.github.io/2019/05/30/markdown2pdf_pandoc/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eConverting Markdown to Beautiful PDF with Pandoc — jdhao\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Running Tailscale on a Ubiquiti EdgeRouter X",
        "date_published" : "2024-12-14T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2024-12-14T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/running-tailscale-on-a-ubiquiti-edgerouter-x/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/running-tailscale-on-a-ubiquiti-edgerouter-x/",
        "summary": " Running Tailscale on a Ubiquiti EdgeRouter Having grown up in the world of \u0026lsquo;on premise\u0026rsquo; computing, I have always prioritized data privacy in my home network.\nThough there may not be much of interest to hackers, there is still personal data and services that I want to keep secure. I have spent years working with OpenVPN and IPSec, building and supporting a Dynamic Multi-site VPN Mesh with Cisco DMVPN, and I know first hand the challenges of connecting clients to a private network and managing keys.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"running-tailscale-on-a-ubiquiti-edgerouter\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#running-tailscale-on-a-ubiquiti-edgerouter\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Running Tailscale on a Ubiquiti EdgeRouter'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"running-tailscale-on-a-ubiquiti-edgerouter\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Running Tailscale on a Ubiquiti EdgeRouter\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHaving grown up in the world of \u0026lsquo;on premise\u0026rsquo; computing, I have always prioritized data privacy in my home network.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThough there may not be much of interest to hackers, there is still personal data and services that I want to keep secure. I have spent years working with OpenVPN and IPSec, building and supporting a Dynamic Multi-site VPN Mesh with Cisco DMVPN, and I know first hand the challenges of connecting clients to a private network and managing keys.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen WireGuard emerged a few years ago, I quickly switched to an Edge Router X to make it my default VPN technology. Though WireGuard had some scaling challenges to manage, it was still significantly easier to use than what I was used to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen Tailscale came along, which made WireGuard even more user-friendly with additional security features like key rotation and single sign-on. While I’ve been using Tailscale on all of my systems, including Linux, macOS, and iOS, I recently decided to shift the endpoint to the edge of my network to make connectivity even easier.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eMy EdgeRouter passed away, it served me well, and has been replaced by a UniFi Cloud Gateway Max, And is quite happy to assume the \u003ccode\u003etailscale\u003c/code\u003e responsibility\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eLatest builds now support the \u003ccode\u003etailscale update\u003c/code\u003e command, which makes the maintenance trivial.\nRemoved defunct configuration details from the post\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eUpdating notes to reflect switch from Unstable which I have been using since verision 1.7, to the current stable branch running 1.38.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eUpdating notes to reflect switch from stable 1.40 to 1.50.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"ubuquiti-edge-router-x\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Ubuquiti Edge Router X\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe router at the edge of my home network is currently a Ubiquiti EdgeRouter X, which boasts a power-efficient MIPSLE CPU and runs on a Linux-based operating system that was derived from VyattaOS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe device offers a wide range of settings that can be adjusted via SSH that are not available through the web UI. With Tailscale, which provides MIPS binaries in addition to ARM, I can now connect the router to Tailscale and treat it like any other Linux system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn this post, we\u0026rsquo;ll explore how to configure the EdgeRouter to function as a gateway, allowing external systems to access internal networks.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"installation-and-upgrade\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Installation and Upgrade\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Tailscale client comes in two branches, Tailscale Unstable and Tailscale Stable. While Unstable was necessary for me a few years ago, I now prefer using Stable. To download the latest version for the MIPS platform, visit the \u003ca href=\"https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/?ref=www.damianflynn.com#static\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eTailscale Stable\u003c/a\u003e page and scroll down to find the current build, such as \u003cem\u003etailscale_1.54.0_mips.tgz\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo install and set up Tailscale, follow these steps:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNavigate to your home folder and download the current build. Then, extract it and delete the download file:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ~\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecurl https://pkgs.tailscale.com/stable/tailscale_1.54.0_mipsle.tgz -o tailscale.tgz  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etar xzvf tailscale.tgz  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erm tailscale.tgz\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMove the extracted files to their proper locations on the router and create the necessary directories for log data and runtime socket file:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 18 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Change into a real shell and switch to root user \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo bash \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Navigate to the extracted download \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e tailscale_1.50.0_mipsle \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Move the application to the right location \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emv tailscale* /usr/sbin \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Place systemd and defaults into etc \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emv systemd/tailscaled.service /etc/systemd/system \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emv systemd/tailscaled.defaults /etc/default/tailscaled \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Create the state storage folders \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir /var/lib/tailscale /run/tailscale\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Create a symbolic link from /usr/bin which is in the path\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ln -s /usr/sbin/tailscale /usr/bin/tailscale\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"initial-confuration\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#initial-confuration\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Initial Confuration'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Initial Confuration\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe following steps are not typically required if you are upgrading between versions; however if this is a fresh installation you will need to start the service, and authenticate your node with the tailnet.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart it up! If you have any issues, they should appear here as the service gets started. Check the logs by tailing the output from Tailscale using  \u003ccode\u003etail -f /var/log/messages\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esystemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e --now tailscaled\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003col start=\"2\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuthenticate your device to Tailscale by starting it up and following the instructions. You can also use some options, such as:\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--advertise-routes\u003c/code\u003e: a comma-separated list of subnets that other clients can reach via this router\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e--advertise-exit-node\u003c/code\u003e: allows any Tailscale instance to act as an exit node, sending your otherwise-public traffic to a specific node that will NAT your traffic out to the internet. This option is useful when you\u0026rsquo;re on an untrusted network or if you want to source your traffic from a different network.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etailscale up --advertise-routes\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e172.16.1.0/24 --advertise-exit-node --accept-routes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 24 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1208d006daae3bc60db4bdfd96cca8e4-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eWhen you start Tailscale, it will present you with a URL to visit that allows you to authenticate the device to your Tailscale account. \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e- ![](./sw.tailscale.configuration.authenticate.png)\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e- Once you do this, your router will show up under the “Machines” list in the admin UI\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e- ![](./sw.tailscale.configuration.tailscale-settings.png)\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026gt; [!Warning] Disconnect\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026gt; At this point all traffic on the router will appear to black hole for both ingress and egress. \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026gt; To restore service, we must acknowledge the settings in the Tailscale portal; this may required that you use an alternate device that is not on this network to reach the port. Once in the portal we should validate and enable both settings we applied in the `tailscale up` command, which will then unblock the device\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026gt; ![](./sw.tailscale.configuration.device-configuration.png)\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e## Final Testing\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eIf you’ve made it this far, you should be able to ping other Tailscale nodes bidirectionally.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eIf you’d like hosts behind the EdgeRouter to communicate to other Tailscale clients outside the local network, you’ll want to add a NAT so that traffic knows where to go (without one, you’ll only have inbound access to devices on the network). To do this, you can add it via CLI:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e```shell\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erouter$ configure\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erouter# set service nat rule 5012 description Tailscale\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erouter# set service nat rule 5012 outbound-interface tailscale0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erouter# set service nat rule 5012 protocol all\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erouter# set service nat rule 5012 type masquerade\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e…or find it in the Ubiquiti web UI under “Firewall/NAT” and click a few options. The \u003ccode\u003etailscale0\u003c/code\u003e interface will not show up in the dropdown list, so you must choose “Other” and type in \u003ccode\u003etailscale0\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    }
    {
        "title" : "Terraform or Bicep for Azure: Strengths Compared",
        "date_published" : "2023-02-15T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2023-02-15T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/terraform-or-bicep-for-azure-strengths-compared/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/terraform-or-bicep-for-azure-strengths-compared/",
        "summary": " Considering Terraform and Bicep As more organizations adopt cloud infrastructure, the demand for infrastructure as code (IAC) solutions has grown. Infrastructure as code allows developers to manage and automate infrastructure deployments using code, making it easier to track changes and maintain consistency.\nTerraform and Bicep are two popular IAC solutions that enable developers to manage and automate infrastructure deployments using code.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"considering-terraform-and-bicep\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#considering-terraform-and-bicep\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Considering Terraform and Bicep'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"considering-terraform-and-bicep\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Considering Terraform and Bicep\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs more organizations adopt cloud infrastructure, the demand for infrastructure as code (IAC) solutions has grown. Infrastructure as code allows developers to manage and automate infrastructure deployments using code, making it easier to track changes and maintain consistency.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTerraform and Bicep are two popular IAC solutions that enable developers to manage and automate infrastructure deployments using code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile both tools share some similarities, Terraform is more widely adopted solution with many benefits,  In this post, we will highligh some of the benfits each expose, so you can start to figure out where you next learning should be focused\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"bicep-and-arm\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Bicep and ARM\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAzure Resource Manager (ARM) templates are a popular way to define and deploy infrastructure as code in Azure. However, writing ARM templates can be challenging, particularly for beginners. Bicep is a new language developed by Microsoft that makes writing Azure infrastructure code easier and more streamlined. In this blog post, we will explore the benefits of using Bicep over ARM.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSimpler Syntax\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep\u0026rsquo;s syntax is simpler and easier to read and write than ARM\u0026rsquo;s. The code is written in JSON-like format and requires less boilerplate code. Additionally, Bicep has a smaller learning curve than ARM, making it easier for beginners to get started.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBetter Modularity\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep\u0026rsquo;s modular design allows developers to define reusable components and deploy them across multiple environments. This can help reduce code duplication and improve code maintainability. The modules in Bicep are simpler to define and use than the modules in ARM, which can make code reuse more accessible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eImproved Type Safety\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep provides type safety to help developers catch errors before deployment. The language\u0026rsquo;s strong typing system ensures that variables are defined correctly and that the correct data types are used. This can help prevent errors in deployments and improve the overall quality of the code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBetter Tooling\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep has better tooling support than ARM. It is integrated with Visual Studio Code, which provides auto-completion and syntax highlighting for the language. Additionally, Bicep is integrated with Azure CLI, which makes it easier to manage and automate infrastructure deployments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEasier to Read and Maintain\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep\u0026rsquo;s simpler syntax and modular design make it easier to read and maintain compared to ARM. The code is less verbose and easier to understand, which can help reduce errors and improve code quality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGreater Consistency\u003c/strong\u003e: Bicep promotes consistency in infrastructure deployments. Developers can use templates across different environments, which can ensure that infrastructure is deployed consistently across all environments. This can help reduce errors and improve the overall quality of the infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOf course, we can also ask the question, of what are the Benfits of ARM over Bicep. Azure Resource Manager (ARM) templates have been around for a while and are a widely adopted way to define and deploy infrastructure as code in Azure. While Bicep has many benefits, there are still some advantages to using ARM templates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWidely Adopted\u003c/strong\u003e: ARM templates have been around for a while and are a widely adopted way to deploy infrastructure in Azure. Many organizations have already invested time and resources in building ARM templates, and they may find it easier to continue using them rather than switching to a new language.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBetter Compatibility\u003c/strong\u003e: ARM templates are compatible with more Azure services than Bicep. While Bicep is designed to work with Azure, ARM templates can be used with many other services and platforms, for example Azure Policy still requires ARM syntax.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eEasier to Write for Experienced Developers\u003c/strong\u003e: Experienced developers \u003cem\u003emay\u003c/em\u003e find it easier to write ARM templates than Bicep code. While Bicep is simpler and easier to learn for beginners, experienced developers may prefer the greater flexibility and complexity offered by ARM template\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn conclusion, Bicep offers several benefits over ARM. Its simpler syntax, better modularity, improved type safety, better tooling, and easier-to-read code make it an attractive option for developers who are focused on Azure infrastructure. Additionally, its focus on consistency can help improve the overall quality of infrastructure deployments. While ARM templates remain a popular way to deploy Azure infrastructure, Bicep provides a more accessible and streamlined approach that can make infrastructure as code more accessible to developers of all skill levels.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"considerating-terraform\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Considerating Terraform\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth Terraform  and bicep use a declarative language, which means that it focuses on the desired end-state rather than the specific steps needed to achieve it. This makes it easier to manage and automate infrastructure changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth options are very popular, and very powerful. At one point in time, Terraform was a poor option for working with Azure, and Bicep did not even exist (its just 2 years young).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSelecting the Declarative Language and tooling is not black and white; so consider your requirements, and lets take a little time to conside their respective strengths.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"bicep-strengths\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#bicep-strengths\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Bicep Strengths'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Bicep Strengths\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimpler Syntax: Bicep has a simpler syntax than Terraform, making it easier for beginners to get started. The syntax is also more concise and readable, which can make code maintenance easier. The code is written in JSON-like format and requires less boilerplate code compared to Terraform\u0026rsquo;s HashiCorp Configuration Language (HCL).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIntegrated Language: Bicep is built on top of the Azure Resource Manager (ARM) language and is fully integrated with Azure. This means that developers can use Bicep to write ARM templates that can be used with any Azure resource type. Additionally, Bicep has direct access to all Azure resources, including new features and services.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eType Safety: Bicep provides type safety to help developers catch errors before deployment. The language\u0026rsquo;s strong typing system ensures that variables are defined correctly and that the correct data types are used. This can help prevent errors in deployments and improve the overall quality of the code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImproved Modularity: Bicep\u0026rsquo;s modular design allows developers to define reusable components and deploy them across multiple environments. This can help reduce code duplication and improve code maintainability. The modules in Bicep are simpler to define and use than the modules in Terraform, which can make code reuse more accessible.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccessability: Bicep is included in the Azure Quickstart templates, which can make it easier to deploy infrastructure with a single click.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"terraform-strengths\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#terraform-strengths\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Terraform Strengths'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Terraform Strengths\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMulti-cloud support: Terraform supports more cloud providers compared to Bicep. Terraform can be used to manage infrastructure across multiple cloud providers, including AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, and many others, while Bicep is currently only available for Azure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreater ecosystem and community: Terraform has a larger and more active community compared to Bicep, making it easier to find resources, get help, and share knowledge.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eModular design: Terraform\u0026rsquo;s modular design allows for code reusability and easier management of large infrastructure deployments, while Bicep\u0026rsquo;s module system is less robust and can be more challenging to maintain.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBuilt-in state management: Terraform has built-in state management, which allows it to keep track of the current state of the infrastructure and make changes accordingly. Bicep relies on external state management - essentially the Azure Resource Manager.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRicher documentation: Terraform has extensive documentation that covers every aspect of the tool, including configuration options, provider support, and best practices. Bicep\u0026rsquo;s documentation is still developing and can be less comprehensive.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore provider support: Terraform has a broader range of provider support compared to Bicep. This means that it can integrate with more services and resources from various cloud providers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWider range of configuration options: Terraform provides more configuration options for its users, including custom providers, modules, and backend configurations, while Bicep\u0026rsquo;s configuration options are more limited.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMore testing options: Terraform has more testing options compared to Bicep, such as testing infrastructure deployments with Terraform\u0026rsquo;s built-in testing framework, Terratest.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGreater maturity: Terraform has been around longer and has a more mature feature set, while Bicep is a relatively new tool and still in active development. Terraform has been battle-tested over the years and has a robust set of features.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"summary\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Summary\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile Terraform is a popular IAC solution with many benefits, Bicep has some unique advantages that can make it the right choice for certain projects. Its simpler syntax, integrated language, type safety, improved modularity, and integration with other Azure tools make it an attractive option for developers who are focused on Azure-specific infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTerraform has several advantages over Bicep in terms of multi-cloud support, community, modular design, declarative language, state management, documentation, provider support, configuration options, testing options, and maturity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChoosing the right IAC tool for your organization is critical, and evaluating the features of each tool can help you make an informed decision. Ultimately, the choice between Terraform and Bicep will depend on the specific needs of your organization and the nature of your projects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Theming Hugo with a Hugo Module",
        "date_published" : "2022-11-21T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2022-11-21T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/theming-hugo-with-a-hugo-module/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/theming-hugo-with-a-hugo-module/",
        "summary": " Theming Hugo with Module To utilize modules in Hugo for our theme, we first must ensure that our site supports Hugo Modules.\nYou can quickly verify that you site is configured for Hugo Modules, as it should contain a go.mod file in the repository root.\nImport the theme module The concept of a Hugo theme has been superseded with the concept of modules, with the main difference that the former will allow you to build your site entirely, while the latter might implement only some modular features like enabling the ATOM feed, or adding a search to your website.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"theming-hugo-with-module\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#theming-hugo-with-module\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Theming Hugo with Module'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"theming-hugo-with-module\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Theming Hugo with Module\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo utilize modules in Hugo for our theme, we first must ensure that our site supports Hugo Modules.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eYou can quickly verify that you site is configured for Hugo Modules, as it should contain a  \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e file in the repository root.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"import-the-theme-module\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Import the \u003ccode\u003etheme\u003c/code\u003e module\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe concept of a Hugo \u003cem\u003etheme\u003c/em\u003e has been superseded with the concept of \u003cem\u003emodules\u003c/em\u003e, with the main difference that the former will allow you to build your site entirely, while the latter might implement only some modular features like enabling the ATOM feed, or adding a search to your website.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eImporting a module as a theme will typically follow the convention:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate the sites \u003ccode\u003econfig.toml\u003c/code\u003e file with the below content, so that it imports the \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/DamianFlynn/hugo-bilberry-theme\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehugo-bilberry-theme\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e \u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etoml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003emodule\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003emodule\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eimports\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003epath\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;github.com/Lednerb/bilberry-hugo-theme/v3\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn this case, the path \u003ccode\u003egithub.com/Lednerb/bilberry-hugo-theme/v3\u003c/code\u003e references the Github repo hosting the theme to be used.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eIt’s possible to take any Hugo theme git repo and import that as a Hugo Module even if that repo isn’t actually one i.e. doesn’t have a \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e. But it’s recommended that the theme be a proper Hugo Module so that you have better dependency tracking between your site and the theme.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"testing\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#testing\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Testing'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Testing\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eCreate \u003ccode\u003econtent/testing.md\u003c/code\u003e. This step is optional and is only so that your test site as some content.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003emd\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e---\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etitle = \u0026#34;Hello\u0026#34;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etype = Article\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e---\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"gh\"\u003e# Hey!\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eWe have a sample article posted\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat’s it! Now run the Hugo server with the command \u003ccode\u003ehugo server\u003c/code\u003e and look at your site running on localhost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust to summerise\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDid you need to manually clone any theme? \u003cstrong\u003eNo\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWould you need to deal with the \u003ccode\u003e.gitmodules\u003c/code\u003e file? \u003cstrong\u003eNo\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"tidy-up-the-modules\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Tidy up the modules\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, run \u003ca href=\"https://gohugo.io/commands/hugo_mod_tidy/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003e\u003ccode\u003ehugo mod tidy\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/a\u003e to clean up the \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e and update or generate the \u003ccode\u003ego.sum\u003c/code\u003e file. These files will track the module dependencies for your site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e contains the direct module dependencies for your site.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003ego.sum\u003c/code\u003e contains the versions and hashes of all the direct \u003cstrong\u003eand indirect\u003c/strong\u003e dependencies\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust as you added a theme as a Hugo Module to your site, it’s possible that that theme is depending on other Hugo Modules for your site.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eYou should ensure that both the \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003ego.sum\u003c/code\u003e are not excluded from your respoitory, for example due to a \u003ccode\u003e.gitignore\u003c/code\u003e inclusion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eCurrently you \u003ccode\u003ego.mod\u003c/code\u003e will be similar to the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ego\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003emodule\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003egithub\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eDamianFlynn\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ehugo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ego\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e1.19\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003erequire\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003egithub\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003eLednerb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ebilberry\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ehugo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003etheme\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ev3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nx\"\u003ev3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e.14.0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e// indirect\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ewhile, you now also should have a new \u003ccode\u003ego.sum\u003c/code\u003e which again should be similar to this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egithub.com/Lednerb/bilberry-hugo-theme/v3 v3.14.0 h1:4kahS1hSN/txeL2J9MzsEqidz52N0Fltf2iwE2Jmbn0=\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egithub.com/Lednerb/bilberry-hugo-theme/v3 v3.14.0/go.mod h1:ERTLq/0yIBb0jN0Dh+w5G4wCp9TrB0JY86+Zh+26Dkg=\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"updating-the-theme\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Updating the theme \n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIssing the command will instruct our Hugo module to update all the modules it depends on recursivly.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehugo mod get -u ./..\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you wish to target a specif module only, for example our theme, then we would issue the following command\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehugo mod get -u github.com/DamianFlynn/hugo\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd, if you wish to reference a specific tag or commit in git with the following format\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehugo mod get \u0026lt;module path\u0026gt;@\u0026lt;git ref\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eIf you have a theme added as a Hugo Module, which depends on other Hugo Modules, it’s often helpful to know the dependency graph. You can do that by running:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e hugo mod graph\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhich in our current configuration, appears as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-32e76d43b00ffb5403efc72305745ee5-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egithub.com/DamianFlynn/hugo github.com/Lednerb/bilberry-hugo-theme/v3@v3.14.0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Network Change Detection with Oxidized and Git",
        "date_published" : "2022-11-17T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2022-11-17T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/network-change-detection-with-oxidized-and-git/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/network-change-detection-with-oxidized-and-git/",
        "summary": "The process is very simple:\nLogin to each device in the router list router.db, Run Commands to get the information that will be saved Clean the output Commit the Changes to GIT Repository The tool is coded in Ruby, and implements a Domain Specific Language (DSL) for interaction.\nFinally, there is a Web based User experience included in the solution so we can get a fast overview of the world.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eThe process is very simple:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLogin to each device in the router list \u003ccode\u003erouter.db\u003c/code\u003e,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRun Commands to get the information that will be saved\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClean the output\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommit the Changes to GIT Repository\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe tool is coded in \u003cem\u003eRuby\u003c/em\u003e, and implements a Domain Specific Language (DSL) for interaction.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, there is a Web based User experience included in the solution so we can get a fast overview of the world.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"docker-container\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Docker Container\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll of the configuration for my container is hosted at the file system location \u003ccode\u003e/opt/appdata/oxidized\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI will also select to execute the Web Interface for Oxidized using its default port with is \u003ccode\u003etcp:8888\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the follow command, we will grab the latest container version from Docker Hub, and call the container \u003cem\u003eoxidized\u003c/em\u003e locally. Additionally, if the container should stop, I am providing the flag to instruct docker to always restart the service again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo docker run --restart always -v /opt/appdata/oxidized:/root/.config/oxidized -p 8888:8888/tcp -t oxidized/oxidized:latest oxidized\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"configuration\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Configuration\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe need a configuration file to guide Oxidized running process\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003evi config\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe following is the configuration sample that I am running with\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 56 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nn\"\u003e---\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eusername\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eadmin\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eP@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ejunos\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eresolve_dns\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003einterval\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e3600\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003euse_syslog\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edebug\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ethreads\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e30\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eretries\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eprompt\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e!\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eruby/regexp /^([\\w.@-]+[#\u0026gt;]\\s?)$/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003erest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0.0.0.0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003enext_adds_job\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003evars\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e{}\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003egroups\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e{}\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emodels\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e{}\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003epid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/root/.config/oxidized/pid\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ecrash\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edirectory\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/root/.config/oxidized/crashes\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ehostnames\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estats\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ehistory_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003einput\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edefault\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003essh, telnet\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edebug\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003essh\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003esecure\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003efalse\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eftp\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003epassive\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eutf8_encoded\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edefault\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003egit\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003efile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edirectory\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/root/.config/oxidized/configs\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003egit\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003esingle_repo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003euser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eOxidized\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eemail\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eoxidized@email.target\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003erepo\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;~/.config/oxidized/oxidized.git\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003esource\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edefault\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ecsv\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ecsv\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003efile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e~/.config/oxidized/router.db\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003edelimiter\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e!\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eruby/regexp /:/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emap\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eip\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emodel\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eusername\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emodel_map\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ecisco\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eios\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ejuniper\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ejunos\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eunifiap\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eairos\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eedgeos\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eedgeos\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"device-list\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#device-list\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Device list'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Device list\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe table based on the configuration we just defined, will be formatted as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eName\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eIP\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eModel\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eUsername\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ePassword\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDevice Name\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e172.16.1.x\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eunifiap\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003esysadmin\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eP@ssw0rd!\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo populate the table, we can open the editor \u003ccode\u003evi router.db\u003c/code\u003e, and then inset the following sample entries\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-723658597f7b728a89aec908d3a50ba0-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eBedroom1_ap:172.16.1.114:unifiap:sysadmin:P@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eKitchen_ap:172.16.1.121:unifiap:sysadmin:P@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eCinema_ap:172.16.1.160:unifiap:sysadmin:P@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eServerRoom_ap:172.16.1.115:unifiap:sysadmin:P@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eFirewall:172.16.1.1:edgeos:ubnt:P@ssw0rd!\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we are ready, we have the configuration all set for this installation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"web-interface\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#web-interface\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Web Interface'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Web Interface\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eLaunching our browser to the oxidized site hosted on \u003ccode\u003eTCP 8888\u003c/code\u003e renders the current status\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/posts/obsidian-to-hugo-with-obsidian2hugo/\" rel=\"\"\u003eHugo and Obsidian\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003e(image unavailable — “List of Devices Monitored for Change Detection” screenshot not in source vault)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom here we can see all the version changes for the devices configuration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/network-change-detection-with-oxidized-and-git/assets/images/index_2020-07-01-16-46-41.png\" alt=\"History of Changes on the Firewall Device\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd even select any one of these change sets, and view the changes which were applied to the configuration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/network-change-detection-with-oxidized-and-git/assets/images/index_2020-07-01-16-48-20.png\" alt=\"Change Difference View\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"closing-thoughts\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Closing Thoughts\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, I wonder if we could integrate this with Azure?\u0026hellip;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Obsidian to Hugo with Obsidian2Hugo",
        "date_published" : "2022-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2022-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/obsidian-to-hugo-with-obsidian2hugo/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/obsidian-to-hugo-with-obsidian2hugo/",
        "summary": "My Blog has evolved over the years, initially hosted on Wordpress, but some 6 years back I abandond that plaform for Static Sites, initially with Jekyll and used Github Pages, but that also got sunset in favor of my current generator Hugo.\nAs part of my current workflow, I use Obsidian for almost all my notes, which includes the posts which you get to read publically on this blog.\nTo make this happen, there are some very cool open source projects which I am relying to pipeline the content for its raw source, to the presentation which is finally published.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eMy Blog has evolved over the years, initially hosted on Wordpress, but some 6 years back I abandond that plaform for Static Sites, initially with Jekyll and used Github Pages, but that also got sunset in favor of my current generator Hugo.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs part of my current workflow, I use Obsidian for almost all my notes, which includes the posts which you get to read publically on this blog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo make this happen, there are some very cool open source projects which I am relying to pipeline the content for its raw source, to the presentation which is finally published.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll the documentation I create, presonally and professionally, is authored in Markdown. So keeping this source standard based is critically important to me.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne thing I didn’t like was to have to put the title into frontmatter and to manually write the description used by hugo as a \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;meta\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e description which is important for search engine optimization (SEO). The here introduced \u003ccode\u003eobsidian2hugo\u003c/code\u003e does exactly this. I t parses a obsidian source (sub)tree, parses every markdown file and extracts (and deletes) a \u003ccode\u003eh1\u003c/code\u003e title (if present) and uses the content of a named \u003ccode\u003eh2\u003c/code\u003e header (standard \u003ccode\u003e## tl;dr\u003c/code\u003e)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"obsidian-export\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Obsidian Export\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/aadimator/obsidian-export\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://github.com/aadimator/obsidian-export\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"dependencies\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#dependencies\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Dependencies'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Dependencies\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eInstall the rust development tools on our workstation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003excode-select --install\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ebrew install rust\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"clone-and-build\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#clone-and-build\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Clone and Build'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Clone and Build\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eGrab the source of the tool, and compile it\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ~/vault\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egit clone https://github.com/aadimator/obsidian-export\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e obsidian-export\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecargo build --release --locked\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecp target/release/obsidian-export ~/vault/obsidian-exporter\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ..\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./obsidian-exporter --help\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"export-from-the-vault\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Export from the Vault\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir ./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./obsidian-exporter ./Cranium/knowledge/blog  ./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article --hard-linebreaks --no-recursive-embeds --embed-info --hugo-frontmatter --retain-wikilinks --flat\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Using a Start-At folder\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./obsidian-exporter ./Cranium/  ./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article --start-at ./Cranium/knowledge/blog --hard-linebreaks --no-recursive-embeds --embed-info  --retain-wikilinks --flat --hugo-frontmatter\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Using an .export-ignore\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./obsidian-exporter ./Cranium/  ./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article --hard-linebreaks --no-recursive-embeds --embed-info  --retain-wikilinks --flat --hugo-frontmatter\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e### From the Video\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./obsidian-exporter ./Cranium/  ./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article --add-titles --frontmatter\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ealways\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"hugo-obsidian\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Hugo Obsidian\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"install\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#install\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Install'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Install\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ego install github.com/aadimator/hugo-obsidian@latest\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"test\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#test\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Test'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Test\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e~/go/bin/hugo-obsidian --help\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"convert-content\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#convert-content\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Convert Content'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Convert Content\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-187d16f692b545405c576f6fdacd61f5-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehugo-obsidian -input\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e./damianflynn.com-hugo/content/article -output\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003edamianflynn.com-hugo/assets/indices -index\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e -root\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Active Directory Administrative Limits: Finding and Resolving the Bloat",
        "date_published" : "2021-07-27T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-07-27T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/active-directory-administrative-limits-finding-and-resolving-the-bloat/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/active-directory-administrative-limits-finding-and-resolving-the-bloat/",
        "summary": "I recently ran into an issue with a particular environment where Active Directory and PKI services were deployed. One of the service accounts which I was attempting to \u0026lsquo;unlock\u0026rsquo; refused to co-operate and instead offered the most unhelpful message.\nAdministrative limit for this request was exceeded - this was not my first time encountering the message, previously this haunted me while I was managing a Windows PKI infrastructure and with some quick searches, confirmed my initial suspicion. This is a symptom of an AD object quite simply being to large!\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eI recently ran into an issue with a particular environment where Active Directory and PKI services were deployed. One of the service accounts which I was attempting to \u0026lsquo;unlock\u0026rsquo; refused to co-operate and instead offered the most unhelpful message.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eAdministrative limit for this request was exceeded\u003c/code\u003e - this was not my first time encountering the message, previously this haunted me while I was managing a Windows PKI infrastructure and with some quick searches, confirmed my initial suspicion. This is a symptom of an AD object quite simply being to large!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"explaination\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Explaination\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eActive Directory is in the simplest form a Database, and each object can be considered as a row in this database. Like any database there are limits to what data can be stored in the table, the type of data, but also the amount.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"resolving-the-problem\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Resolving the problem\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing a tool like \u003cstrong\u003eADSI Edit\u003c/strong\u003e will allow you to open the database, and select the schema partition we would like to work with. Standard objects which we can see in the \u003cem\u003eActive Directory Users and Computers\u003c/em\u003e extension are all hosted in the partition called the \u003cem\u003eDefault Naming Context\u003c/em\u003e; which is where we need to focus for this problem\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/active-directory-administrative-limits-finding-and-resolving-the-bloat/sw_active-directory_administrative-limits_2021-07-27-10-55-18.png\" alt=\"ADSI Edit - Default Naming Context\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"identifying-the-bloat\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#identifying-the-bloat\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Identifying the Bloat'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Identifying the Bloat\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThere is no super cool trick here, we just need a little investigation. Start by navigating the OU structure you are familiar with in Active Directory Users and Computers, to locate the account with issues.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/active-directory-administrative-limits-finding-and-resolving-the-bloat/sw_active-directory_administrative-limits_2021-07-27-11-00-37.png\" alt=\"AD Object Navigation in ADSI Edit\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRight Click on the object, and select \u003cstrong\u003eProperties\u003c/strong\u003e where you now get to view the 100\u0026rsquo;s of columns of data which AD stores for each object.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick on the \u003cstrong\u003eFilter\u003c/strong\u003e button and enable the option \u003cem\u003eShow only attributes that have values\u003c/em\u003e - this will remove all the columns which are empty - and therefore not adding to our overside object!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/active-directory-administrative-limits-finding-and-resolving-the-bloat/sw_active-directory_administrative-limits_2021-07-27-11-03-48.png\" alt=\"ADSI Properties Filter\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, you can check each of the remaining attributes (columns) and see what they contain, I\u0026rsquo;ll save a few minutes, and in this case I expect my issue is to do with Certificates, so we will focus on the attribute called \u003cem\u003euserCertificate\u003c/em\u003e which contains an collection of \u003cem\u003e[byte[]]\u003c/em\u003e, each representing a Base64 encoded Certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBINGO! looking at this property I can see 100\u0026rsquo;s of entries, and each one has the same \u003cem\u003ebyte[]\u003c/em\u003e string, which implies the same certificate is loaded into the object a lot of times.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am going to flush the lot of them out, as these are added by the system, and it will reload them as required; but for now, I am simply the garbage collector.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the UX, we can delete these 1 at a time, so we need a little automation, or the rest of the week will be wasted.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"powershell-helper\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Powershell Helper\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing standard Active Directory module for Powershell, we can get a reference to the object which needs to be flushed\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certUser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-Aduser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;svc_PKI_NDES\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Properties\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertificates\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, let\u0026rsquo;s check what we got from AD\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certuser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eCertificates\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eCount\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e1169\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRight, time to fix this, we will use the following command to remove all the certificates from the object\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ePS \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eC:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eUsers\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esysadmin\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAD\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset-ADUser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esvc_PKI_NDES\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Certificates\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"vm\"\u003e@\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd, let\u0026rsquo;s confirm it worked\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3437aee2a0c70b6ba7743a5244a32a5e-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certuser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-ADUser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esvc_PKI_NDES\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Properties\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCertificates\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certuser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eCertificates\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ecount\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd now, just check that you can unlock the account, or complete the operation that sent you chasing this wild goose!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "FreeRADIUS for 802.1X with Certificates: EAP and PKI Setup",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-07T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-07T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/freeradius-for-802.1x-with-certificates-eap-and-pki-setup/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/freeradius-for-802.1x-with-certificates-eap-and-pki-setup/",
        "summary": "In a pervious post, I covered the steps to deploy the current stable release of FreeRadius, by installing the packages from the NetworkRadius organizations repository.\nWe will now, focus on configuring the FreeRadius server so that it can authenticate 802.1x requests, which depends on valid [Computer Certificates](/posts/issue-a-windows-pki-certificate-to-a-linux-server-with-openssl/#Creating our Certificate Request).\nWhy? Why would we go to this trouble, especially given the fact that Windows has shipped with its own NPS service, for the past 20 years?\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eIn a pervious post, I covered the steps to \u003ca href=\"/posts/install-freeradius-on-ubuntu-from-the-network-radius-repository/\" rel=\"\"\u003edeploy the current stable release of FreeRadius, by installing the packages from the NetworkRadius organizations repository\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe will now, focus on configuring the FreeRadius server so that it can authenticate 802.1x requests, which depends on valid [Computer Certificates](/posts/issue-a-windows-pki-certificate-to-a-linux-server-with-openssl/#Creating our Certificate Request).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"why\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Why?\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhy would we go to this trouble, especially given the fact that Windows has shipped with its own NPS service, for the past 20 years?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimple really, In the world of Cloud First, many customers are now selecting the option of Azure AD Joined only, for their machines in preference to AD Joined, or even Hybrid Joined. This matters, as the Windows NPS Service is hardcoded to check if a computer account object is present in the Active Directory; which is obviously not the case for Cloud Only systems. The result - every authentication request will automatically respond as failed validation!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"configuring-free-radius\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Configuring Free Radius\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are a number of files used to configure the behavior of the FreeRadius service, the default configuration within these files is very verbose, so in this post we will clean up the configuration, and implement the settings required to validate 802.1x requests - Specifically we will check the computer certificate to ensure it is valid.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eFreeRaidus by default protects all the configuration so that your normal account has no access to the files, and folders. To enable a lower resistance path to working on this server, you can \u003cstrong\u003eAssume \u003ccode\u003eroot\u003c/code\u003e access\u003c/strong\u003e with the following command\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo su -\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"radius-server\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#radius-server\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Radius Server'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Radius Server\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe will turn off proxy features in the server, and enable logging for authentication. We begin by editing the core configuration file called \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/radiusd.conf\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 74 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eprefix\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/usr\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eexec_prefix\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/usr\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003esysconfdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/etc\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elocalstatedir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/var\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003esbindir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${exec_prefix}/sbin\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elogdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/var/log/freeradius\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eraddbdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/etc/freeradius\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eradacctdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${logdir}/radacct\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003efreeradius\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003econfdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${raddbdir}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003emodconfdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${confdir}/mods-config\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecertdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${confdir}/certs\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecadir\u003c/span\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${confdir}/certs\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003erun_dir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${localstatedir}/run/${name}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edb_dir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${raddbdir}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elibdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e/usr/lib/freeradius\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003epidfile\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${run_dir}/${name}.pid\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecorrect_escapes\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003emax_request_time\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e30\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecleanup_delay\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e5\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003emax_requests\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e16384\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ehostname_lookups\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elog {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edestination\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003efiles\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  colourise = yes\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  file = ${logdir}/radius.log\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  syslog_facility = daemon\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  stripped_names = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  auth = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  auth_badpass = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  auth_goodpass = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  msg_denied = \u0026#34;You are already logged in - access denied\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003echeckrad\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e${sbindir}/checkrad\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eENV {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003esecurity {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003euser\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003efreerad\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  group = freerad\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  allow_core_dumps = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  max_attributes = 200\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  reject_delay = 1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  status_server = yes\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eproxy_requests\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eyes\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e$INCLUDE proxy.conf\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e$INCLUDE clients.conf\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ethread pool {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003estart_servers\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e5\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  max_servers = 32\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  min_spare_servers = 3\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  max_spare_servers = 10\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  max_requests_per_server = 0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  auto_limit_acct = no\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003emodules {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e$INCLUDE mods-enabled/\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003einstantiate {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003epolicy {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e$INCLUDE policy.d/\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e$INCLUDE sites-enabled/\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"proxy-configuration\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#proxy-configuration\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Proxy Configuration'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Proxy Configuration\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe configuration of the proxy feature is maintained in the file `/etc/freeradius/proxy.conf'\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 44 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eproxy server {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edefault_fallback\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ehome_server localhost {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eauth\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  ipaddr = 127.0.0.1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  port = 1812\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  secret = testing123\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  response_window = 20\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  zombie_period = 40\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  revive_interval = 120\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  status_check = status-server\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  check_interval = 30\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  check_timeout = 4\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  num_answers_to_alive = 3\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  max_outstanding = 65536\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecoa {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eirt\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e2\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    mrt = 16\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    mrc = 5\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    mrd = 30\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  }\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elimit {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003emax_connections\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e16\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    max_requests = 0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    lifetime = 0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e    idle_timeout = 0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  }\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ehome_server_pool my_auth_failover {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003efail-over\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e  home_server = localhost\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003erealm example.com {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eauth_pool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003emy_auth_failover\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003erealm LOCAL {\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"radius-clients\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#radius-clients\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Radius Clients'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Radius Clients\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo specify the clients allowed to send requests to the RADIUS server. Most of the times we want to configure a router or wireless access points as a Network Access Server (NAS), so that WiFi clients connecting will communicate to the RADIUS server via the router. We define the client networks in the file \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/clients.conf\u003c/code\u003e configuration file\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003econf\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 27 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e############################ /clients.conf\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eclient localhost {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  ipaddr = 127.0.0.1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  proto = *\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  secret = testing123\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  require_message_authenticator = no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  nas_type = other\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  limit {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    max_connections = 16\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    lifetime = 0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    idle_timeout = 30\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e}\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# IPv6 Client\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eclient localhost_ipv6 {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  ipv6addr= ::1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  secret= testing123\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e}\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# Our Clients Network\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eclient private-network-1 {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  ipaddr= 10.46.0.0/16\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  secret= radius\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  require_message_authenticator = yes\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe section \u003cstrong\u003eprivate-network-1\u003c/strong\u003e lists the IP range of the Radius Clients (ipaddr) and the secret they must provide to be trusted (secret).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"freeradius-default-service\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#freeradius-default-service\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'FreeRadius Default Service'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    FreeRadius Default Service\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNext we will update the service so that the modules required for WiFi authentication are enabled, and all additional services are disabled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe will replace the content in \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/sites-enabled/default\u003c/code\u003e with the following configuration\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003econf\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 68 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e############################ sites-enabled/default\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eserver {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  listen {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    type = auth\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    port = 1812\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    ipaddr = *\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  authorize {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    preprocess\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    eap {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      ok = return\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    expiration\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    logintime\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  authenticate {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    eap\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Auth-Type eap {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      eap {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        handled = 1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      if (handled \u0026amp;\u0026amp; (Response-Packet-Type == Access-Challenge)) {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        attr_filter.access_challenge.post-auth\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        handled # override the \u0026#34;updated\u0026#34; code from attr_filter\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  preacct {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    preprocess\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    acct_unique\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    suffix\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    files\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  accounting {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    detail\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    radutmp\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    attr_filter.accounting_response\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  session {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    radutmp\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  post-auth {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Post-Auth-Type REJECT {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      attr_filter.access_reject\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Post-Auth-Type Challenge {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      remove_reply_message_if_eap\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      attr_filter.access_challenge.post-auth\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    }        \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  pre-proxy {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  post-proxy {\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    eap\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  }\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"freeradius-eap-configuration\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  FreeRadius EAP Configuration\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the heart of the configuration, we will disable all the options and focus only on using EAP-TLS for the WiFi authentication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis configuration will require that we complete the following steps\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIssue a certificate for this Radius Server, from the same PKI service which we will be issuing certificates to our client devices.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Private Key for this issued Certificate is stored on this server\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Root Certificate of the chain we are issuing from (intermediate issuing servers are not required) is also available on this server\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA working folder, to be used to host the certificates passed from the clients for verification\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"create-a-certificate-for-the-radius-server\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#create-a-certificate-for-the-radius-server\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Create a Certificate for the Radius Server'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Create a Certificate for the Radius Server\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThere are a few steps to this process, Follow this guide \u003cstrong\u003eCreate PKI Certificate for Linux Server\u003c/strong\u003e to complete the exercise, after which we should have a certificate which matches the requirements called \u003ccode\u003eserver.pem\u003c/code\u003e (1), and a matching private key file called \u003ccode\u003eserver.key\u003c/code\u003e (2)  to place in our \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/certs\u003c/code\u003e folder.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe need to ensure also the service has read access to this files\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003echmod \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e644\u003c/span\u003e /etc/freeradius/certs/server.pem\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003echmod \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e644\u003c/span\u003e /etc/freeradius/certs/server.key\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"pki-chain-for-radius-server\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#pki-chain-for-radius-server\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'PKI Chain for Radius Server'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    PKI Chain for Radius Server\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe certificates we have created for the Server and the Clients which will be authenticating to the server are all issued by the same PKI environment. To successfully validate any certificate, we will need a copy of the public keys for each server in this chain, which will be stored in Base64 format in the \u003ccode\u003eca.pem\u003c/code\u003e(3) file.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"manually-creating-the-pem-file\"\u003eManually Creating the PEM File\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#manually-creating-the-pem-file\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Manually Creating the PEM File'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eExport all the certificates in the chain, for example \u003cem\u003eRoot CA\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eIssuing CA\u003c/em\u003e in turn as Base64.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCopy all the Certificates content into a file called \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/ca.pem\u003c/code\u003e, so that it looks similar to the following example - If you issue your certificates directly from your Root CA, then there will be only 1 certificate, or more typically you will have multiple issuers, implying you will have multiple to paste.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 15 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eMIIGRDCCBCygAwIBAgITaQAAAASav/V29nA9rgAAAAAABDANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsF\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e....\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e.... Root CA Base64 Content\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e....\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003egQtDSbTj5kKWLuyPEWT3VepWpJ0MRIceZ/UCpf9KCkR8y9hcMEd+1/vDlFD/AJxz\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eMvZ0K7TQqxqCJ5OiB3SfH91Bc1D7Yvwn\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e-----END CERTIFICATE-----\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eMIIGRDCCBCygAwIBAgITaQAAAASav/V29nA9rgAAAAAABDANBgkqhkiG9w0BAQsF\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e....\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e.... Issuing CA Base64 Content\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e....\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eMvZ0K7TQqxqCJ5OiB3SfH91Bc1D7Yvwn\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e-----END CERTIFICATE-----\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"creating-pem-from-a-pfx\"\u003eCreating PEM from a PFX\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#creating-pem-from-a-pfx\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Creating PEM from a PFX'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf we have a PFX file containing the chain of certificates, we can use openssl to create the \u003ccode\u003eca.pem\u003c/code\u003e file for us\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl pkcs12 -in exported.pfx -cacerts -nokeys -chain -out ca.pem\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"dh-ciphers\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#dh-ciphers\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'DH Ciphers'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    DH Ciphers\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor DH cipher suites to work, you have to run OpenSSL to create the DH file first:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl dhparam -out certs/dh \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2048\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"eap-module\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#eap-module\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'EAP Module'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    EAP Module\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe begin by creating a soft link for EAP module under \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ln -s /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-available/eap /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen change group right of \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/eap\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chgrp -h freerad /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-available/eap\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chown -R freerad:freerad /etc/freeradius/3.0/mods-enabled/eap\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext configure the logic we need the server to follow. We will edit the file for the module \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/mods-available/eap\u003c/code\u003e and set the content as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003econf\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 47 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e############################ /etc/freeradius/mods-available/eap\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eeap\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edefault_eap_type\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etls\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etimer_expire\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e60\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eignore_unknown_eap_types\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecisco_accounting_username_bug\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emax_sessions\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e4096\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etls\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econfdir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecerts\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecadir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003econfdir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecerts\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eprivate_key_password\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eS3cur3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e!\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e2021\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eprivate_key_file\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertdir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ekey\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertificate_file\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertdir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epem\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eca_path\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecadir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eca_file\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecadir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eca\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epem\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edh_file\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e$\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertdir\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edh\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erandom_file\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edev\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eurandom\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecipher_list\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;HIGH\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emake_cert_command\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;${certdir}/bootstrap\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eecdh_curve\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;prime256v1\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etls_max_version\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etls_min_version\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.2\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecache\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Optionally enable\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003elifetime\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e24\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# hours\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emax_entries\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e255\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003everify\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etmpdir\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003evar\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003elog\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003efreeradius\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eradiusd\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eclient\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/usr/bin/openssl verify -CAfile ${..ca_file} %{TLS-Client-Cert-Filename}\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eocsp\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# optionally enable\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eoverride_cert_url\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eurl\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;http://aez-app-prd-scep.azurewebsites.net/ocsp/\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esoftfail\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eyes\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etimeout\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e10\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003euse_nonce\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eno\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"working-folder-for-verification\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#working-folder-for-verification\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Working folder for Verification'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Working folder for Verification\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe EAP flow utilizes \u003ccode\u003eopenssl\u003c/code\u003e to validate the clients certificate, in order to complete this, we need to store the certificate to the file system first, and ensure that the service has access to this folder\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mkdir /var/log/freeradius/radiusd\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chown freerad:freerad /var/log/freeradius/radiusd\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"running-in-debug-mode\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Running in Debug mode\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOur FreeRadius service is now ready to test, to make this process a lot easier, we can choose to start the service interactively in the console, and watch the debug logs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esystemctl stop freeradius\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e/usr/sbin.freeradius -x \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThis is a great scenario to leverage \u003ccode\u003etmux\u003c/code\u003e, which will allow you have multiple sessions, and keep the session open even after you disconnect, rendering it simple to return to at a later stage\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eWith the service online, we can emulate a client connecting, and providing its client secret e.g. \u003cem\u003etesting123\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eradtest client@ullensaker.kommune.no testing123 127.0.0.1 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e testing123 -x\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen you are satisfied that all is good, we can restart in service mode\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-15\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-15\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esystemctl start freeradius\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow - Get a Certificate on your test client, and WiFi gateways configured to communicate with our Radius server; and TEST!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"synchronizing-multiple-servers\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#synchronizing-multiple-servers\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Synchronizing Multiple Servers'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Synchronizing Multiple Servers\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor production deployments, you will wish to have multiple instances of the FreeRadius server deployed. As the function of the server is primarily stateless, we really only need to synchronies the actual configuration files, to ensure all our instances are built the same.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe FreeRadius configuration is protected by the  root user; therefore to sync files, we need to ensure that the source permissions are respected.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo allow \u003ccode\u003ersync\u003c/code\u003e complete this, we need to append to the \u003cstrong\u003esudoers\u003c/strong\u003e file \u003ccode\u003e/etc/sudoers\u003c/code\u003e setup your user like this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eusername ALL= NOPASSWD:/usr/bin/rsync\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003cstrong\u003eNOPASSWD:/usr/bin/rsync\u003c/strong\u003e tells sudo that when your user runs \u003cstrong\u003e/usr/bin/rsync\u003c/strong\u003e or just \u003cstrong\u003ersync\u003c/strong\u003e that no password is needed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe can try the following to sync the files from our source server using SSH based authentication.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-16\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-3ebe01c0c962efa5da2fe8c663728b1d-16\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ersync -avz -e ssh username@x.x.x.x:/etc/freeradius /etc/freeradius --rsync-path\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;sudo rsync\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Extract Public and Private Keys from a PFX with OpenSSL",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-05T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-05T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/extract-public-and-private-keys-from-a-pfx-with-openssl/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/extract-public-and-private-keys-from-a-pfx-with-openssl/",
        "summary": " OpenSSL seperating a PFX into Public and Private Key Files Using OpenSSL we can extract the private key, and the certificate into independent file\u0026rsquo;s, which is required for most networking devices, and linux services.\nYou will need to install the OpenSSL, package, either on your system.\nExport the private key from the PFX file We begin, by passing in the PFX and requesting the Private key to be placed into its own file. This process will require that you provide the password which is used to protect the PFX file, and also a new password to protect the new private key file (this is not optional).\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"openssl-seperating-a-pfx-into-public-and-private-key-files\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#openssl-seperating-a-pfx-into-public-and-private-key-files\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'OpenSSL seperating a PFX into Public and Private Key Files'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"openssl-seperating-a-pfx-into-public-and-private-key-files\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  OpenSSL seperating a PFX into Public and Private Key Files\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing \u003cstrong\u003eOpenSSL\u003c/strong\u003e we can extract the private key, and the certificate into independent file\u0026rsquo;s, which is required for most networking devices, and linux services.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou will need to install the \u003ca href=\"/posts/build-and-install-the-latest-openssl-on-ubuntu/\" rel=\"\"\u003eOpenSSL\u003c/a\u003e, package, either on your system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"export-the-private-key-from-the-pfx-file\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Export the private key from the PFX file\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe begin, by passing in the PFX and requesting the Private key to be placed into its own file. This process will require that you provide the password which is used to protect the PFX file, and also a new password to protect the new private key file (this is not optional).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl pkcs12 -in filename.pfx -nocerts -out PrivateKeyWithPassword.pem\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnter\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eImport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eInput\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eexport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eof\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePFX\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eFile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMAC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003everified\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOK\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnter\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePEM\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003epass\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ephrase\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMin\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mi\"\u003e5\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eChar\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eNew\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eTemp\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"remove-the-passphrase-from-the-private-key\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#remove-the-passphrase-from-the-private-key\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Remove the passphrase from the private key'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Remove the passphrase from the private key\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe previous step created a new password protected file, which we called \u003ccode\u003ePrivateKeyWithPassword.pem\u003c/code\u003e that contains only the certificates private key. In many cases, we may need to use this file, without the password protection, so the following step will generate a new private key file \u003ccode\u003ekey.pem\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl rsa -in PrivateKeyWithPassword.pem -out Private.key\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eEnter pass phrase for c:\\temp\\SSL\\key.pem: [Min 5 Char New Temp Password]\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewriting RSA key\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"export-the-public-certificate-from-the-pfx-file\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Export the public certificate from the PFX file\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe final requirement in this typical configuration is to export the public certificate as an independent file from the PFX without the private key.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSimilar to the previous steps, we will provide the name of the PFX and the new certificate file, for example \u003ccode\u003ecert.pem\u003c/code\u003e. Again as the PFX contains the private key, you need to provide the export password to allow this process to complete.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl pkcs12 -in filename.pfx -clcerts -nokeys -out cert.pem\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnter\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eImport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eInput\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eexport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eof\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePFX\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eFile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMAC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003everified\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOK\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"exporting-all-cerificates-in-the-chain\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#exporting-all-cerificates-in-the-chain\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Exporting all cerificates in the chain'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Exporting all cerificates in the chain\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWhen your PFX contains all the certificates in the chain, you can also export all these to the certificate file, \u003ccode\u003ecert.pem\u003c/code\u003e using the following command syntax.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl.exe pkcs12 -in filename.pfx -out cert.pem -nodes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eoutput\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-1641e47444b44d3b4f855f72e9274fea-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnter\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eImport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eInput\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eexport\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eof\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ethe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePFX\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"ne\"\u003eFile\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMAC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003everified\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOK\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Export a PFX from the Windows Certificate Store (MMC and PowerShell)",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-04T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-04T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/export-a-pfx-from-the-windows-certificate-store-mmc-and-powershell/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/export-a-pfx-from-the-windows-certificate-store-mmc-and-powershell/",
        "summary": " Exporting Windows Certificates to PFX A .pfx file is in essence an archive which can contain multiple objects, and can also be password protected; The format of this file is known as PKCS#12\nTypically, a .pfx usually contains one or more certificate, typically the chain of upstream authorities, and the corresponding private key. The most common usage of a PFX file is simplify certificate distribution to alternate systems or deployed to services.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"exporting-windows-certificates-to-pfx\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#exporting-windows-certificates-to-pfx\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Exporting Windows Certificates to PFX'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"exporting-windows-certificates-to-pfx\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Exporting Windows Certificates to PFX\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e file is in essence an archive which can contain multiple objects, and can also be password protected; The format of this file is known as \u003cem\u003ePKCS#12\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTypically, a \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e usually contains one or more certificate, typically the chain of upstream authorities, and the corresponding private key. The most common usage of a PFX file is simplify certificate distribution to alternate systems or deployed to services.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"logical-stores\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Logical stores\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWithin Windows, all certificates exist in logical storage locations referred to as \u003cstrong\u003ecertificate stores\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLogical stores are virtual locations that map to certificate physical paths. Powershell uses the \u003cstrong\u003eCert\u003c/strong\u003e PSDrive to map certificates to the physical stores.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eJust to keep things nice and simple, Microsoft Style \u003cem\u003e(yes I am being sarcastic)\u003c/em\u003e The \u003cstrong\u003eCertificates\u003c/strong\u003e Microsoft Management Console (MMC) logical store labeling is different from the \u003cstrong\u003eCert\u003c/strong\u003e PSDrive store labeling. The table below shows the comparison between both:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003ePS CERT: Drive\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eCertificates MMC\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eMy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePersonal\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRemote Desktop\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRemote Desktop\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRoot\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTrusted Root Certification Authorities\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eCA\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eIntermediate Certification Authorities\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAuthRoot\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eThird-Party Root Certification Authorities\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTrustedPublisher\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTrusted Publishers\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eTrust\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eEnterprise Trust\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eUserDS\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eActive Directory User Object\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"exporting-the-certificates\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Exporting the Certificates\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis article will guide the relatively simple steps required to extract a certificate from the logical store, and create a PFX that we can use to transport the certificate to other systems. PFX support the containment of Private Keys, and should typically be password protected to assist in securing the certificate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"windows-certificates-mmc\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#windows-certificates-mmc\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Windows Certificates MMC'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Windows Certificates MMC\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the \u003cem\u003eCertificates\u003c/em\u003e Snap-In the following steps will guide to exporting the certificate to a PFX file, which we can later process with the OpenSSL tools.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStart the Microsoft Management Console \u0026gt; Run \u003ccode\u003emmc.exe\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the \u003cstrong\u003eConsole\u003c/strong\u003e menu and then click \u003cstrong\u003eAdd/Remove Snap-in\u003c/strong\u003e.\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick the \u003cstrong\u003eAdd\u003c/strong\u003e button and then choose the \u003cstrong\u003ecertificates\u003c/strong\u003e snap-in and click on \u003cstrong\u003eAdd\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect \u003cstrong\u003eCertificates\u003c/strong\u003e and click \u003cstrong\u003eAdd\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect \u003cstrong\u003eComputer Account\u003c/strong\u003e then click \u003cstrong\u003eNext\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect \u003cstrong\u003eLocal Computer\u003c/strong\u003e and then click \u003cstrong\u003eOK\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick \u003cstrong\u003eClose\u003c/strong\u003e and then click \u003cstrong\u003eOK\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the Snap in now loaded and focused on the \u003cem\u003eLocal Computer Certificate Store\u003c/em\u003e, we can locate a target \u003cem\u003eCertificate\u003c/em\u003e to export.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eExpand the menu for \u003cstrong\u003eCertificates\u003c/strong\u003e and click on the \u003cstrong\u003ePersonal\u003c/strong\u003e folder.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight click on the certificate that you want to export and select \u003cstrong\u003eAll tasks\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026gt; \u003cstrong\u003eExport\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA wizard will appear - \u003cstrong\u003eExport Certificate\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMake sure you \u003cstrong\u003echeck\u003c/strong\u003e the box to include the \u003cstrong\u003eprivate key\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eYou will be asked to password protect the PFX for importing\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eContinue through with this wizard until you have a \u003ccode\u003e.PFX\u003c/code\u003e file.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRather simple right. You now have a \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e file, which is password protected, containing your Certificate and its private key\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"powershell\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#powershell\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Powershell'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Powershell\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe Powershell \u003ccode\u003ePKI\u003c/code\u003e module can be used to export or import PFX files. The following are some examples of the process\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"export-pfxcertificate\"\u003eExport-PfxCertificate\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#export-pfxcertificate\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Export-PfxCertificate'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003eExport-PfxCertificate\u003c/code\u003e cmdlet exports a certificate or to a Personal Information Exchange \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e file. By default, extended properties and the entire chain are exported.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo export a \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e certificate a password is needed for encrypting the private key.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the example below, we use the \u003cstrong\u003eSubject\u003c/strong\u003e property to find the certificate to be exported by selecting the certificate whose Subject value equals \u003cem\u003emyCertificate\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-ChildItem\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Path\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCert\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eLocalMachine\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMy\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eWhere-Object\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$_\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eSubject\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-match\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;myCertificate\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter selecting the certificate it can be exported from its store location to a folder with the command below:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$password\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;P@ssw0rd\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eConvertTo-SecureString\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-AsPlainText\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Force\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eExport-PfxCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Cert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$certificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-FilePath\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$env:USERPROFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eDocuments\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003emyCertificate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003epfx\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Password\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$password\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"importing-a-certificate\"\u003eImporting a Certificate\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#importing-a-certificate\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Importing a Certificate'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe Powershell Cmdlet \u003ccode\u003eImport-PfxCertificate\u003c/code\u003e is used to install a \u003ccode\u003e.pfx\u003c/code\u003e certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo install a PFX certificate to the current user\u0026rsquo;s personal store, use the command below:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-a791c1fa32d435667f6db8139f2fb54e-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eImport-PfxCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-FilePath\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e./\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePFXCertificate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003epfx\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CertStoreLocation\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCert\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCurrentUser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMy\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Password\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eP\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e@ssw0rd\u003c/span\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo install into the system personal location change the store location in the command above from \u003ccode\u003eCert:\\CurrentUser\\My\u003c/code\u003e to \u003ccode\u003eCert:\\LocalMachine\\My\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Issue a Windows PKI Certificate to a Linux Server with OpenSSL",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-03T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-03T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/issue-a-windows-pki-certificate-to-a-linux-server-with-openssl/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/issue-a-windows-pki-certificate-to-a-linux-server-with-openssl/",
        "summary": " Issuing a Certificate using OpenSSL It is enevitable, that at some point in time, you will need to issue a certificate for your system. There are a couple of relativly simple steps to acheive this, begining with the creation of a certificate request, then submitting this to an online certificate authority, which will process the request and issue you a certificate with both a Public and Private Key.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"issuing-a-certificate-using-openssl\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#issuing-a-certificate-using-openssl\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Issuing a Certificate using OpenSSL'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"issuing-a-certificate-using-openssl\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Issuing a Certificate using OpenSSL\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt is enevitable, that at some point in time, you will need to issue a certificate for your system. There are a couple of relativly simple steps to acheive this, begining with the creation of a certificate request, then submitting this to an online certificate authority, which will process the request and issue you a certificate with both a Public and Private Key.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn this post, we will use the \u003cstrong\u003e\u003ca href=\"/posts/build-and-install-the-latest-openssl-on-ubuntu/\" rel=\"\"\u003eOpenSSL\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e utility to create such a request file, and walk trough the steps of issuing a certificate from a Windows PKI Server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"creating-our-certificate-request\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Creating our Certificate Request\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe will create a Certificate Request template file which defines the requirements or purpose of the certificate, optional data can be encoded into the certificate, for illustrative purposes. I will include Subject Alternate Name in the issued certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eIn this article, the certificates we are working with are to be used in validating a computers identity. This is a common requirement when authenticating with WiFi or VPN services within the organisation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe request file we create can be named as you wish, I will be using  \u003ccode\u003e~/san.cnf\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 14 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e[ req ]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edefault_bits\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e2048\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edistinguished_name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ereq_distinguished_name\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ereq_extensions\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003ereq_ext\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e[ req_distinguished_name ]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecountryName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eCountry Name (2 letter code)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003estateOrProvinceName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eState or Province Name (full name)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003elocalityName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eLocality Name (eg, city)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eorganizationName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eOrganization Name (eg, company)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ecommonName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eCommon Name (e.g. server FQDN or YOUR name)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e[ req_ext ]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003esubjectAltName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e@alt_names\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003e[alt_names]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eDNS.1\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eradius.diginerve.ie\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe above is a working template - the only changes you should make to this file is the \u003cstrong\u003eatl_names\u003c/strong\u003e at the bottom, where these  should represent the name of the system you wish to have the certificate issued on behalf of; In my example this is \u003cem\u003eradius.diginerve.ie\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"create-the-private-key\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Create the Private Key\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom the computer you are wishing to create the certificate for (for example a \u003ca href=\"/posts/install-freeradius-on-ubuntu-from-the-network-radius-repository/\" rel=\"\"\u003eLinux FreeRadius server\u003c/a\u003e, we will generate the request for private key using the template as follows.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eOpenSSL will ask some additional questions during execution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eThe following command parameters instruct \u003ca href=\"/posts/build-and-install-the-latest-openssl-on-ubuntu/\" rel=\"\"\u003eOpenSSL\u003c/a\u003e to generate a certificate request\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003ereq\u003c/code\u003e: OpenSSL should generate a Certificate Request\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-newkey rsa:2048\u003c/code\u003e: The Request should be encrypted using \u003cstrong\u003eRSA 2048\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-nodes\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-keyout server.key\u003c/code\u003e: The Private Key should be saved as \u003ccode\u003eserver.key\u003c/code\u003e. This file should be protected\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-out server.csr\u003c/code\u003e: The name of the output file which containes the public shareable, encoded request we will send to the issuing server.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-config san.cnf\u003c/code\u003e: The name of the file which we previosuly saved as the [[#Creating our Certificate Request|request template]]\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 22 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl req -newkey rsa:2048 -nodes -keyout server.key -out server.csr -config san.cnf\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eGenerating a RSA private key\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e............................+++++\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e........................................................+++++\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewriting new private key to \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;server.pem\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e-----\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eYou are about to be asked to enter information that will be incorporated\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003einto your certificate request.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eWhat you are about to enter is what is called a Distinguished Name or a DN.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eThere are quite a few fields but you can leave some blank\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eFor some fields there will be a default value,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eIf you enter \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;.\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e, the field will be left blank.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e-----\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eCountry Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e letter code\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eAU\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e:ie\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eState or Province Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003efull name\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eSome-State\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e:Mayo\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eLocality Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eeg, city\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e:Ballina\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eOrganization Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eeg, company\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eInternet Widgits Pty Ltd\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e:DigiNerve\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eOrganizational Unit Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003eeg, section\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e:IT\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eCommon Name \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003ee.g. server FQDN or YOUR name\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e:radius.diginerve.ie\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eEmail Address \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[]\u003c/span\u003e:support@diginerve.ie\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"validate-the-request-file\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#validate-the-request-file\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Validate the Request File'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Validate the Request File\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eBefore we take the Certificate to the PKI server to issue the certificate for the server, we can double check the request to ensure that the SAN is included as per the Template.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl x509 -in server.crt -text -noout\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis command will read in the new certificate request file, and dump its content in a readable text format so we can validate the request is correct.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"present-the-certificate-request-to-windows-pki\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Present the Certificate Request to Windows PKI\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith our Certificate Request file (\u003ccode\u003e.csr\u003c/code\u003e) now created, we will proceed to submit the request to the PKI Infrastructure which we will be requesting to issue us the certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"windows-pki-infrastructure\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#windows-pki-infrastructure\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Windows PKI Infrastructure'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Windows PKI Infrastructure\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThis portion of the Article focuses on using a Windows PKI deployed to provide a Private Key Infrastructure within an Organisation to process the request and issue the certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eAs this article is focusing on the use of a Private Enterprise Certificate to authenticate a trusted computer access the organisations WiFi or VPN environment, we will concentrate on working with this technology to process and issue a certificate fit for purpose from the organisations infrastructure.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore we begin, we do need to have a copy of the certicate request we created,  \u003ccode\u003eserver.csr\u003c/code\u003e transferred to the system we will be operating on to process the request.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"check-the-windows-pki-server-templates\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#check-the-windows-pki-server-templates\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Check the Windows PKI Server Templates'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Check the Windows PKI Server Templates\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eDespite the fact that we created a template earlier for our certicicate to indicate that we going to concentrate on a \u003cem\u003eComputer\u003c/em\u003e certificate, the Windows PKI environment premits the System Adminstrators to name the templates which it will issue certificates using to match the organisations governance standard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore, before we present the certificate to the Issuing server to process our request, we should first ask the Issuing Server what are the templates which it is willing to allow us to request, and what name has been associated with the various templates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eWindows PKI services follow an RBAC architecture, in which the templates that are offered will depend on the context of the request, for example its quite common to find that users are not premitted to request machine or computer certificates. These will typically be resticted to a computer or service identity.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eUsers looking to issue a computer or machine certificate, typically are using the certicicates to protect a web site using HTTPS for transport, therefore, it is common that the only suitable template that we can choose maybe a \u003cem\u003eweb server\u003c/em\u003e or \u003cem\u003eserver\u003c/em\u003e template, from the list offered by the Issuing CA\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertutil\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CATemplates\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eIPSECIntermediateOffline\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eIPSec\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOffline\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAuto-Enroll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccess\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edenied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCEPEncryption\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCEP\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEncryption\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAuto-Enroll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccess\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edenied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnrollmentAgentOffline\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eExchange\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnrollment\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAgent\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOffline\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequest\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAuto-Enroll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccess\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edenied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAdministrator\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAdministrator\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAuto-Enroll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccess\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edenied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eWebServer\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eWeb\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eServer\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAuto-Enroll\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccess\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eis\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edenied\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCertUtil\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CATemplates\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecommand\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecompleted\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003esuccessfully\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"requesting-the-certificate\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#requesting-the-certificate\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Requesting the Certificate'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Requesting the Certificate\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eFrom the list of offered Certificate templates, we are technially looking tof the template which include\u0026rsquo;s the \u003cstrong\u003eServer Authentication\u003c/strong\u003e OID.\nFor systems which do not include templates with the \u003cstrong\u003eServer Authentication\u003c/strong\u003e OID in the available list, refer to the topic [[#Optional - Manually Adding the OID to the Certificate Request|Manually adding the Server Authentication OID]]\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn this context I will use \u003cstrong\u003e\u0026lsquo;Web Server\u0026rsquo;\u003c/strong\u003e in the request the certificate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertreq\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eexe\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-attrib\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;CertificateTemplate:Web Server\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecsr\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA window will popup asking you to select the Certificate Authority (CA) where your request is to be submitted to, typically any of the presented servers will work fine, as long as they are approved to issue certificates based on the selected template. If the selected Certificate Authority has a problem with processing the request, try selecting an alternative, or checking within the organisation PKI support team to identify the correct server to utilize.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a sucessful presentation, the \u003ccode\u003ecertreq\u003c/code\u003e tool will present a dialog asking for where to save the new certificate. Provide a filename (for this simple example, Ill just call it \u003ccode\u003eserver\u003c/code\u003e) and complete the wizard.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt this point we now have our issued certificate with ONLY its public key, stored in a file called \u003ccode\u003eserver.cer\u003c/code\u003e which we will next need to transfer back to the system we orginally created the request on.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe Certificate we just received from the PKI server only contains the Public Key, the matching Private Key (the main secret for decrypting) is stored on the machine we created the request from initially, which in this article was called \u003ccode\u003eserver.key\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eCopy the public key certificate file, \u0026lsquo;server\u0026rsquo; back to the machine we created the request on, in this case, it was our FreeRadius server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"optional---manually-adding-the-oid-to-the-certificate-request\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#optional---manually-adding-the-oid-to-the-certificate-request\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Optional - Manually Adding the OID to the Certificate Request'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Optional - Manually Adding the OID to the Certificate Request\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThis following step is only relevant if the issueing server, will not offer a template which includes the property for Server Authentication\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eWhen generating certificates for use by \u003cstrong\u003eFreeRadius EAP-TLS\u003c/strong\u003e, This has two requirements so that the service will successfully validate the certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInclude the \u0026ldquo;Server Authentication\u0026rdquo; (OID 1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInclude a Subject Alternate Name\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e802.1x\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen a client uses PEAP-EAP-MS-Challenge Handshake Authentication Protocol (CHAP) version 2 authentication, PEAP with EAP-TLS authentication, or EAP-TLS authentication, Microsoft specifies that certificates must have the \u0026ldquo;Enhanced Key Usage\u0026rdquo; attribute with the value \u0026ldquo;Server Authentication\u0026rdquo; (OID 1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1). [Ref.: http://support.microsoft.com/kb/814394/en-us ]\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf these extension are not present in your FreeRadius certificate, the auth process will fail, because the client will stop communicating with your server due that it can\u0026rsquo;t validate your cert.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince the certificate request generated in openssl according to the procedure above does not provide this attribute, it is necessary to add it to the pending request with the Windows CLI command \u003ccode\u003ecertutil\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe general syntax is \u003ccode\u003ecertutil -setextension RequestID ExtensionOID Flags @InFile\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe \u003cem\u003eRequestID\u003c/em\u003e is the sequence ID for our requested certificate from the issueing Certificate Authority\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe \u003cem\u003eExtensionOID\u003c/em\u003e for the attribute \u0026ldquo;Enhanced Key Usage\u0026rdquo; is \u003cstrong\u003e2.5.29.37\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe \u003cem\u003eflags\u003c/em\u003e value is set to \u003cem\u003e0\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFor the \u003cem\u003e@InFile\u003c/em\u003e, we will create an input text file \u003ccode\u003eeku.txt\u003c/code\u003e as follows\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e30\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e0a\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e06\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e08\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e2b\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e06\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e01\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e05\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e05\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e07\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e03\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e01\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eeku\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etxt\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, with all the information required, we can run the following command, Remember to replace \u003ccode\u003e[RequestID]\u003c/code\u003e with the actual numeric request ID\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ecertutil\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-setextension\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"no\"\u003eRequestID\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e2.5\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003e29\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003e37\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e@eku\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etxt\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce the command has completed, launch the Windows  Certification Authority application\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen \u003cstrong\u003ePending request\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRight click on the request we just modified (RequestID)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect \u003cstrong\u003eAll tasks\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026ndash;\u0026gt;  \u003cstrong\u003eIssue\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGo to \u003cstrong\u003eIssued certificates\u003c/strong\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLocate and double-click on the one you just issued \u003cem\u003e[RequestID]\u003c/em\u003e.\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA window will open displaying cert\u0026rsquo;s info.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGo to the tab \u003cstrong\u003eDetails\u003c/strong\u003e and check that the field \u003cstrong\u003eEnhanced Key Usage\u003c/strong\u003e is present and its value is \u003cstrong\u003eServer Authentication (1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1)\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eClick on the button \u003cstrong\u003eCopy to file\u0026hellip;\u003c/strong\u003e and save it as either DER encoded or Base-64 encoded\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProvide a filename (let\u0026rsquo;s call it \u003ccode\u003eserver\u003c/code\u003e) and finish the wizard.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThis will give you a file \u003ccode\u003eserver.cer\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCopy the public key certificate file, \u0026lsquo;server\u0026rsquo; back to the machine we created the request on, in this case, it was our FreeRadius server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"verify-the-servers-certificate\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Verify the Servers Certificate\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBack on our Linux node, with a copy of our new certificate on hand \u003ccode\u003eserver.cer\u003c/code\u003e, we can now check that the certificate matches all the requirements we outlined at the beginning of this process\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInclude the Servers \u003cstrong\u003eCommon name\u003c/strong\u003e, eg \u003ccode\u003eradius.diginerve.ie\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInclude the \u003cstrong\u003eServer Authentication\u003c/strong\u003e (OID 1.3.6.1.5.5.7.3.1)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInclude a \u003cstrong\u003eSubject Alternate Name\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eFreeRaidus expects that the public certificates be placed in the folder \u003ccode\u003e/etc/freeradius/certs\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eUsing OpenSSL can view the certificate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 50 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eroot@p-nps-radius01:/etc/freeradius/certs# openssl x509 -in server.pem -text -noout\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eCertificate:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Data:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Version: \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e0x2\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Serial Number:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            51:~~~~:33\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Signature Algorithm: sha256WithRSAEncryption\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Issuer: \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e IE, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e diginerve, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e ie, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eCN\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e MY Domain CA Issuer\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Validity\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            Not Before: Apr  \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e7\u003c/span\u003e 11:34:18 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2021\u003c/span\u003e GMT\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            Not After : Feb  \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e 12:16:46 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2022\u003c/span\u003e GMT\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Subject: \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eC\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e IE, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eST\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e Mayo, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eL\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e Ballina, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eO\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e MIS, \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eCN\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e radius.diginerve.ie\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        Subject Public Key Info:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            Public Key Algorithm: rsaEncryption\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                RSA Public-Key: \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2048\u003c/span\u003e bit\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                Modulus:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                    00:d0:6d:0d:14:5b:01:a9:4a:8a:ec:51:84:5b:6c:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                    53:87:86:a5:47:f0:81:e6:85:06:c6:96:10:ed:68:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                    31:9d\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                Exponent: \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e65537\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e0x10001\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        X509v3 extensions:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 Subject Alternative Name: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                DNS:radius.diginerve.ie\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 Subject Key Identifier: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                43:35:46:D4:ED:00:89:83:F2:73:B5:6B:51:15:BB:B6:AE:7D:49:8E\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 Authority Key Identifier: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                keyid:0C:21:7E:6B:1D:D6:93:BB:17:7A:55:53:88:CD:5F:5F:64:A3:83:0E\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 CRL Distribution Points: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                Full Name:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                  URI:ldap:///CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eMy%20Issuer,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ep-ie1ca-ca01,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eCDP,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ePublic%20Key%20Services,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eServices,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eConfiguration,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003epki,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ediginerve,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eie?certificateRevocationList?base?objectClass\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ecRLDistributionPoint\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            Authority Information Access: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                CA Issuers - URI:ldap:///CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eMy%20Issuer,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eAIA,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ePublic%20Key%20Services,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eServices,CN\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eConfiguration,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003epki,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ediginerve,DC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eie?cACertificate?base?objectClass\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ecertificationAuthority\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 Key Usage: critical\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                Digital Signature, Key Encipherment\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            1.3.6.1.4.1.311.21.7: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                0..\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e+.....7.....j...#...........,\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e...?......d...\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            X509v3 Extended Key Usage: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                TLS Web Server Authentication\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            1.3.6.1.4.1.311.21.10: \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                0.0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e..+.......\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    Signature Algorithm: sha256WithRSAEncryption\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e         ab:7f:d6:12:80:f7:fe:d6:d9:44:f8:1a:fc:fb:91:2d:eb:05:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e         b1:f2:ae:a5\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSearch for the following to be present and correct\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSubject:\u003c/strong\u003e and check it,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNext, Locate the \u003cstrong\u003eX509v3 Subject Alternative Name:\u003c/strong\u003e and ensure it exists and is correct,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFinally, \u003cstrong\u003eX509v3 Extended Key Usage\u003c/strong\u003e should contain \u003cem\u003eTLS Web Server Authentication  1.3.6.1.4.1.311.21.10\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"freeradius-compatability\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#freeradius-compatability\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'FreeRadius Compatability'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    FreeRadius Compatability\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eFreeRadius does not work with \u003cstrong\u003eDER Encoded Certificates\u003c/strong\u003e, these must be instead in \u003cstrong\u003eBase64\u003c/strong\u003e format to function\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eIf necessary, we may have to convert our certifcate from \u003cstrong\u003eDER Encoding\u003c/strong\u003e to \u003cstrong\u003eBase64 Encoding\u003c/strong\u003e. This can be completed using the \u003ccode\u003eopenssl\u003c/code\u003e tool with the following syntax:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-b85b8c6df476da7d4782474178080c9c-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl x509 -inform DER -in server.cer -outform PEM -out server.pem\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Build and Install the Latest OpenSSL on Ubuntu",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-02T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-02T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/build-and-install-the-latest-openssl-on-ubuntu/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/build-and-install-the-latest-openssl-on-ubuntu/",
        "summary": " Installing the Latest OpenSSL release on Ubuntu Being over 25 years old, OpenSSL can be found on just about any system you work with today; but this does not imply that the version installed is current (or even close).\nDuring its life, there have been many instances where OpenSSL has been in the news, where some new vulnerability has being discovered, and quickly after, patched.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"installing-the-latest-openssl-release-on-ubuntu\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#installing-the-latest-openssl-release-on-ubuntu\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Installing the Latest OpenSSL release on Ubuntu'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"installing-the-latest-openssl-release-on-ubuntu\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Installing the Latest OpenSSL release on Ubuntu\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBeing over 25 years old, OpenSSL can be found on just about any system you work with today; but this does not imply that the version installed is current (or even close).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDuring its life, there have been many instances where OpenSSL has been in the news, where some new vulnerability has being discovered, and quickly after, patched.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Swiss Army Knive of SSL Certificate\u0026rsquo;s, this is a tool that everyone should have at least used once in their administrative duties.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo check if OpenSSL is on your system, and more importantly, the version installed, we can use the following simple command.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl version\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn my case “OpenSSL 1.1.1 ” was the result.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"installing-the-current-release\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Installing the Current Release\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe will go directly to the \u003ca href=\"https://openssl.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eOpenSSL\u003c/a\u003e distribution source, and download the current stable version, which at the time of writing is now \u003cstrong\u003eopenssl-1.1.1k\u003c/strong\u003e  and save it into \u003ccode\u003e~/Downloads\u003c/code\u003e directory:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ~/Downloads\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewget https://www.openssl.org/source/openssl-1.1.1k.tar.gz\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"create-working-folder\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#create-working-folder\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Create Working Folder'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Create Working Folder\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe will install the new version at \u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl\u003c/code\u003e. To do that we need to create and change directory\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mkdir /opt/openssl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /opt/openssl\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExtract the downloaded compressed file into this directory:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo tar xfzv ~/Downloads/openssl-1.1.1k.tar.gz --directory /opt/openssl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /opt/openssl\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"configure-the-build\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Configure the Build\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore we proceed to compile the utility, we first must set some of the configuration settings, which will be used to let OpenSSL know where it is to be installed, and what folder it can use for its working space.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe is quite trivial, as we use the provide \u003ccode\u003econfig\u003c/code\u003e script and pass in the parameters required. We are running this with \u003cem\u003esudo\u003c/em\u003e to ensure the script can check the system for dependencies and create any folders necessary.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe folders I will be using for the installation include\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl\u003c/code\u003e as the home directory and\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl/ssl\u003c/code\u003e as the directory where OpenSSL will store certificates and private keys.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ./config --prefix\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/opt/openssl --openssldir\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/opt/openssl/ssl \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"building-and-installing-openssl\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Building and Installing OpenSSL\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the configuration complete, we now can use the \u003cem\u003eMakefile\u003c/em\u003e which has just being customized, to build, and then install the new version of OpenSSL. Depending on the speed of your system this can take some time to complete.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo make \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo make install\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCongratulations, OpenSSL current version is installed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"multiple-instances\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Multiple Instances\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWait - we do have a small issue. Right now there are two installations of OpenSSL on your system:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe original installation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eand this New Current release we built from source.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"swapping-the-binaries\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Swapping the Binaries\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI won’t delete the original version, instead I will simply rename it to \u003cem\u003eopenssl.old\u003c/em\u003e, keeping this in the original installation path location.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mv /usr/bin/openssl /usr/bin/openssl.old \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eIn the literature there are references to applications that expect openssl to be at the original directory. To maintain compatibility, and avoiding the need to alter the environment variable PATH, we will create a symbolic link \u003ccode\u003e/usr/bin/openssl\u003c/code\u003e pointing to \u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl/bin/openssl\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eWe simply link the new build to the original folder, as follows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ln -s /opt/openssl/bin/openssl /usr/bin/openssl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003els -lisah /usr/bin/openssl\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003els\u003c/code\u003e command above, just offers up a view to ensure that the symbolic link was established from the original path to our new installation.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"setting-the-module-library\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Setting the Module Library\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eOpenSSL is a dependency for a lot of different applications, therefore we should complete the installation, by updating the module library configuration to ensure any application we deploy will find and use this release.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eModify the module loader configuration in \u003ccode\u003e/etc/ld.so.conf.d/openssl.conf\u003c/code\u003e, open the file and edit it using \u003ccode\u003evi /etc/ld.so.conf.d/openssl.conf\u003c/code\u003e so that it reads as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003e/opt/openssl/lib\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, reload the modules\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ldconfig \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"sanity-check\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#sanity-check\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Sanity Check'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Sanity Check\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAnd finally, we can verify that everything is correct\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewhich openssl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl version\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eopenssl\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"clean-up\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Clean up\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReboot your system to make things permanent and execute the last three commands again, targeting, obviously, the same outcome.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBy now you have OpenSSL new version installed and working correctly. But if you try to download any of the previous files, for instance \u003ccode\u003eopenssl-1.1.1k.tar.gz\u003c/code\u003e, you will get the following error:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eerror\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eThe Certificate Authority “Let’s Encrypt Authority X3” that issued the server certificate is not in OpenSSL certificate and private key directory */opt/openssl/ssl*.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is the desired behavior skip what follows and you have \u003cstrong\u003eOpenSSL 1.1.1k\u003c/strong\u003e completely installed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is not your desired behavior, you can copy all certificates in \u003ccode\u003e/etc/ssl/certs/\u003c/code\u003e to \u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl/ssl/certs\u003c/code\u003e. However I prefer a slightly different approach, simply linking by making \u003ccode\u003e/opt/openssl/ssl/certs\u003c/code\u003e a symbolic link pointing \u003ccode\u003e/etc/ssl/certs/\u003c/code\u003e files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo Implement the preferred approach, issue the following command\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-df2de6085883cf830603af35ac8ec8f2-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo ln -s /etc/ssl/certs/. /opt/openssl/ssl/certs/\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Install FreeRADIUS on Ubuntu from the Network RADIUS Repository",
        "date_published" : "2021-03-01T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-03-01T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/install-freeradius-on-ubuntu-from-the-network-radius-repository/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/install-freeradius-on-ubuntu-from-the-network-radius-repository/",
        "summary": " FreeRADIUS Getting Started FreeRADIUS is an open source, high-performance, modular, scalable and feature-rich RADIUS server. It ships with both server and radius client, development libraries and numerous additional RADIUS related utilities, for Linux\nFreeRADIUS supports request proxying, with fail-over and load balancing, as well as the ability to access many types of back-end databases.\nRADIUS, which stands for Remote Authentication Dial-In User Service, is a network protocol used for remote user authentication and accounting. It provides AAA services; namely Authorization, Authentication, and Accounting.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"freeradius-getting-started\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#freeradius-getting-started\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'FreeRADIUS Getting Started'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"freeradius-getting-started\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  FreeRADIUS Getting Started\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFreeRADIUS is an open source, high-performance, modular, scalable and feature-rich RADIUS server. It ships with both server and radius client, development libraries and numerous additional RADIUS related utilities, for Linux\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFreeRADIUS supports request proxying, with fail-over and load balancing, as well as the ability to access many types of back-end databases.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRADIUS, which stands for \u003cem\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eR\u003c/strong\u003eemote \u003cstrong\u003eA\u003c/strong\u003euthentication \u003cstrong\u003eD\u003c/strong\u003eial-\u003cstrong\u003eI\u003c/strong\u003en \u003cstrong\u003eU\u003c/strong\u003eser \u003cstrong\u003eS\u003c/strong\u003eervice\u003c/em\u003e, is a network protocol used for remote user authentication and accounting. It provides AAA services; namely \u003cstrong\u003eA\u003c/strong\u003euthorization, \u003cstrong\u003eA\u003c/strong\u003euthentication, and \u003cstrong\u003eA\u003c/strong\u003eccounting.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"freeradius\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  FreeRadius\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe Article is authored using \u003cstrong\u003eUbuntu 18.04\u003c/strong\u003e as the target distribution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eYou can view versions of FreeRadius available in your distribution:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$ sudo apt policy freeradius\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003efreeradius:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  Installed: \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003enone\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  Candidate: 3.0.16+dfsg-1ubuntu3.1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  Version table:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e *** 3.0.16+dfsg-1ubuntu3.1 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e500\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e500\u003c/span\u003e http://azure.archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu bionic-updates/main amd64 Packages\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e500\u003c/span\u003e http://security.ubuntu.com/ubuntu bionic-security/main amd64 Packages\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e100\u003c/span\u003e /var/lib/dpkg/status\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e     3.0.16+dfsg-1ubuntu3 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e500\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e500\u003c/span\u003e http://azure.archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu bionic/main amd64 Packages\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstall FreeRadius packages from official Ubuntu APT repository with the commands below:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt -y install freeradius freeradius-mysql freeradius-utils\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAmong the packages installed, we have the \u003cstrong\u003efreeradius mysql module\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003efreeradius utilities\u003c/strong\u003e packages.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"freeradius-network-radius-repositories\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  FreeRadius \u0026lsquo;Network Radius\u0026rsquo; Repositories\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe official distributions for FreeRadius are published by \u003cstrong\u003eNetwork Radius\u003c/strong\u003e, and typically are fresher than the builds included with the stock Linux Distribution\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eHowever, the \u003cstrong\u003eUbuntu 18.04\u003c/strong\u003e version of \u003cstrong\u003eFreeRadius\u003c/strong\u003e is \u003cem\u003e3.016\u003c/em\u003e, and has some issues which will essentially block our progress. We can use the official packages to deploy the current release of the service, at the time of writing this is \u003cem\u003e3.0.23\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRead more here: \u003ca href=\"https://networkradius.com/packages/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://networkradius.com/packages/\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"add-the-network-radius-repository\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#add-the-network-radius-repository\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Add the Network Radius Repository'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Add the \u003cstrong\u003eNetwork Radius\u003c/strong\u003e Repository\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAdd the following line to your apt source list \u003ccode\u003e/etc/apt/sources.list\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor \u003cstrong\u003eUbuntu Bionic 18.04\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;deb http://packages.networkradius.com/releases/ubuntu-bionic bionic main\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/networkradius.list \u0026gt; /dev/null\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor \u003cstrong\u003eUbuntu Focal 20.04\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;deb http://packages.networkradius.com/releases/ubuntu-focal focal main\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/networkradius.list \u0026gt; /dev/null\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"trust-the-repository\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#trust-the-repository\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Trust the Repository'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Trust the Repository\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we need to trust this new repository, and then update the applications database, before we finally upgrade FreeRadius\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecurl -s \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;https://packages.networkradius.com/pgp/packages%40networkradius.com\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e sudo tee /etc/apt/trusted.gpg.d/packages.networkradius.com.asc \u0026gt; /dev/null\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get update\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"install-freeradius-from-network-radius-repository\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#install-freeradius-from-network-radius-repository\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Install FreeRadius from Network Radius Repository'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Install FreeRadius from \u003cstrong\u003eNetwork Radius\u003c/strong\u003e Repository\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we should be ready to Install FreeRadius packages from official Network Radius APT repository with the commands below:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f8b4864ccb49ab567f3efebfe247396c-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt -y install freeradius freeradius-mysql freeradius-utils\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Streaming Vinyl to Sonos with a Raspberry Pi and Icecast",
        "date_published" : "2021-02-21T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-02-21T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/streaming-vinyl-to-sonos-with-a-raspberry-pi-and-icecast/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/streaming-vinyl-to-sonos-with-a-raspberry-pi-and-icecast/",
        "summary": " Streaming Music from USB Turntable A little known trivia - I was once a DJ, and spent a lot of my youth behind the decks, in clubs around the West Of Ireland. Today, I still am the proud owner of a very large collection of Vynil and CD music, which of course deserves to get a second life with my digital streaming audio system powered by Sonos\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"streaming-music-from-usb-turntable\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#streaming-music-from-usb-turntable\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Streaming Music from USB Turntable'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"streaming-music-from-usb-turntable\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Streaming Music from USB Turntable\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA little known trivia - I was once a DJ, and spent a lot of my youth behind the decks, in clubs around the West Of Ireland. Today, I still am the proud owner of a very large collection of Vynil and CD music, which of course deserves to get a second life with my digital streaming audio system powered by Sonos\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"usb-turntable-streamer\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  USB Turntable Streamer\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI own a really nice turntable which is modeled on the Legendary Technical SL1200 MK3, which I am so well aquatinted with, including the awesome Citronix DJ Console which was home to 2 of these beauties in so many clubs way back when\u0026hellip;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy \u003ca href=\"http://amzn.to/2drytFC\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAudio-Technica AT-LP120-USB\u003c/a\u003e device is the focus of todays IoT challange, I will be using a Raspberry PI 3, to stream audio from one of these turntables with USB audio codec output.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf your in the market, these are also workable options for this exercise\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://amzn.to/2dSVrGz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eAudio-Technica AT-LP60-USB\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://amzn.to/2e3piLt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eION Audio Classic LP | 3-Speed USB\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://amzn.to/2dW2Xm7\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eSony PSLX300USB\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"enable-ssh-before-booting\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Enable SSH before booting\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBecause we are going to use the Raspberry Pi headless (without a display) and without keyboard attached, we need a way to control the device. Luckily we can enable SSH by adding an \u003cem\u003eempty file\u003c/em\u003e called \u003ccode\u003essh\u003c/code\u003e to the root of the SD card. This will enable \u003cstrong\u003eSSH\u003c/strong\u003e for us automatically.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you are using the Ethernet port on the Raspberry Pi, networking and SSH should work out of the box with DHCP.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"update-to-current-os\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Update to Current OS\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate your Raspbian install:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get update\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe Rasbian Version used at the time of writing is Buster 2021-02\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"connect-the-usb-turntable-to-the-raspberry-pi\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Connect the USB Turntable to the Raspberry Pi\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, connect the turntable to the Raspberry Pi, using USB. You can use the command \u003ccode\u003earecord -l\u003c/code\u003e to check if your device has been detected. Mine shows this:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epi@raspberrypi:~ $ arecord -l\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e**** List of CAPTURE Hardware Devices ****\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecard 1: CODEC \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eUSB AUDIO  CODEC\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e, device 0: USB Audio \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eUSB Audio\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  Subdevices: 1/1\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  Subdevice \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#0: subdevice #0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMake a note of the card number, \u003cem\u003e1 in my case\u003c/em\u003e. This is probably the same for you, but if it differs, you may need to remember it and change accordingly in the following steps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"fix-volume-issues\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#fix-volume-issues\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Fix volume issues'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Fix volume issues\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAs most USB turntables do not have hardware volume control, and the input volume is stuck on roughly half of what it should be, we need to add a software volume control. Create the file \u003ccode\u003e/etc/asound.conf\u003c/code\u003e and edit it to add the following contents:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 20 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epcm.dmic_hw \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e hw\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    card \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    channels \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    format S16_LE\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epcm.dmic_mm \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e mmap_emul\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    slave.pcm dmic_hw\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003epcm.dmic_sv \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etype\u003c/span\u003e softvol\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    slave.pcm dmic_hw\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    control \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        name \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Boost Capture Volume\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        card \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    min_dB -5.0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    max_dB 20.0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext, run this command to refresh the \u003cstrong\u003ealsa\u003c/strong\u003e state and also show VU Meters to test the input volume:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003earecord -D dmic_sv -r \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e44100\u003c/span\u003e -f S16_LE -c \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e --vumeter\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003estereo /dev/null\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs you might notice, the volume is way too low. You can use \u003ccode\u003ealsamixer\u003c/code\u003e to change the volume. Press \u003ccode\u003eF6\u003c/code\u003e to select the USB Turntable device, and press \u003ccode\u003eTAB\u003c/code\u003e until you see the boost slider.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have it set to \u003cstrong\u003e65\u003c/strong\u003e on my setup, but you might try out. Make sure you are not turning it up too high, or your sound quality might degrade due to clipping.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"streaming-using-icecast2\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Streaming using \u003ccode\u003eicecast2\u003c/code\u003e\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, to stream we will use the \u003ccode\u003eicecast2\u003c/code\u003e package, which of course needs to be deployed to our Pi.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get install icecast2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"configure-icecast2\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configure-icecast2\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Configure icecast2'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Configure icecast2\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNext, we will edit \u003ccode\u003e/etc/icecast2/icecast.xml\u003c/code\u003e, which is the casting servers settings, to provide a name for the stream, and some credential\u0026rsquo;s to protect the stream.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003exml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 63 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;icecast\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;location\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eRecord Room\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/location\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;admin\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eicemaster@localhost\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/admin\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;limits\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;clients\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e100\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/clients\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;sources\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e2\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/sources\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;queue-size\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e524288\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/queue-size\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;client-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e30\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/client-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;header-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e15\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/header-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;source-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e10\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/source-timeout\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;burst-on-connect\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e0\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/burst-on-connect\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;burst-size\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e65535\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/burst-size\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/limits\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;authentication\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;source-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003evynil\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/source-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;relay-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003evynil\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/relay-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e\u0026lt;!-- Admin logs in with the username given below --\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;admin-user\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eadmin\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/admin-user\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;admin-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003evynil\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/admin-password\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/authentication\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;hostname\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003elocalhost\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/hostname\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;listen-socket\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;port\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e80\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/port\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/listen-socket\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;http-headers\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;header\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003ename=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\u0026#34;Access-Control-Allow-Origin\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003evalue=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\u0026#34;*\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e/\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/http-headers\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;fileserve\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e1\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/fileserve\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;paths\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;basedir\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e/usr/share/icecast2\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/basedir\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;logdir\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e/var/log/icecast2\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/logdir\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;webroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e/usr/share/icecast2/web\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/webroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;adminroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e/usr/share/icecast2/admin\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/adminroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;alias\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003esource=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\u0026#34;/\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003edestination=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003e\u0026#34;/status.xsl\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e/\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e\u0026lt;!-- The certificate file needs to contain both public and private part.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e             Both should be PEM encoded.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e        \u0026lt;ssl-certificate\u0026gt;/usr/share/icecast2/icecast.pem\u0026lt;/ssl-certificate\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e        --\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/paths\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;logging\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;accesslog\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eaccess.log\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/accesslog\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;errorlog\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003eerror.log\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/errorlog\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;loglevel\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e3\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/loglevel\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e\u0026lt;!-- 4 Debug, 3 Info, 2 Warn, 1 Error --\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;logsize\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e10000\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/logsize\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"c\"\u003e\u0026lt;!-- Max size of a logfile --\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/logging\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;security\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;chroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e0\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/chroot\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/security\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026lt;/icecast\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"starting-icecast2\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#starting-icecast2\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Starting IceCast2'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Starting IceCast2\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe are going to start the casting server, but we will bing to TCP 80, which requires that we allow this to happen, but following these simple steps.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo setcap \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;cap_net_bind_service=+ep\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003ewhich icecast2\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eupdate-rc.d icecast2 defaults\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esystemctl status icecast2.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"icecast2-admin\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#icecast2-admin\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Icecast2 admin'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Icecast2 admin\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we should have the casting server online, and working, It will be listening at \u003ca href=\"http://pi-ipaddress/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttp:\\\\Pi\u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003e(replacing PI with the IP or name you assigned to the device)\u003c/em\u003e and is good for checking the status of connected clients, authenticate with the account \u003cem\u003eadmin\u003c/em\u003e and password \u003cem\u003evynil\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"darkice\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Darkice\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow we need to link the USB audio source, to our Icecast server, and to make this work, we will use another excellent package called \u003ccode\u003edarkice\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen install a bunch of needed packages:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get -y install darkice\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"configure-darkice\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configure-darkice\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Configure Darkice'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Configure Darkice\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis time, we will update the DarkIce configuration file located at \u003ccode\u003e/etc/darkice.cfg\u003c/code\u003e so that it is aware of where the USB turntable is connected to our system (remember the pointer earlier), and how to connect with our Icecast server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 32 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# this section describes general aspects of the live streaming session\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003egeneral\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eduration\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# duration of encoding, in seconds. 0 means forever\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ebufferSecs\u003c/span\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# size of internal slip buffer, in seconds\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ereconnect\u003c/span\u003e       \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e yes       \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# reconnect to the server(s) if disconnected\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003erealtime\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e yes       \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# run the encoder with POSIX realtime priority\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ertprio\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e3\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# scheduling priority for the realtime threads\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# this section describes the audio input that will be streamed\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003einput\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003edevice\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e hw:1,0    \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# OSS DSP soundcard device for the audio input\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003esampleRate\u003c/span\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e44100\u003c/span\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# other settings have crackling audo, esp. 44100\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ebitsPerSample\u003c/span\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e16\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# bits per sample. try 16\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003echannel\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# channels. 1 = mono, 2 = stereo\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# this section describes a streaming connection to an IceCast2 server\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# there may be up to 8 of these sections, named [icecast2-0] ... [icecast2-7]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# these can be mixed with [icecast-x] and [shoutcast-x] sections\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eicecast2-0\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ebitrateMode\u003c/span\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e cbr\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eformat\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e mp3\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ebitrate\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e320\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eserver\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e localhost\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e80\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003epassword\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e vynil\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003emountPoint\u003c/span\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e listen.mp3\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e Turntable\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003edescription\u003c/span\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e Audio-Technica AT-LP120 Turntable\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eurl\u003c/span\u003e             \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e http://turntable\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003egenre\u003c/span\u003e           \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e vinyl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003epublic\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e no\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003elocalDumpFile\u003c/span\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e recording.m4a\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"darkice-init-script\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#darkice-init-script\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Darkice Init Script'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Darkice Init Script\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOk, we now need to create a simple script which will autostart this darkice service each time the Pi is rebooted, so that we can set and forget about this little IoT solution.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStart by creating a new \u003cem\u003einit.d\u003c/em\u003e file called \u003ccode\u003e/etc/init.d/darkice\u003c/code\u003e and then populating the file with the following script\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 211 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cp\"\u003e#!/bin/sh\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Copyright (c) 2007 Javier Fernandez-Sanguino \u0026lt;jfs@debian.org\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Copyright (c) 2009 Jochen Friedrich \u0026lt;jochen@scram.de\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# This is free software; you may redistribute it and/or modify\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# it under the terms of the GNU General Public License as\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# published by the Free Software Foundation; either version 2,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# or (at your option) any later version.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# This is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE.  See the\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# GNU General Public License for more details.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# You should have received a copy of the GNU General Public License with\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# the Debian operating system, in /usr/share/common-licenses/GPL;  if\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# not, write to the Free Software Foundation, Inc., 59 Temple Place,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Suite 330, Boston, MA 02111-1307 USA\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e### BEGIN INIT INFO\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Provides:          darkice\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Required-Start:    $network $local_fs $remote_fs\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Required-Stop:     $network $local_fs $remote_fs\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Should-Start:\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Should-Stop:\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Default-Start:     2 3 4 5\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Default-Stop:      0 1 6\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Short-Description: Live audio streamer\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Description:       DarkIce is an IceCast, IceCast2 and ShoutCast\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e#                    live audio streamer.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e### END INIT INFO\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ePATH\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eNAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003edarkice\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDAEMON\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/bin/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Live audio streamer\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eLOGDIR\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/var/log\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eUSER\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003enobody\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eGROUP\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003enogroup\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eLOGFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$LOGDIR\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e.log\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ePIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/var/run/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e.pid\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etest\u003c/span\u003e -x \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DAEMON\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e||\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e. /lib/lsb/init-functions\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Default options, these can be overriden by the information\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# at /etc/default/$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDAEMON_OPTS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Additional options given to the server\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDIETIME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e               \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Time to wait for the server to die, in seconds\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# If this value is set too low you might not\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# let some servers to die gracefully and\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e                        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# \u0026#39;restart\u0026#39; will not work\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Include defaults if available\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e -f /etc/default/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t. /etc/default/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Use this if you want the user to explicitly set \u0026#39;RUN\u0026#39; in\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# /etc/default/\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;x\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$RUN\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e !\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;xyes\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e -e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erunning_pid\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Check if a given process pid\u0026#39;s cmdline matches a given name\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003epid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$2\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e -z \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e ! -d /proc/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ecmd\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003ecat /proc/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e/cmdline \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e tr \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\\000\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\\n\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003ehead -n \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003ecut -d : -f 1\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Is this the expected server\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$cmd\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e !\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$name\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erunning\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Check if the process is running looking at /proc\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# (works for all users)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    sleep \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# No pidfile, probably no daemon present\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e ! -f \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003epid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003ecat \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    running_pid \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DAEMON\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e||\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003estart_server\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Start the process using the wrapper\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        start-stop-daemon --start --quiet --make-pidfile --pidfile \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            --background --chuid \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$USER\u003c/span\u003e:\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$GROUP\u003c/span\u003e --no-close \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t    --exec \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DAEMON\u003c/span\u003e -- \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DAEMON_OPTS\u003c/span\u003e \u0026gt;\u0026gt; \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$LOGFILE\u003c/span\u003e 2\u0026gt;\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eerrcode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$errcode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003estop_server\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Stop the process using the wrapper\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        start-stop-daemon --stop --quiet --remove-pidfile --pidfile \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            --exec \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DAEMON\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eerrcode\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$errcode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eforce_stop\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e()\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Force the process to die killing it manually\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e ! -e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ereturn\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ekill\u003c/span\u003e -15 \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Is it really dead?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\tsleep \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DIETIME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003es\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ekill\u003c/span\u003e -9 \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\tsleep \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DIETIME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003es\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\t\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Cannot kill \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e (pid=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$pid\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e)!\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\t\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\trm -f \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$PIDFILE\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ecase\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e in\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  start\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\tlog_daemon_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Starting \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e \u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Check if it\u0026#39;s running first\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_progress_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;apparently already running\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e start_server \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# It\u0026#39;s ok, the server started and is running\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Either we could not start it or it is not running\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# after we did\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# NOTE: Some servers might die some time after they start,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# this code does not try to detect this and might give\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# a false positive (use \u0026#39;status\u0026#39; for that)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  stop\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_daemon_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Stopping \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Only stop the server if we see it running\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            stop_server\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# If it\u0026#39;s not running don\u0026#39;t do anything\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_progress_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;apparently not running\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  force-stop\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# First try to stop gracefully the program\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$0\u003c/span\u003e stop\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# If it\u0026#39;s still running try to kill it more forcefully\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_daemon_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Stopping (force) \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            force_stop\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  restart\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003eforce-reload\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_daemon_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Restarting \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        stop_server\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Wait some sensible amount, some server need this\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e -n \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DIETIME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e sleep \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DIETIME\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        start_server\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        running\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$?\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  status\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_daemon_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Checking status of \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$DESC\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eif\u003c/span\u003e running \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003ethen\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_progress_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;running\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eelse\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_progress_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;apparently not running\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            log_end_msg \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003efi\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  reload\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_warning_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Reloading \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e daemon: not implemented, as the daemon\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        log_warning_msg \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;cannot re-read the config file (use restart).\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  *\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e)\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eN\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/etc/init.d/\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$NAME\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Usage: \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$N\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e {start|stop|force-stop|restart|force-reload|status}\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u0026gt;\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\t\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"k\"\u003eesac\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSave the file!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"autostarting-darkice\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#autostarting-darkice\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Autostarting Darkice'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Autostarting \u003ccode\u003eDarkice\u003c/code\u003e\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAlmost ready, Now, In \u003ccode\u003e/etc/default/darkice\u003c/code\u003e check that you have\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eini\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"na\"\u003eRUN\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s\"\u003eyes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen restart the service\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esystemctl daemon-reload\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd default user nobody to the audio group (in my case, to work with ALSA)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eadduser nobody audio\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFix start sequence so that Darkice is one of the last services to load\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eupdate-rc.d -f darkice remove\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eupdate-rc.d darkice defaults \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e99\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot directly related to the init script, but note that darkice is being run as nobody:nobody. This user can’t set the realtime scheduling priority requests in darkice’s configuration file, so we give the binary that capability:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-8d64cc37010d2e7040d1c4ba5006fd9b-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo setcap \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ecap_sys_nice\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e+ep \u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003ewhich darkice\u003cspan class=\"sb\"\u003e`\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWrap up with a \u003ccode\u003ereboot\u003c/code\u003e, and we should be ready to stream\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"connecting-to-the-stream\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Connecting to the Stream\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe can validate that everything worked as expiected by connect your streaming client to our new stream server, which is waiting for our conenction at the address \u003ccode\u003ehttp://vinyl/listen.mp3\u003c/code\u003e. For this we can use for example VLC or even your favourite browser client.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePut on a record, sit back, and you should now be able to enjoy the tunes from the turntable and soak in all that nostalgia.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"sonos--tunein\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#sonos--tunein\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Sonos / Tunein'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Sonos / Tunein\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOn Sonos, add your streaming turntable URL (http://vinyl/listen.mp3) by Using the Sonos App for iOS or Android:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFrom the \u003cstrong\u003eBrowse\u003c/strong\u003e tab, select \u003cstrong\u003eRadio by TuneIn\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTap \u003cstrong\u003eMy Radio Stations\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTap the t\u003cstrong\u003ehree dots\u003c/strong\u003e in the \u003cem\u003etop right\u003c/em\u003e and tap \u003cstrong\u003eAdd New Radio Station\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnter the \u003cem\u003eStreaming URL\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eStation Name\u003c/em\u003e and tap \u003cstrong\u003eOK\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"pi-musicbox\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#pi-musicbox\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Pi Musicbox'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Pi Musicbox\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOn Pi Musicbox, add the URL to your \u003ccode\u003e/boot/config/radiostations.js\u003c/code\u003e file or use the GUI.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"acknowledgements\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Acknowledgements\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eData in this post is a collection from 3 sources, and combined into a single unified flow, tested on a Pi3, running Buster 2021-02\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://mykter.com/2019/02/02/streaming-vinyl-raspberry-pi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://mykter.com/2019/02/02/streaming-vinyl-raspberry-pi\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/basdp/USB-Turntables-to-Sonos-with-RPi\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://github.com/basdp/USB-Turntables-to-Sonos-with-RPi\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://github.com/coreyk/darkice-libaacplus-rpi-guide/blob/master/README.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://github.com/coreyk/darkice-libaacplus-rpi-guide/blob/master/README.md\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Tags as ARM Template Parameters",
        "date_published" : "2021-01-17T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2021-01-17T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/",
        "summary": " Azure as a State Machine, dogfooding Tags In the post, I am going to introduce a concept which will allow you to greatly up your Infrastructure as Code game, by using Azure as a State Machine!\nOne of the typical challenges when deploying ARM templates, is the sheer number of parameters which we find as a requirement to complete a deployment; which as you will appreciate gets considerably harder as we target many environments.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azure-as-a-state-machine-dogfooding-tags\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-as-a-state-machine-dogfooding-tags\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure as a State Machine, dogfooding Tags'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-as-a-state-machine-dogfooding-tags\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure as a State Machine, dogfooding Tags\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the post, I am going to introduce a concept which will allow you to greatly up your Infrastructure as Code game, by using Azure as a State Machine!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of the typical challenges when deploying ARM templates, is the sheer number of parameters which we find as a requirement to complete a deployment; which as you will appreciate gets considerably harder as we target many environments.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are a number of methods to address this, including the use of Parameter files or Continuous deployment variables; each with their own challenges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"putting-tags-to-work\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Putting Tags to Work\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTags can be applied at both the level of the subscription and resources.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the purpose of this post we will use a scenario of the recovery vault. At the subscription level, we will apply 2 tags to identity the vault we will target for the resources, and then on the actual resource we will add a tag to identity the recovery policy we wish to be applied.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eresource\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003etag\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003evalue\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003esubscription\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003erecoveryVault\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ep-vault-001\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003esubscription\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003erecoveryVaultRG\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ep-vault\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eresource\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003erecoveryPolicy\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eDefaultPolicy\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"subscription-level-tags\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#subscription-level-tags\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Subscription Level Tags'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Subscription Level Tags\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWith these Tags applied, we will have something similar to the following at the subscription level:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/iac-state-azure_tags_2021-07-27-12-38-12.png\" alt=\"Subscription Tags\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn my lab the subscription is \u003ccode\u003e/subscriptions/547d54ea-411b-459e-b6f8-b3cc5e84c535\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"resource-tags\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#resource-tags\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Resource Tags'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Resource Tags\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAnd the VM called \u003cstrong\u003ep-vm001\u003c/strong\u003e, which will represent the resource which we are going to monitor the tag on in my lab will be in the same subscription (for permissions to be simplified), hosted in a resource group called \u003cstrong\u003ep-vm\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe full resource ID of this VM in the lab is \u003ccode\u003e/subscriptions/547d54ea-411b-459e-b6f8-b3cc5e84c535/resourceGroups/p-vm/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/p-vm001\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/iac-state-azure_tags_2021-07-27-12-43-35.png\" alt=\"VM with its Tags\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-resource-manager-magic\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure Resource Manager Magic\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we have all the parts of this environment in place, we will create an ARM template, which simply looks up the values of these tags for us, and to illustrate how it works, it will return the values as outputs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the \u003cstrong\u003eCustom Template Deployment\u003c/strong\u003e in Azure Portal, paste the sample template below\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 43 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;$schema\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;contentVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;parameters\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;sourceResourceId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;String\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/subscriptions/547d54ea-411b-459e-b6f8-b3cc5e84c535/resourceGroups/p-vm/providers/Microsoft.Compute/virtualMachines/p-vm001\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;The resource ID of the resource we wish to look up a tag from.\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(\u0026#39;/subscriptions/\u0026#39;, subscription().subscriptionId, \u0026#39;/providers/Microsoft.Resources/tags/default\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceResourceTagsResourceId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(parameters(\u0026#39;sourceResourceId\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;/providers/Microsoft.Resources/tags/default\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceTagsApi\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;2020-06-01\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resources\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;outputs\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;recoveryVaultId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;String\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceId(subscription().subscriptionId,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVaultRG ,\u0026#39;Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults\u0026#39;,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVault) ]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;recoveryPolicyId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat( resourceId(subscription().subscriptionId,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVaultRG ,\u0026#39;Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults\u0026#39;,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVault), \u0026#39;/backupPolicies/\u0026#39;, reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceResourceTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryPolicy )]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;subscriptionRecoveryVaultRGTag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVaultRG]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;subscriptionRecoveryVaultTag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVault]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resourceRecoveryPolicyTag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;String\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceResourceTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryPolicy]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext, Check your going to deploy to the lab environment subscription, and resource group where we have the test VM which we will check the tag on\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/iac-state-azure_tags_2021-07-27-12-52-12.png\" alt=\"Project Details in Custom Deployment\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eClick on the \u003cstrong\u003eReview and Create\u003c/strong\u003e Button, allow the validation to complete, and then click again on \u003cstrong\u003eCreate\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs this is simply a reference deployment, it will complete instantly, so next we can check the output from the deployment\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-tags-as-arm-template-parameters/iac-state-azure_tags_2021-07-27-12-54-16.png\" alt=\"Template Output\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we should see all the tag values which we set in the lab!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"behind-the-scenes---explain-the-template\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Behind the Scenes - Explain the Template\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, How?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe following ARM JSON uses the \u003ccode\u003ereference\u003c/code\u003e function to lookup the data we care about\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe establish to variables which we use to point at both the tags provider for the current subscription \u003ccode\u003ereferenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u003c/code\u003e and also, the Resource ID of the lab VM \u003ccode\u003ereferenceResourceTagsResourceId\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe also will need a provider API version, while looking up the values of these tags, so we also can use a variable \u003ccode\u003ereferenceTagsApi\u003c/code\u003e to store this.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(\u0026#39;/subscriptions/\u0026#39;, subscription().subscriptionId, \u0026#39;/providers/Microsoft.Resources/tags/default\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceResourceTagsResourceId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(parameters(\u0026#39;sourceResourceId\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;/providers/Microsoft.Resources/tags/default\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;referenceTagsApi\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;2020-06-01\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"subscription-tags\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#subscription-tags\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Subscription Tags'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Subscription Tags\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, the magic. In the outputs, we simply reference the resource ID of the Tag provider for the subscription, with its API version, naming the tag as the last parameter, for example \u003ccode\u003erecoveryVaultRG\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[reference(variables('referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId'), variables('referenceTagsApi')).tags.recoveryVaultRG]\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe do exactly the same for the subscription Recovery Vault tag called \u003ccode\u003erecoveryVault\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[reference(variables('referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId'), variables('referenceTagsApi')).tags.recoveryVault]\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"resource-tags-1\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#resource-tags-1\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Resource tags'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Resource tags\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIn a very similar manner we can reference the tags on the resource, returning the \u003ccode\u003erecoveryPolicy\u003c/code\u003e tag value\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[reference(variables('referenceResourceTagsResourceId'), variables('referenceTagsApi')).tags.recoveryPolicy]\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"getting-creative\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#getting-creative\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Getting Creative'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Getting Creative\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, with some concatenation, we can now build resource identifiers dynamically so that we an combine the values of the tags to reference recovery vaults, and recovery policies\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 8 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-893fbb68e5b424f75a665fd92d61f3fd-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;recoveryVaultId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;String\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceId(subscription().subscriptionId,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVaultRG ,\u0026#39;Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults\u0026#39;,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVault) ]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;recoveryPolicyId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat( resourceId(subscription().subscriptionId,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVaultRG ,\u0026#39;Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults\u0026#39;,  reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceSubscriptionTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryVault), \u0026#39;/backupPolicies/\u0026#39;, reference(variables(\u0026#39;referenceResourceTagsResourceId\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;referenceTagsApi\u0026#39;)).tags.recoveryPolicy )]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn this case our lab produced the following references\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eOutput Key\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eOutput value\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003erecoverVaultId\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e/subscriptions/547d54ea-411b-459e-b6f8-b3cc5e84c535/resourceGroups/p-vault/providers/Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults/p-vault-001\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003erecoveryPolicyId\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e/subscriptions/547d54ea-411b-459e-b6f8-b3cc5e84c535/resourceGroups/p-vault/providers/Microsoft.RecoveryServices/vaults/p-vault-001/backupPolicies/DefaultPolicy\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow - we have the ability to leverage Azure as a stateful configuration database!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Enterprise Agreement: Delegating Roles for Subscription Creation",
        "date_published" : "2020-04-24T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2020-04-24T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/",
        "summary": " Azure Enterprise Agreement, Privilages Delegating Under the Enterprise agreement we have some different Persona\u0026rsquo;s, which have quite different abilities and operations upon which they are permitted to preform.\nBilling account simplifies billing for your organization while providing you enhanced billing and cost management capabilities. The following diagram explains how billing is organized in the new billing account.\nhttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/mca-setup-account\nRoles and Accounts Before we being the process of delegation, It is important to understand this Hierarchy, so we can correctly proceed with the technical work ahead.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azure-enterprise-agreement-privilages-delegating\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-enterprise-agreement-privilages-delegating\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure Enterprise Agreement, Privilages Delegating'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-enterprise-agreement-privilages-delegating\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure Enterprise Agreement, Privilages Delegating\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnder the Enterprise agreement we have some different Persona\u0026rsquo;s, which have quite different abilities and operations upon which they are permitted to preform.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBilling account simplifies billing for your organization while providing you enhanced billing and cost management capabilities. The following diagram explains how billing is organized in the new billing account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/mca-setup-account\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/mca-setup-account\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/az-billing-ea_privilege_delegation.new_structure.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"roles-and-accounts\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Roles and Accounts\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore we being the process of delegation, It is important to understand this Hierarchy, so we can correctly proceed with the technical work ahead.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"enterprise-administrator\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#enterprise-administrator\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Enterprise Administrator'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Enterprise Administrator\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHas the ability to add additional Enterprise and Department Administrators, Additional this persona can\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd Departments\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd or Associate Accounts to and Enrollment\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCan view usage and charges across ALL Accounts and Subscriptions\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCan view the monetary commitment balance associated to the Enrollment\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere is no limit on the number of Enterprise Administrators that can be associated with an Enrollment, and additionally a notification contact can be assigned to receive all email notifications issued.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"department-administrator\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#department-administrator\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Department Administrator'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Department Administrator\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe Department Administrator has ability to do the following:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate Department Administrator (Department focus – click on add administrator)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView/Edit Department properties such as name or Cost Center (Department focus – click on edit pen icon)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a new Account Owner on the Department they administer (Switch to Account focus – click on add account)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRemove the associated Accounts from the Department they administer (In Account focus – hover over account and then select the x icon to delete)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDownload usage details of the Department they administer (Switch to Reports panel on left – Select Download Usage focus)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView the monthly Usage and Charges associated to their Department if Enterprise Administrator has granted permission to do so. (Switch to Reports panel on left –Select Usage Summary focus)\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnable the Account owners to create Non Production Subscriptions\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSubscription Offer MS-AZR-0148P for Dev/Test\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSubscription Offer MS-AZR-0017P for Production\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"account-owners\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#account-owners\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Account Owners'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Account Owners\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe Account Owner can add Subscriptions to their Accounts. Additionally they have the ability to\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUpdate the Service Administrator for a Subscription\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eView Usage Data for their Account\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIf enabled by the Enterprise Administrator, can also view Account Charges\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnumerate existing subscriptions in their account\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate new subscriptions within the scope of their account\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Account Owner also has the privilege\u0026rsquo;s of delegating their responsibility (Role) to a Service Principal; which is the core of the process we are going to undertaken in this post.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eAs of March 2020; this is no longer relevant.\n\u003cdel\u003eThis account is REQUIRED to have established at least on subscription manually.\u003c/del\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eIn the \u003ca href=\"https://ea.azure.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eEA Portal\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003cem\u003eAccount\u003c/em\u003e page for a Department will present a list of established subscription.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/azure-billing-ea_privilege_delegation-EAPortalAccountsView.png\" alt=\"EP Portal\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/az-billing-ea_privilege_delegation.ibiza_experience.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eFor the test implemention we have created a new account with the following identity \u003ccode\u003eVDCSubscriptionDeploy@sky.uit.no\u003c/code\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/az-billing-ea_privilege_delegation.delegation_account.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eThis account needs to be added to the \u003cstrong\u003eCost Management + Billing\u003c/strong\u003e blade in the Azure portal, by a user which has the premissions on the EA\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd the account\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/az-billing-ea_privilege_delegation.new_account.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAccount Delegation Details\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/az-billing-ea_privilege_delegation.account_details.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"programmatic-subscription-creation\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Programmatic Subscription Creation\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe objective of the is process is to delegate the EA Account Owner privilege\u0026rsquo;s to a Service Principal, which can be leveraged to programmatically establish subscriptions. While the procedure is not overly complex; we will break the operation in 4 key milestones, which should make this easier to understand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEA Department Account Owner\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eService Principal for Delegation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDelegating EA Account Owner Privilege\u0026rsquo;s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eValidation\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"ea-department-account-owner\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#ea-department-account-owner\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'EA Department Account Owner'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    EA Department Account Owner\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the Azure AD account credentials for your Microsoft Tenant, you should be able to authenticate with the \u003ca href=\"https://ea.azure.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eEA Portal\u003c/a\u003e, and view the \u003cem\u003eAccount\u003c/em\u003e page, as illustrated earlier.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce you have confirmed that this works as expected, we will repeat this authentication again, however this time, using either the Azure Powershell Module or the Azure CLI; The guide will present the commands used in either scenario.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"authenticate-to-azure-the-ea-account-owner-credentials\"\u003eAuthenticate to Azure the EA Account Owner Credentials\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#authenticate-to-azure-the-ea-account-owner-credentials\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Authenticate to Azure the EA Account Owner Credentials'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWith working credentials validated in the EA Web portal, proceed with a new shell session and authenticate to Azure with your \u003cstrong\u003eEA Account Owner\u003c/strong\u003e credentials; you may also take advantage of the Azure Cloud Shell which will automate the login experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe credentials \u003cstrong\u003eMUST\u003c/strong\u003e be hosted in the tenants AAD instance.\nMicrosoft Accounts, or Guest accounts from other AAD Tenants are NOT Supported for the following procedures.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\n\u003ch5 class=\"heading heading-5\" id=\"az-cli\"\u003eAZ CLI\u003c/h5\u003e\u003ca href=\"#az-cli\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'AZ CLI'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eaz login --allow-no-subscriptions\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Authenticate as the account which was established with EA Account Permissions\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# This will create a new context, for us to work with the EA API\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch5 class=\"heading heading-5\" id=\"powershell\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/h5\u003e\u003ca href=\"#powershell\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Powershell'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$aadTenantId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$azSubscriptionId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;42d96448-0b0a-4b33-9d9a-5653a3f11811\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eConnect-AzAccount\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-TenantId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$aadTenantId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Subscription\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$azSubscriptionId\u003c/span\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az login\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"check-the-ea-accounts-which-we-have-access-to\"\u003eCheck the EA Accounts which we have access to\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#check-the-ea-accounts-which-we-have-access-to\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Check the EA Accounts which we have access to'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOnce you have authenticated, we will verify that the credentials do indeed have access to the EA environment, but getting a list of the EA Accounts which can be accessed\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch5 class=\"heading heading-5\" id=\"az-cli-1\"\u003eAZ CLI\u003c/h5\u003e\u003ca href=\"#az-cli-1\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'AZ CLI'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eshell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eaz billing enrollment-account list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch5 class=\"heading heading-5\" id=\"powershell-1\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/h5\u003e\u003ca href=\"#powershell-1\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Powershell'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003e``\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 8 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$eaAccountList\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzEnrollmentAccount\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$eaAccountList\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eObjectId\u003c/span\u003e                              \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePrincipalName\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--------\u003c/span\u003e                              \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-------------\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e88888888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e888888888888\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eeaaccountowner\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e@org\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eonmicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$EAAccountId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$eaAccountList\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eObjectId\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 10 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az billing enrollment-account list\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;id\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;principalName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;eaaccountowner@org.onmicrosoft.com\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssuming the results of these commands, presents back your account, and a billing enrollment object we are ready to proceed. If this is not the case, you must check that you are using the correct account.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe important data you have as we complete this stage is\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eVariable\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eValue\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure AD Tenant Id\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eaaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eEA Account ID\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003e88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"service-principal-for-delegation\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#service-principal-for-delegation\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Service Principal for Delegation'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Service Principal for Delegation\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThe EA Portal has been deprecated, and its features migrated to the Azure Portal\n\u003ca href=\"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/assign-roles-azure-service-principals\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/cost-management-billing/manage/assign-roles-azure-service-principals\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eOur objective is to delegate the role of creating new Azure Subscriptions to a Service Principal. Before we begin that effort; we first need to know the ObjectID of the (Service Principal) SPN which we are delegating to.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWe have two options, we can create a new Enterprise Application Credential, or we can create a Managed User Identity for the delegation\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"create-a-new-principal\"\u003eCreate a new principal\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#create-a-new-principal\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Create a new principal'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eEstablish a new AzureAD Application and a Service Principal in the AD Tenant. If you have an existing application which you would rather utilize; we can skip this step and reference that object in the next stage\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$password\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;S3cR3tP@ssw0rd!\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$credentials\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eNew-Object\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eCommands\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eActiveDirectory\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ePSADPasswordCredential\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Property\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"vm\"\u003e@\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eStartDate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-Date\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEndDate\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-Date\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Year\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e2024\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePassword\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$password\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$spName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AZ GOV Subscription Provision\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$sp\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eNew-AzAdServicePrincipal\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-DisplayName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$spName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-PasswordCredential\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$credentials\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 8 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eaz ad sp create-for-rbac --name \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;azGOVSubscriptionProvision\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;appId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;eeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;displayName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;azGOVSubscriptionProvision\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;http://azGOVSubscriptionProvision\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;password\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;8ff3e80e-a518-4dfa-ad5f-235bfb1d8bd9\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;tenant\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssuming no errors with this command, you should be able to locate the new principal in the Azure AD portal, under Enterprise Applications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n    \n  \n\n\n\u003cfigure class=\"my-8\"\u003e\n  \u003cimg src=\"/posts/azure-enterprise-agreement-delegating-roles-for-subscription-creation/azure-billing-ea_privilege_delegation-AADServicePrincipal.png\" alt=\"AAD SPN\" class=\"w-full rounded-lg\"  /\u003e\n  \n\u003c/figure\u003e\n\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"get-the-application-id\"\u003eGet the Application ID\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#get-the-application-id\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Get the Application ID'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf you plan on using a newly created Service Principal for the delegation, we can quickly reference it, and store it to a variable\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$sp\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eId\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appId\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eeeeeeeee-eeee\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAlternative, we can reference an existing application, and get its Application Id, in this case we simply provide the display name of the service principal we are going to reference\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az ad sp list --display-name azGOVSubscriptionProvision --query \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[].objectId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e -o tsv\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eeeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"delegating-ea-account-owner-privileges\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#delegating-ea-account-owner-privileges\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Delegating EA Account Owner Privilege\u0026rsquo;s'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Delegating EA Account Owner Privilege\u0026rsquo;s\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, we are at the heart of the show. We will delegate the Account Owner role to the chosen Service Principal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"add-the-service-principal-to-your-enrollment-account\"\u003eAdd the service principal to your enrollment account\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#add-the-service-principal-to-your-enrollment-account\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Add the service principal to your enrollment account'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe following command will allocate the \u003cstrong\u003eOwner\u003c/strong\u003e role to the EA Account Id which we discovered earlier, to our chosen Service Principal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ePowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eNew-AzRoleAssignment\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ObjectId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-RoleDefinitionName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Owner\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Scope\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$eaAccountId\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRoleAssignmentId\u003c/span\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eproviders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBilling\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eenrollmentAccounts\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e88888888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e888888888888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eproviders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAuthorization\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eroleAssignments\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eaa516c46\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e1954\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e4bac-bddf\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e618f1f03acf6\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eScope\u003c/span\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eproviders\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eMicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBilling\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eenrollmentAccounts\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e88888888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e8888\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e888888888888\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eDisplayName\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAZ\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eGOV\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eSubscription\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eProvision\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eSignInName\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRoleDefinitionName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eOwner\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRoleDefinitionId\u003c/span\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e8e3af657-a8ff\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e443c-a75c\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e2fe8c4bcb635\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eObjectId\u003c/span\u003e           \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eeeeeeeee-eeee\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eObjectType\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eServicePrincipal\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCanDelegate\u003c/span\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eFalse\u003c/span\u003e                           \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az role assignment create --role Owner --assignee-object-id eeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee --scope /providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;canDelegate\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: null,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;id\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888/providers/Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments/11341c1d-7785-46a9-a415-147b5c5aec5c\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;11341c1d-7785-46a9-a415-147b5c5aec5c\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;principalId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;eeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;roleDefinitionId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Authorization/roleDefinitions/8e3af657-a8ff-443c-a75c-2fe8c4bcb635\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;scope\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e   \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Authorization/roleAssignments\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"azure-ad-directory-reader\"\u003eAzure AD Directory Reader\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-ad-directory-reader\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure AD Directory Reader'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFinally, To ensure the ability of assigning Onwers to the new subscriptions, we MUST also ensure that the Service Principal has the minimum privilege\u0026rsquo;s of  Azure AD \u0026lsquo;Directory Reader\u0026rsquo; role\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eConnect-AzureAD\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-TenantId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eaaaaaaaa-aaaa\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccount\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnvironment\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eTenantId\u003c/span\u003e                             \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eTenantDomain\u003c/span\u003e             \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAccountType\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-------\u003c/span\u003e         \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-----------\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--------\u003c/span\u003e                             \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e------------\u003c/span\u003e             \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e-----------\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003euser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e@my\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eorg\u003c/span\u003e     \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzureCloud\u003c/span\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eaaaaaaaa-aaaa\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eorg\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eonmicrosoft\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eUser\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePS\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzureADDirectoryRoleMember\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ObjectId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e(\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzureADDirectoryRole\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ewhere-object\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$_\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eDisplayName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e-eq\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Directory Readers\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}).\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eObjectid\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-RefObjectId\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appId\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFantastic - now we need to wait for the clock work engine in the back of the cloud to wake up the Noddy. Go have a Coffee, and then we can check the results of our efforts\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThese delegations must be allowed to propagate, I have observed this taking up to 1 Hour!\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"validation\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Validation\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe final stage of this effort is to validate that everything is working as desired. After waiting for delegations to propagate, we will authenticate to Azure as our Service Principal, and then attempt to communicate with the services we have granted access to.  Ready?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"login-as-your-new-service-principal\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#login-as-your-new-service-principal\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Login as your new Service Principal'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Login as your new Service Principal\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWith a new shell (or an existing on if you wish); we will proceed to login to Azure using the Service Principal Credentials.\nI assume the service principal has no Azure subscriptions delegated to it; so we will indicate that also at login time, to prevent warning.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 16 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az login --service-principal -u eeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee --password Easter2019 --tenant aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa --allow-no-subscriptions\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;cloudName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AzureCloud\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;id\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;369b7bfe-5c66-41ef-837a-e2df4e9db6dd\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;isDefault\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: true,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Management\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;state\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Enabled\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;tenantId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;aaaaaaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-aaaaaaaaaaaa\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;user\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;eeeeeeee-eeee-eeee-eeee-eeeeeeeeeeee\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;servicePrincipal\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"check-you-have-directory-access\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#check-you-have-directory-access\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Check you have Directory Access'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Check you have Directory Access\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFirst test, lets see if we can read some object from the Azure AD\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az ad user list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssuming no issues, you should see a list of users scroll by, feel free to terminate that process when you are satisfied that this is working to plan\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"check-we-have-access-to-the-enterprise-agreement-account\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#check-we-have-access-to-the-enterprise-agreement-account\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Check we have access to the Enterprise Agreement Account'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Check we have access to the Enterprise Agreement Account\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, the real meat; Do we have access to the Enterprise Agreement Account?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 9 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-15\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-75ec929788fa16936a5f19d232a72e16-15\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e$\u0026gt; az billing enrollment-account list\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;id\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;/providers/Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts/88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;88888888-8888-8888-8888-888888888888\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;principalName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;eaaccountowner@org.onmicrosoft.com\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e,\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e: \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Billing/enrollmentAccounts\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAssuming you get a response, take a close look at the \u003cem\u003eprincipalName\u003c/em\u003e and you will be presented with the name of the account who have delegated their privilege\u0026rsquo;s to this active service account to work as.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Appending Tags to Azure Resources with ARM Templates",
        "date_published" : "2020-04-01T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2020-04-01T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/appending-tags-to-azure-resources-with-arm-templates/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/appending-tags-to-azure-resources-with-arm-templates/",
        "summary": "Todays conundrum: As I am leveraging templates, there will always be some standard tags I require to implement within the template, but I also require to provide additional tags as a parameter to be appended with the deployment.\nMy objective is to set up tags within an ARM template in accordance with good governance and the Cloud adoption framework.\nSolution ARM Template functions to the rescue. Todays salvation is called union, which you can learn more about on the actual [reference site][https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/resource-group-template-functions-array#union]\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eTodays conundrum: As I am leveraging templates, there will always be some standard tags I require to implement within the template, but I also require to provide additional tags as a parameter to be appended with the deployment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy objective is to set up tags within an ARM template in accordance with good governance and the Cloud adoption framework.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"solution\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Solution\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eARM Template functions to the rescue. Todays salvation is called \u003ccode\u003eunion\u003c/code\u003e, which you can learn more about on the actual [reference site][https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/azure-resource-manager/resource-group-template-functions-array#union]\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the existing implementation\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 120 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;$schema\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;contentVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;parameters\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;configVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;The version of the parameters file that holds the configuration.\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;purpose\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;diag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;log\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;audit\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;data\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;data\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;The designated purpose of the storage account. \u0026#39;diag\u0026#39; for diagnostics, \u0026#39;log\u0026#39; for logging, \u0026#39;audit\u0026#39; for auditing, \u0026#39;data\u0026#39; for data storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resilience\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_LRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_ZRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_GRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_RAGRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_LRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose a level of resilience and tier suitable for the purpose and region\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Premium\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose tier, Standard or Premium.\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;kind\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;StorageV2\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;BlobStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FileStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;BlockBlobStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;StorageV2\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose a kind of storage account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;iacVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;undefined\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;rgName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceGroup().name]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;rgLocation\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceGroup().location]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;uniqueString\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[uniqueString(subscription().id, resourceGroup().id)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountAffix\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(replace(variables(\u0026#39;rgName\u0026#39;), \u0026#39;-\u0026#39;, \u0026#39;\u0026#39;), parameters(\u0026#39;purpose\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[toLower(substring(replace(concat(variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountAffix\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;uniqueString\u0026#39;)), \u0026#39;-\u0026#39;, \u0026#39;\u0026#39;), 0, 23) )]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resources\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;comments\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;~~ Storage Account  ~~\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;apiVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;2018-07-01\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;sku\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;resilience\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;tier\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;kind\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;kind\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;location\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;rgLocation\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tags\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;IaCVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;iacVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;ConfigVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;configVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;scale\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003enull\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;properties\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;supportsHttpsTrafficOnly\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;encryption\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;services\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;file\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keyType\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;enabled\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;blob\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keyType\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;enabled\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keySource\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;accessTier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[if(equals(parameters(\u0026#39;kind\u0026#39;), \u0026#39;Storage\u0026#39;), json(\u0026#39;null\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;Hot\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;dependsOn\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;outputs\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceId(\u0026#39;Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts\u0026#39;, variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-change-set\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-change-set\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The Change Set'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The Change Set\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAnd using our new \u003ccode\u003eunion\u003c/code\u003e we can resolve the puzzle with 3 simple changes\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo the \u003ccode\u003eparameter\u003c/code\u003e we add a new object\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;tagValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;object\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;Dept\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Undefined\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;Environment\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Development\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the \u003ccode\u003evariables\u003c/code\u003e we can define our default tags\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultTag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;IaCVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;iacVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;ConfigVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;configVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd in the \u003ccode\u003eresource\u003c/code\u003e we can use the \u003ccode\u003eunion\u003c/code\u003e function to merge the objects together\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;tags\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[union(parameters(\u0026#39;tagValues\u0026#39;),variables(\u0026#39;defaultTag\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"final-view\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#final-view\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Final View'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Final View\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe final template will look as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 128 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-0222b53b496fecd6c6b5f23c82851efc-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;$schema\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;contentVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;parameters\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;configVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;The version of the parameters file that holds the configuration.\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tagValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;object\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;Dept\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Undefined\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;Environment\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Development\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;purpose\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;diag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;log\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;audit\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;data\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;data\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;The designated purpose of the storage account. \u0026#39;diag\u0026#39; for diagnostics, \u0026#39;log\u0026#39; for logging, \u0026#39;audit\u0026#39; for auditing, \u0026#39;data\u0026#39; for data storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resilience\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_LRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_ZRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_GRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_RAGRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard_LRS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose a level of resilience and tier suitable for the purpose and region\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Premium\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Standard\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose tier, Standard or Premium.\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;kind\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;allowedValues\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;StorageV2\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;BlobStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FileStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;BlockBlobStorage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;StorageV2\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;description\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Choose a kind of storage account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;iacVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;undefined\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultTag\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;IaCVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;iacVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;ConfigVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;configVersion\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;rgName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceGroup().name]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;rgLocation\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceGroup().location]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;uniqueString\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[uniqueString(subscription().id, resourceGroup().id)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountAffix\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[concat(replace(variables(\u0026#39;rgName\u0026#39;), \u0026#39;-\u0026#39;, \u0026#39;\u0026#39;), parameters(\u0026#39;purpose\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[toLower(substring(replace(concat(variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountAffix\u0026#39;), variables(\u0026#39;uniqueString\u0026#39;)), \u0026#39;-\u0026#39;, \u0026#39;\u0026#39;), 0, 23) )]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resources\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;comments\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;~~ Storage Account  ~~\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;apiVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;2018-07-01\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;sku\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;resilience\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;tier\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;kind\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[parameters(\u0026#39;kind\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;location\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;rgLocation\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;tags\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[union(parameters(\u0026#39;tagValues\u0026#39;),variables(\u0026#39;defaultTag\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;scale\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003enull\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;properties\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;supportsHttpsTrafficOnly\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;encryption\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;services\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;file\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keyType\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;enabled\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;blob\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keyType\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Account\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;enabled\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"kc\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;keySource\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Storage\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;accessTier\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[if(equals(parameters(\u0026#39;kind\u0026#39;), \u0026#39;Storage\u0026#39;), json(\u0026#39;null\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;Hot\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;dependsOn\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e],\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;outputs\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[resourceId(\u0026#39;Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts\u0026#39;, variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;))]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;storageAccountName\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;value\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[variables(\u0026#39;storageAccountName\u0026#39;)]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e    \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, Feel the force, and see what you can create\u0026hellip;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "ZFS Primer: Disks, Pools, Redundancy and Health Checks",
        "date_published" : "2020-03-05T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2020-03-05T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/zfs-primer-disks-pools-redundancy-and-health-checks/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/zfs-primer-disks-pools-redundancy-and-health-checks/",
        "summary": "For years, my home lab ran on a Dell PowerEdge R620 and R510, both well supplied with disks and RAM. They were dependable machines and gave me plenty of room to learn about virtualisation, networking and the architecture behind Azure Stack.\nThey also had a second job. From my wife\u0026rsquo;s point of view, I\u0026rsquo;d installed a very elaborate airing cupboard. The room stayed warm enough to dry clothes, while the server fans did an excellent job of collecting the resulting fluff.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eFor years, my home lab ran on a Dell PowerEdge R620 and R510, both well supplied with disks and RAM. They were dependable machines and gave me plenty of room to learn about virtualisation, networking and the architecture behind Azure Stack.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThey also had a second job. From my wife\u0026rsquo;s point of view, I\u0026rsquo;d installed a very elaborate airing cupboard. The room stayed warm enough to dry clothes, while the server fans did an excellent job of collecting the resulting fluff.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEventually, the heat, power consumption and dust were enough. I powered down the two servers and replaced them with a much smaller box. That prompted a fresh look at how I wanted to manage its disks, and brought me to ZFS.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese notes grew out of work on my Linux and Proxmox server. Ubuntu LTS was already familiar territory, so I wanted to understand the storage from the command line: which disks belonged to it, how the data was organised, and how to make that data available to containers and other machines.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe examples follow that process. They start with the physical disks, build a pool, divide it into datasets, then share selected datasets over the network. The Kubernetes section at the end is optional; you don\u0026rsquo;t need a cluster to get useful storage out of this setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBefore using the commands:\u003c/strong\u003e these are Linux/OpenZFS examples, with Debian/Ubuntu-style package commands and some historical output from my Proxmox host. They assume ZFS is already installed. Run administrative commands as root or with \u003ccode\u003esudo\u003c/code\u003e. Replace device IDs, hostnames, addresses and paths with your own. Pool creation writes to the selected disks and can destroy existing data; none of the creation examples should be run against an existing pool or your Proxmox boot disk.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"understand-what-youre-building\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Understand what you\u0026rsquo;re building\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eZFS combines storage management and a filesystem. There are a few names worth getting straight before creating anything:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003evdev\u003c/strong\u003e is a group of disks arranged as a mirror, RAIDZ group or another supported layout. Its layout determines its redundancy.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003epool\u003c/strong\u003e combines one or more vdevs into the storage you allocate from.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003edataset\u003c/strong\u003e is a filesystem within that pool, with its own properties, mount point and optional quota. Datasets can have children.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eA \u003cstrong\u003ezvol\u003c/strong\u003e is a block device backed by the pool. Proxmox can use these for VM disks; they are different from the filesystem datasets created below.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe two commands I\u0026rsquo;ll use most are \u003ccode\u003ezpool\u003c/code\u003e for the pool and its disks, and \u003ccode\u003ezfs\u003c/code\u003e for datasets and their properties:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool --help\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool status\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the examples, \u003ccode\u003etank\u003c/code\u003e is the data pool. My host also had an \u003ccode\u003erpool\u003c/code\u003e, which held the operating system. Keep that distinction in mind when reading the output: the data-pool instructions are not instructions to recreate \u003ccode\u003erpool\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"identify-the-disks-before-choosing-a-layout\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Identify the disks before choosing a layout\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe first job over SSH was to find the disks\u0026rsquo; persistent identifiers:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003els /dev/disk/by-id\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLinux device names such as \u003ccode\u003e/dev/sda\u003c/code\u003e are convenient, but their assignment can change as hardware is moved or detected in a different order. ZFS also stores pool information on the disks, so a changed letter does not automatically mean a lost pool. Persistent IDs still make administration much clearer, particularly when identifying a disk for replacement.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLook for the whole-disk identifiers for the drives you intend to use, and match them to the physical disks. A single disk may have several identifiers. Don\u0026rsquo;t mistake those aliases for separate drives, or select a \u003ccode\u003e-partN\u003c/code\u003e entry when you intend to use the whole disk.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSector sizes are the next thing to check:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003efdisk -l \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e grep Units\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003efdisk -l \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e grep Sector\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecat /sys/class/block/sda/queue/physical_block_size\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecat /sys/class/block/sdb/queue/logical_block_size\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe last two commands show different properties on two example disks. Inspect both properties for every disk you\u0026rsquo;re considering, substituting its current device name.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSome drives expose 512-byte logical sectors while using 4 KiB physical sectors; these are usually called 512e drives. ZFS\u0026rsquo;s \u003ccode\u003eashift\u003c/code\u003e property controls the minimum allocation alignment for a vdev: \u003ccode\u003eashift=12\u003c/code\u003e means 2¹² bytes, or 4 KiB. \u003ccode\u003eashift=13\u003c/code\u003e means 8 KiB, not a higher performance setting to choose automatically.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUse the disks\u0026rsquo; actual requirements to make that choice. Mixed sector sizes are possible, but deserve planning; setting \u003ccode\u003eashift\u003c/code\u003e appropriately is something to do at creation, rather than assuming it can be adjusted easily afterwards.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"choose-redundancy-then-create-the-pool\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Choose redundancy, then create the pool\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith two data disks, a mirror is a straightforward starting point. Each disk holds a copy, so usable capacity is roughly that of one disk. RAIDZ uses parity instead: RAIDZ1 tolerates one disk failure in its vdev, RAIDZ2 two, and RAIDZ3 three. The disk count, usable capacity and performance trade-offs differ.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRedundancy is chosen per vdev. Losing a normal data vdev can lose the whole pool, even when other vdevs are healthy. And redundancy is still not a backup: it won\u0026rsquo;t undo an accidental deletion or give you another copy after the server is stolen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe general creation syntax is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create [-o ashift=12] [-m \u0026lt;mountpoint\u0026gt;] \u0026lt;pool\u0026gt; \u0026lt;layout\u0026gt; \u0026lt;disk-ids...\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere is a two-disk mirror example using the drive IDs from my original notes. This is an example for a \u003cstrong\u003enew\u003c/strong\u003e pool, not a command to run on an existing \u003ccode\u003etank\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create -o \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eashift\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e12\u003c/span\u003e -m /tank tank mirror \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  /dev/disk/by-id/ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KMXVC \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  /dev/disk/by-id/ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KNTJA\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e-m /tank\u003c/code\u003e sets the root dataset\u0026rsquo;s mount point. Without an explicit mount point, the usual default for a pool named \u003ccode\u003etank\u003c/code\u003e is \u003ccode\u003e/tank\u003c/code\u003e, not \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a different set of disks, these are alternative RAIDZ2 examples. Replace \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;ids\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e with the space-separated persistent paths for enough disks to support the layout; the angle-bracket notation is not literal shell input. Choose one layout, not all three commands:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 8 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# Create a RAIDZ2 pool named storage.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create storage raidz2 \u0026lt;ids\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# Explicitly choose its mount point.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create -m /mnt/storage storage raidz2 \u0026lt;ids\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e# Set 4 KiB alignment at creation.\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create -o ashift=12 storage raidz2 \u0026lt;ids\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMy original commands used \u003ccode\u003e-f\u003c/code\u003e, for example \u003ccode\u003ezpool create -f -o ashift=12 ...\u003c/code\u003e. That flag forces past certain safety checks. It is not a routine fix for a label error: if ZFS objects to a disk, stop and understand why before considering an override.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"what-the-original-server-actually-used\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#what-the-original-server-actually-used\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'What the original server actually used'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    What the original server actually used\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThere was a misleading label in my original notes: I called this a mirror, but the command and output show a two-disk \u003cstrong\u003eRAIDZ1\u003c/strong\u003e vdev. I\u0026rsquo;ve kept the transcript here because it records what I actually created, rather than quietly rewriting the history:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 23 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eroot@hufflepuff:~# zpool create -f -o ashift=12 tank raidz1 ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KMXVC ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KNTJA\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eroot@hufflepuff:~# zpool status\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  pool: rpool\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e state: ONLINE\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003econfig:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        NAME                                             STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        rpool                                            ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          ata-M4-CT512M4SSD1_00000000121209086D4A-part3  ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eerrors: No known data errors\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  pool: tank\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e state: ONLINE\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003econfig:\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        NAME                                   STATE     READ WRITE CKSUM\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e        tank                                   ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          raidz1-0                             ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KMXVC  ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e            ata-ST16000NM001G-2KK103_ZL2KNTJA  ONLINE       0     0     0\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eerrors: No known data errors\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA mirror and a two-disk RAIDZ1 arrangement are not interchangeable layouts. For the two-disk starting point described above, use the mirror example rather than copying this historical command.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"check-health-capacity-and-activity-separately\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Check health, capacity and activity separately\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter creating a pool, I want to answer three different questions: are all its disks healthy, how much space is available, and what work is it doing?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool status\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool list\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool list -v\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool iostat\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool iostat -v\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ezpool status\u003c/code\u003e shows the topology, device state and read, write and checksum error counters. Look for the intended disks, an \u003ccode\u003eONLINE\u003c/code\u003e state and no unexplained errors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ezpool list\u003c/code\u003e gives a capacity summary; \u003ccode\u003e-v\u003c/code\u003e breaks it down by vdev. The original pool reported:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eNAME    SIZE  ALLOC   FREE  CKPOINT  EXPANDSZ   FRAG    CAP  DEDUP    HEALTH  ALTROOT\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003erpool   476G  2.37G   474G        -         -     0%     0%  1.00x    ONLINE  -\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank   29.1T   768K  29.1T        -         -     0%     0%  1.00x    ONLINE  -\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThat \u003ccode\u003e29.1T\u003c/code\u003e is pool-level space accounting for the historical RAIDZ layout. It is not a promise of 29.1 TiB of usable file storage. Parity, metadata and reserved space affect what datasets can actually use. Check \u003ccode\u003ezfs list\u003c/code\u003e for dataset availability.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003ezpool iostat\u003c/code\u003e reports operations and bandwidth, with \u003ccode\u003e-v\u003c/code\u003e showing the individual devices. A single invocation gives averages since boot; for a view of current activity, use an interval:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool iostat -v \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e2\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter the initial report, this refreshes every two seconds. Stop it with Ctrl+C.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"create-datasets-around-the-data\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Create datasets around the data\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce the pool exists, it is tempting to put everything straight into \u003ccode\u003e/tank\u003c/code\u003e. Separate datasets make it easier to apply different quotas, mount points and sharing policies without turning every ordinary directory into its own filesystem.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCompression is a useful property to set before writing data:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ecompression\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003elz4 tank\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eChild datasets inherit this setting unless they override it. LZ4 is a sensible general-purpose choice and can reduce disk I/O for compressible data. It won\u0026rsquo;t make every workload faster, and already-compressed media may shrink very little. Changing the setting does not recompress existing files automatically.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere is a consistent version of the dataset structure from my notes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/movies\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/tv\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/share\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/share/downloads\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003equota\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e1000G tank/share/downloads\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/vmstorage\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/vmstorage/limited\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003equota\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e1000G tank/vmstorage/limited\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/images\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003emountpoint\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/opt/images tank/images\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreate the parent \u003ccode\u003etank/share\u003c/code\u003e before its child \u003ccode\u003etank/share/downloads\u003c/code\u003e. The download dataset has a \u003ccode\u003e1000G\u003c/code\u003e quota, as does \u003ccode\u003etank/vmstorage/limited\u003c/code\u003e. ZFS interprets that suffix in binary units, so this is 1,000 GiB rather than exactly one decimal terabyte. A quota caps usage; it does not reserve that space in advance.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe images dataset illustrates another useful separation: its ZFS name is \u003ccode\u003etank/images\u003c/code\u003e, but applications see its files at \u003ccode\u003e/opt/images\u003c/code\u003e. Choose an empty, appropriate target before changing a mount point, or you may hide files already present beneath it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003evmstorage\u003c/code\u003e example is an ordinary filesystem dataset. Creating it does not register storage in Proxmox or create VM disks. Proxmox\u0026rsquo;s ZFS storage backend and directory storage backend have different roles; configure the appropriate one for VM disks, ISO images or container templates.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWithin a dataset, normal directories still work normally:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003els /tank\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003els /tank/share\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir /tank/share/Software\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir /tank/share/Backups\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir /tank/share/Projects\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir /tank/share/junk\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003els /tank/share\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThese directories share the parent dataset\u0026rsquo;s properties. Create another dataset only when you need a separate boundary, such as a quota or snapshot policy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor ISO images or container templates, a complete dataset name would be:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/share/iso\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYou can then add its mounted path as directory storage in Proxmox and enable the relevant content types. The incomplete \u003ccode\u003ezfs create tank/\u003c/code\u003e in my early notes wasn\u0026rsquo;t a usable command.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"containers-and-vms-access-the-data-differently\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#containers-and-vms-access-the-data-differently\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Containers and VMs access the data differently'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Containers and VMs access the data differently\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eA Proxmox container can use a host directory through a configured bind mount, subject to permissions and, for unprivileged containers, UID/GID mappings. A VM doesn\u0026rsquo;t share the host\u0026rsquo;s filesystem namespace. NFS or SMB provides a network route to the files; other file-sharing mechanisms are possible, but require their own configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe following sections are alternatives for exposing selected data. You don\u0026rsquo;t need to enable every sharing method.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"sharing-a-dataset-over-smb\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Sharing a dataset over SMB\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe ZFS sharing properties are worth inspecting before making changes:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs get sharesmb,sharenfs\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhere the installed OpenZFS and Samba integration supports it, the property command from my notes is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-15\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-15\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003esharesmb\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eon tank/tv\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is not the entire Samba setup. Samba must be installed and configured, users need access, and Linux distribution support for ZFS-managed SMB shares varies. An explicit Samba share pointing at the dataset\u0026rsquo;s mount point may be the appropriate approach on your host.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFilesystem permissions and Samba authentication are separate pieces. For example, assuming the local user \u003ccode\u003ebackups\u003c/code\u003e and group \u003ccode\u003ebackupusers\u003c/code\u003e already exist:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-16\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-16\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003echown backups:backupusers /tank/tv\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esmbpasswd -a backups\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe first command changes ownership of the dataset\u0026rsquo;s root directory, not every file underneath it. The second adds the user to Samba\u0026rsquo;s password database. My original note mixed \u003ccode\u003ebackups\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003ebackup\u003c/code\u003e, and used \u003ccode\u003esmbpasswd -b backup\u003c/code\u003e; use the intended account consistently and \u003ccode\u003e-a\u003c/code\u003e when adding it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"exporting-storage-over-nfs\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Exporting storage over NFS\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNFS was useful for making host storage available to other Linux machines and, later, Kubernetes workloads. Before configuring it, choose the actual dataset path and the clients allowed to access it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn a Debian/Ubuntu-style host, install the server package and start the service:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-17\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-17\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt update\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt install nfs-kernel-server\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e --now nfs-server\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe original preparation notes also included these commands:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-18\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-18\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt update \u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e sudo apt upgrade\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo hostnamectl set-hostname nfs-server.example.com --static\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNeither a full system upgrade nor a hostname change is required just to export a dataset. Schedule upgrades separately on a working Proxmox host, and don\u0026rsquo;t rename an existing Proxmox node casually, particularly if it belongs to a cluster.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the examples below, the export is \u003ccode\u003e/tank/pvc-nfs\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-19\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-19\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs create tank/pvc-nfs\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ecompression\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003elz4 tank/pvc-nfs\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eatime\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eoff tank/pvc-nfs\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eatime=off\u003c/code\u003e disables access-time updates on reads. That can reduce metadata writes for a file share, but check whether an application depends on access times before applying it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are two ways to define the export. Pick one for this dataset rather than maintaining conflicting definitions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"option-a-manage-the-export-in-etcexports\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#option-a-manage-the-export-in-etcexports\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Option A: manage the export in /etc/exports'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Option A: manage the export in \u003ccode\u003e/etc/exports\u003c/code\u003e\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOpen the server\u0026rsquo;s export configuration:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-20\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-20\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano /etc/exports\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEach entry has this structure:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-21\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-21\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003edirectory_to_share    client(share_option1,...,share_optionN)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor one permitted client, replace \u003ccode\u003eclient_ip\u003c/code\u003e with its real address:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-22\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-22\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e/tank/pvc-nfs    client_ip(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,root_squash)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003erw\u003c/code\u003e allows writes, while \u003ccode\u003esync\u003c/code\u003e asks the server to commit changes to stable storage before replying. \u003ccode\u003eno_subtree_check\u003c/code\u003e disables subtree checking, avoiding some problems with file handles when files are renamed. \u003ccode\u003eroot_squash\u003c/code\u003e maps requests from client root to an anonymous identity instead of granting it server-root privileges.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe earlier version of these notes included \u003ccode\u003e/home\u003c/code\u003e with \u003ccode\u003eno_root_squash\u003c/code\u003e. That is a substantial trust decision, not a default to copy: it allows client root to act as root within the export. Keep root squashing unless a specific, trusted workload requires otherwise.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApply the configuration, then inspect what the server is exporting:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-23\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-23\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo exportfs -rav\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo exportfs -s\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf service troubleshooting calls for it, you can restart NFS:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-24\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-24\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl restart nfs-server\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn ordinary export change generally needs a reload with \u003ccode\u003eexportfs\u003c/code\u003e, not a restart. You can also query the server remotely:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-25\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-25\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo showmount --exports 172.16.1.21\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003eshowmount\u003c/code\u003e is useful, but is not a complete test for an NFSv4-only configuration. Test an actual mount from the intended client, and restrict NFS access at the firewall as well as in the export definition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"option-b-use-the-zfs-nfs-property\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#option-b-use-the-zfs-nfs-property\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Option B: use the ZFS NFS property'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Option B: use the ZFS NFS property\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOn Linux systems with the relevant NFS integration installed, ZFS can manage the export through \u003ccode\u003esharenfs\u003c/code\u003e. For a client at the documentation-only example address \u003ccode\u003e192.0.2.10\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-26\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-26\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003esharenfs\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;rw=192.0.2.10,sync,no_subtree_check,root_squash\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e tank/pvc-nfs\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezfs get sharenfs\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSubstitute your actual client address. My old \u003ccode\u003erw.no_subtree_check,no_root_squash\u003c/code\u003e example had malformed option separation and granted more privilege than a general example should. Check the resulting active export with \u003ccode\u003eexportfs -s\u003c/code\u003e rather than assuming a property value alone proves that clients can use it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"mount-the-export-from-linux\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#mount-the-export-from-linux\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Mount the export from Linux'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Mount the export from Linux\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOn the client, ensure NFS client tools are installed and the target directory exists. Then mount the share:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-27\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-27\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mkdir -p /mnt/nfshare\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mount -t nfs -o \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003enfsvers\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e4\u003c/span\u003e nfs-server:/tank/pvc-nfs /mnt/nfshare\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReplace \u003ccode\u003enfs-server\u003c/code\u003e with a resolvable hostname or IP address. This is a manual mount, not a persistent \u003ccode\u003e/etc/fstab\u003c/code\u003e entry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe old generic example used a different server directory:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-28\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-28\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mkdir -p /data/nfshare\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you choose that path instead, create it on the server, export it, and use it in the client mount command too. Creating a directory alone does not make it a ZFS dataset or an NFS export. Matching paths is more useful than copying a working command from a different machine.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"a-macos-example-from-the-original-setup\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#a-macos-example-from-the-original-setup\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'A macOS example from the original setup'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    A macOS example from the original setup\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe Mac notes came from macOS Catalina 10.15.6 and used a separate music export. The intended \u003ccode\u003e/etc/exports\u003c/code\u003e entry is a \u003cstrong\u003esingle line\u003c/strong\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-29\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-29\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e/pool/music client_ip(rw,sync,insecure,no_subtree_check,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000)\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere, \u003ccode\u003eall_squash\u003c/code\u003e maps every client\u0026rsquo;s user and group IDs to the anonymous identity, with \u003ccode\u003eanonuid\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eanongid\u003c/code\u003e choosing UID/GID 1000. That identity must have the intended access on the server. This can suit a simple shared media directory, but removes per-user identity at the filesystem boundary. The \u003ca href=\"https://serverfault.com/a/241272/407465\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eServer Fault explanation\u003c/a\u003e is a useful reference for those options.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe original used \u003ccode\u003e*\u003c/code\u003e for the client. Restrict it to the actual client or trusted subnet. \u003ccode\u003einsecure\u003c/code\u003e permits requests from unprivileged source ports; only retain it if needed by your client setup.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReload the server\u0026rsquo;s exports:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-30\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-30\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo exportfs -ra\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOn the Mac, the historical configuration edit was:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-31\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-31\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo vi /etc/nfs.conf\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this setting \u003cstrong\u003einside the file\u003c/strong\u003e, not entered as a shell command:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-32\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-32\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003enfs.client.mount.options = vers=4\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe mount command was:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-33\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-33\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mkdir -p /Users/me/mount\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mount -t nfs -o resvport,rw,noowners 172.20.0.100:/pool/music /Users/me/mount\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReplace the address and username. \u003ccode\u003eresvport\u003c/code\u003e requests a reserved source port. The client\u0026rsquo;s \u003ccode\u003enoowners\u003c/code\u003e behaviour does not configure the server\u0026rsquo;s anonymous identity; \u003ccode\u003eall_squash\u003c/code\u003e, \u003ccode\u003eanonuid\u003c/code\u003e and \u003ccode\u003eanongid\u003c/code\u003e do that. Treat these as historical Mac settings to check against your current macOS version.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"optional-use-the-nfs-dataset-from-kubernetes\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Optional: use the NFS dataset from Kubernetes\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce a client can mount and write to the export, Kubernetes can use it. The NFS subdirectory external provisioner creates a subdirectory on an existing export for each claim. It does not create the ZFS pool, configure NFS, or create a separate ZFS dataset per claim.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe original setup used this Helm repository:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-34\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-34\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehelm repo add nfs-subdir-external-provisioner https://kubernetes-sigs.github.io/nfs-subdir-external-provisioner\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehelm repo update\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eInstall the provisioner with the server and export path that you have already tested:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-35\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-35\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ehelm install nfs-subdir-external-provisioner nfs-subdir-external-provisioner/nfs-subdir-external-provisioner \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  --set nfs.server\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e172.16.1.21 \u003cspan class=\"se\"\u003e\\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  --set nfs.path\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/tank/pvc-nfs\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAll participating nodes need NFS client support and network access. Set the export directory\u0026rsquo;s ownership and permissions for the identities the provisioner and workloads actually use. A write failure is a reason to inspect permissions and UID/GID mappings, not immediately disable root squashing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis claim explicitly selects the chart\u0026rsquo;s usual \u003ccode\u003enfs-client\u003c/code\u003e StorageClass. Save it as \u003ccode\u003etest-pvc.yaml\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003eyaml\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 12 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-36\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-36\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eapiVersion\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ev1\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ekind\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003ePersistentVolumeClaim\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003emetadata\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003etest-claim\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003enamespace\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003edefault\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003espec\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eaccessModes\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e- \u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003eReadWriteMany\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estorageClassName\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003enfs-client\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e  \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003eresources\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e    \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003erequests\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e      \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003estorage\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"w\"\u003e \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"l\"\u003e128Mi\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApply it and inspect the result:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-37\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-37\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ekubectl apply -f test-pvc.yaml\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ekubectl get pvc test-claim\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe requested \u003ccode\u003e128Mi\u003c/code\u003e does not, by itself, enforce a 128 MiB limit on a subdirectory of the NFS export. That differs from the ZFS dataset quotas used earlier.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you deliberately want this StorageClass to become the cluster default, the correctly quoted patch is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-38\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-38\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ekubectl patch storageclass nfs-client -p \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;{\u0026#34;metadata\u0026#34;:{\u0026#34;annotations\u0026#34;:{\u0026#34;storageclass.kubernetes.io/is-default-class\u0026#34;:\u0026#34;true\u0026#34;}}}\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck existing defaults first. This is a cluster-wide choice for claims that omit a StorageClass, not a required step for the explicit claim above. The backticks in my original command would have caused shell command substitution rather than passing the JSON as intended.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"optional-cache-devices-and-larger-layouts\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Optional: cache devices and larger layouts\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTwo commands in the original notes deserve to sit outside the basic setup, because neither is required to get a working pool.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAn SSD can be added as an L2ARC read-cache device:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-39\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-39\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool add tank cache \u0026lt;drive-id\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eReplace \u003ccode\u003e\u0026lt;drive-id\u0026gt;\u003c/code\u003e with the intended persistent device path. This writes to the chosen cache device; inspect it as carefully as the data disks. The original command included \u003ccode\u003e-f\u003c/code\u003e, which should not be a routine addition here either.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eL2ARC is a secondary read cache, not extra usable pool capacity and not a write cache. It also has memory overhead. Measure your workload before assuming an SSD cache will improve it; a media library doing mostly sequential reads may see little benefit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor a larger \u003cstrong\u003enew\u003c/strong\u003e pool, the earlier notes also sketched two mirrored vdevs and a spare. Here is the corrected \u003ccode\u003eashift\u003c/code\u003e spelling and persistent-path form:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 7 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-40\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-40\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool create -o ashift=12 storage \\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  mirror /dev/disk/by-id/\u0026lt;disk-a\u0026gt; /dev/disk/by-id/\u0026lt;disk-b\u0026gt; \\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  mirror /dev/disk/by-id/\u0026lt;disk-c\u0026gt; /dev/disk/by-id/\u0026lt;disk-d\u0026gt; \\\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  spare /dev/disk/by-id/\u0026lt;disk-e\u0026gt;\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool status\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ezpool list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is an alternative design, not an extra command to run after creating \u003ccode\u003etank\u003c/code\u003e. Each mirror provides redundancy within its own vdev. The spare is available as a replacement device; it does not add normal data capacity or turn the whole arrangement into a higher-parity RAIDZ group.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"what-the-organisation-looked-like-in-practice\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  What the organisation looked like in practice\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA later \u003ccode\u003ezfs list\u003c/code\u003e from my server shows why I found datasets useful. These are historical paths and sizes, not the output of following every example above:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003etext\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-41\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-5d8aa0f3694061c644ad2b8e2bd96987-41\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eNAME          USED   AVAIL   REFER   MOUNTPOINT\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank          12.6T  1.45T   75.3G   /mnt/tank\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/appdata  19.0G  1.45T   19.0G   /opt/appdata\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/books     560M  1.45T    560M   /mnt/local/books\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/devices   174G  1.45T    174G   /mnt/tank/devices\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/feeder   51.6G  1.45T   51.6G   /mnt/feeder\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/images   9.73G  1.45T   9.73G   /opt/images\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/movies   3.08T  1.45T   3.08T   /mnt/local/movies\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/music     116G  1.45T    116G   /mnt/local/music\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/pvc-nfs   128K  1.45T    128K   /mnt/tank/pvc-nfs\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etank/tv       9.13T  1.45T   9.13T   /mnt/local/tv\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe datasets all draw from the pool, while their mount points suit the applications using them. The repeated \u003ccode\u003eAVAIL\u003c/code\u003e value is shared availability, not a separate allocation of 1.45T to each dataset.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor my smaller home server, this gave me a way to keep application data, media and shared storage organised without fixing each one into a separate disk partition. It also left me with a few useful commands to return to: \u003ccode\u003ezpool status\u003c/code\u003e for health, \u003ccode\u003ezpool iostat\u003c/code\u003e for activity, and \u003ccode\u003ezfs list\u003c/code\u003e for the filesystems consuming the space.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBefore trusting important data to a setup like this, arrange regular scrubs, health alerts and backups to another system, then test a restore. Pool redundancy helps with disk failures; recovery still needs a copy that survives losing this server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Application Gateway and WAF Updates (Ignite 2019)",
        "date_published" : "2019-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-application-gateway-and-waf-updates-ignite-2019/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-application-gateway-and-waf-updates-ignite-2019/",
        "summary": "Ignite Session: BRK3169 Presenter: Amit Srivastava\nMission Critical HTTP Applications, there are many things to consider\nPersonalized, Micro-Services, Rich Context\u0026hellip;. To support this MS have a number of services i the Suite - Azure Frontdoor, Application Gateway, Azure CDN, Web Application Firewall, Azure Load Balancer, and Azure Traffic Manager\nAzure Application Gateway Regional Gateway as a service\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eIgnite Session: BRK3169\nPresenter: Amit Srivastava\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMission Critical HTTP Applications, there are many things to consider\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePersonalized, Micro-Services, Rich Context\u0026hellip;. To support this MS have a number of services i the Suite - Azure Frontdoor, Application Gateway, Azure CDN, Web Application Firewall, Azure Load Balancer, and Azure Traffic Manager\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azure-application-gateway\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-application-gateway\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure Application Gateway'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-application-gateway\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure Application Gateway\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRegional Gateway as a service\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ctable\u003e\n  \u003cthead\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eFeature\u003c/th\u003e\n          \u003cth\u003eDescription\u003c/th\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/thead\u003e\n  \u003ctbody\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePlatform managed\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eBuilt in high availability and scalability)\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eLayer 7 balancing\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eURL Path, Host based, round robin, session affinity, redirection\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eSecurity and SSL management\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eWAF, SSL Offload, SSL Re-Encryption, SSL Policy\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePublic or ILB\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003ePublic, Internal or Both\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eFlexible backends\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eVMs, VMSS, AKS, Public IP, Cloud Services, ALB.ILB/ On-Premises\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n      \u003ctr\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eRich Diagnostics\u003c/td\u003e\n          \u003ctd\u003eAzure Monitor, Log analytics, Network Watched, RHC, Azure Security Center\u003c/td\u003e\n      \u003c/tr\u003e\n  \u003c/tbody\u003e\n\u003c/table\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eStandard V2 SKU in GA, Currently Available in 26 regions, Builtin Zone Redundancy, Static VIP, HTTP Header/cookies insertion/modification\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIncreased scale limits 20 -\u0026gt; 100 Listeners\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eKey Vault integration and auto-renewal of SSL Certs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAKS ingress Controller\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"autoscaling-and-performance-improvements\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#autoscaling-and-performance-improvements\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Autoscaling and Performance Improvements'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"autoscaling-and-performance-improvements\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Autoscaling and Performance Improvements\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrow and shrink based on app traffic requirements\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e5X better SSL offloads performance\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e500-50,000 connections/sec with RSA 2048 bit certs\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e30,000-3,000,000 persistent connections\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e2,500-250,000 reqs/sec\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"announcing-general-availability\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#announcing-general-availability\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Announcing General Availability:'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"announcing-general-availability\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Announcing General Availability:\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFrontend TLS cert integration with Azure Key Vault\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUtilized user-assigned managed identity access control for key vault\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUser Certificates or secrets on key vault\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePolls every 4 hours to enable automatic cert renewal\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003emanual override of specific certificate version retrieval\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eManipulate Request and Response headers \u0026amp; cookies\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStrip port from X-Forwarded-for header\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd security headers like HSTS and X-XSS-Protection\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommon header manipulation ex HOST, SERVER\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"aks-ingress-control-using-application-gateways\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  AKS Ingress Control using Application Gateways\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDeployed using Helm\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eUtilizes Pod-AAD for ARM authentication\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTighter integration with AKS add on support coming\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport URI path based, host based, SSL termination, SSL re-encryption, redirection, custom health probes, draining, cookie affinity\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport for Lets Encrypt provide TLS certificates\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eWAF fully supported with custom listener policy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport for multiple AKS as backend\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport for  mixed mode - both AKS and other backend types on the same Application Gateway\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"http://aka.ms/appgwaks\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttp://aka.ms/appgwaks\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"wild-card-listener\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Wild Card Listener\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport for Wildcard characters in the listener host name\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport for * and ? Characters in host name\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAssociated wildcard or SAN certificates the service HTTPS enabled domains\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSend traffic to multiple tenant end points\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"diagnostics-and-logs-enhancements\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Diagnostics and logs enhancements\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTLS Protocol\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eTLS Cipher\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBackend target server\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ebackend response code\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ebackend latency\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"metrics\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Metrics\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBackend response status code\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRPS healthy nodes\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnd to End Latency\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBackend Latency\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBackend connect, first byte and last byte latency\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"app-monitor-insights-for-application-gateway\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#app-monitor-insights-for-application-gateway\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'App Monitor Insights for Application Gateway'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"app-monitor-insights-for-application-gateway\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  App Monitor Insights for Application Gateway\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSingle health and metic console for your entire cloud network\nNo agent/configuration required\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azure-waf---cloud-native-web-application-firewall\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-waf---cloud-native-web-application-firewall\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure WAF - Cloud Native WEB Application Firewall'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-waf---cloud-native-web-application-firewall\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure WAF - Cloud Native WEB Application Firewall\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUnified WAF offering to protect your apps at network edge or region uniformly\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"public-preview-announced\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Public preview announced\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft threats intelligence\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProtect agains automatic attacks\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eManaged good and bad bots with Azure BotManager Rule Set\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eData is refreshed daily\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEasy to configure in WAF policy\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHelps increase your applications performance, by stopping aggressive crawlers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSite and URI path specific WAF Policies\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCustomized WAF police at the region WAF\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAssign different Policies to different sites\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSite specific polices implies you can tune the WAF to suit the needs of each site independently\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGeo filtering on regional WAF\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAllow or Block a list of countries,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSupport log mode\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRule Set for CRS 3.1 added (to be the default soon)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIntegration with Azure Sentinel\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePerformance and concurrency enhancements\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Private Link: Delivering Services Privately (Ignite 2019)",
        "date_published" : "2019-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-11-07T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-private-link-delivering-services-privately-ignite-2019/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-private-link-delivering-services-privately-ignite-2019/",
        "summary": " Azure Private Link MS Ignite 2019 Session: #BRK3168 Presenters: Narayan Annamalai and Sumeet Mittal\nThis service has exited Public Preview, and is now published to all regions as General Availability\nAdditionally today (November 2019) in US West Central, US North, and US East the ability to use with CosmosDB has been added to this service\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"azure-private-link\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#azure-private-link\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Azure Private Link'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-private-link\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure Private Link\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"/posts/microsoft-ignite-2019/\" rel=\"\"\u003eMS Ignite 2019\u003c/a\u003e Session: #BRK3168\nPresenters: Narayan Annamalai and Sumeet Mittal\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eThis service has exited Public Preview, and is now published to all regions as General Availability\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cdel\u003eAdditionally today (November 2019) in US West Central, US North, and US East the ability to use with \u003cem\u003eCosmosDB\u003c/em\u003e has been added to this service\u003c/del\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"your-service\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Your Service\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eScenario, Number of VMs, linked to a Standard Load balancer. With a single click the Front End IP of the SLB, will be implemented as a Private Link, replacing the public IP with its new Private Address\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate or Convert your existing services in Private Link Services\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eVNET-VNET Connectivity\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo Connect to this service, we simply create a \u003cstrong\u003ePrivate Endpoint\u003c/strong\u003e in the VNET linked to the Private Link Endpoint.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate the Service\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConvert to Private Link Service on SLB Frontend IP\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShare the Private Link Service ID Alias (ARM Resource ID) to the customers\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCreate a Private Endpoint in any subnet by specify the private link service URI/Alias\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eConfigure the DNS record to the price ip address\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAct on the request o accept or reject the connection\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOnce approve the Private link is established\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"alias\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#alias\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Alias'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Alias\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo hide the hosting subscription id, and resource group id of the service being published, for security mapping, an Alias can be established which will mask the original ID - The name is established using a GUID, and some customer concatenated strings to identify the resource\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"visibility\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#visibility\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Visibility'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Visibility\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo ensure the exposure of the service is limited, the Endpoint can be protected, even if the link name, or alias is determined; using an approval process:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eRBAC\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSubscription\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eopen to anyone with the link\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"auto-approval\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#auto-approval\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Auto-Approval'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Auto-Approval\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo support a large scale scenario for approvals, an automation can be used to set the audience which will be auto-approved.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"nat-ip\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#nat-ip\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'NAT-IP'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    NAT-IP\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe service provider also has the ability to Allocate a Private IP, which is translated to the Source IP. Logging is linked to the IP Allocated by the Service Provide, which is presented as the SourceIP for inbound packets\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"tcp-proxy-v2\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#tcp-proxy-v2\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'TCP Proxy v2'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    TCP Proxy v2\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eServer Side Settings, including headers for Source IP of customer and Link ID of private Endpoint. Currently been testing in NGNIX to implement a new custom header for Private Link.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "C-Bus to MQTT Bridge on a Raspberry Pi with C-Gate",
        "date_published" : "2019-10-10T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-10-10T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/c-bus-to-mqtt-bridge-on-a-raspberry-pi-with-c-gate/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/c-bus-to-mqtt-bridge-on-a-raspberry-pi-with-c-gate/",
        "summary": " CBus MQTT Bridge on Raspberry PI Turn back to 2007; My wife and I built our home, integrating many smart technologies, including the Clipsal CBus lighting system. This solution is classified as a Prosumer technology, and is designed to integrate into whole house automation systems.\nThe CBus system implements however a proprietary technology, and utilizes a communication protocol which is not \u0026lsquo;open source\u0026rsquo;; however, accepting a license agreement will permit access to this protocol for creating an programming interface.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch1 class=\"relative text-5xl font-semibold leading-tense text-secondary-500 mb-4 -ml-px\" id=\"cbus-mqtt-bridge-on-raspberry-pi\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#cbus-mqtt-bridge-on-raspberry-pi\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'CBus MQTT Bridge on Raspberry PI'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"cbus-mqtt-bridge-on-raspberry-pi\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  CBus MQTT Bridge on Raspberry PI\n\u003c/h1\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTurn back to 2007; My wife and I built our home, integrating many smart technologies, including the Clipsal CBus lighting system. This solution is classified as a Prosumer technology, and is designed to integrate into whole house automation systems.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe CBus system implements however a proprietary technology, and utilizes a communication protocol which is not \u0026lsquo;open source\u0026rsquo;; however, accepting a license agreement will permit access to this protocol for creating an programming interface.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo simplify (arguable) the process of integrating with the CBus environment Clipsal released a Bridge solution which enables a TCP interface using a special Java application called \u0026lsquo;C-GATE\u0026rsquo;.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing a Raspberry Pi, with a USB to RS-232 cable, which is then connected to a Clipsal interface called the \u003cem\u003eSerial PCI Module\u003c/em\u003e,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"prerequisites\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Prerequisites\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDeploy the current release of Rasbian for your Pi.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eUpdate: Jan 2021 - Currently using Rasbian 2021-01-11\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eOnce the Pi have been configured and added to the network, we can connect via SSH, and begin installing the pre-requisites for our gateway.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 6 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Serial 2 Socket Build Tools\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get install git build-essential autotools-dev devscripts libssl-dev \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Java 8 Runtime for CGate\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get installopenjdk-8-jdk\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Node and NPM for CGateWeb\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get installnode npm\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"tcp-to-serial-bridge\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  TCP to Serial Bridge\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eConfiguring the CBus system over TCP however will not work with just C-Gate alone, we need to also establish a TCP connection directly to the \u003cem\u003eSerial PCI Module\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"serial-to-socket\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#serial-to-socket\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Serial To Socket'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Serial To Socket\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThis requires that we compile and run a small \u003cem\u003eC\u003c/em\u003e application (Don\u0026rsquo;t worry, this is painless and fast); It took a lot of searching to find, posted the source to the following GIT repository; the application is called \u003cstrong\u003eser2sock\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHere’s the steps to get it set up:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 9 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egit clone https://github.com/nutechsoftware/ser2sock.git  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ser2sock\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e./configure --without-ssl\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecc -o ser2sock ser2sock.c  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mv ser2sock /usr/local/bin  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /usr/local/bin/ser2sock  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chown -R pi:pi /usr/local/bin/ser2sock \u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"running-as-a-service---systemd\"\u003eRunning as a service - System.d\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#running-as-a-service---systemd\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Running as a service - System.d'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe source offers us a sample init script which we can use for starting the service. First we will place this in the SystemD folder, and then update it to match our requirements for C-Gate\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo cp ~/ser2sock/init/systemd/ser2sock.service /etc/systemd/system\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdate the startup script, \u003ccode\u003e/etc/systemd/system/ser2sock.service\u003c/code\u003e to have the daemon auto-start with the required C-Gate port, which is TCP 10001, and the serial interface baud rate set to 9600.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 11 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eUnit\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDescription\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eProxy that allows tcp connections to serial ports\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eAfter\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003esyslog.target network.target\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eService\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eType\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eforking\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line hl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eExecStart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/local/bin/ser2sock -p \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e10001\u003c/span\u003e -s /dev/ttyUSB0 -b \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e9600\u003c/span\u003e -d\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eExecReload\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/bin/kill -HUP \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$MAINPID\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eInstall\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eWantedBy\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003emulti-user.target\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen activate using:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e ser2sock.service  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl start ser2sock.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"installing-c-gate\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Installing C-Gate\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://updates.clipsal.com/ClipsalSoftwareDownload/mainsite/cis/technical/CGate/cgate-2.11.4_3251.zip\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eDownload\u003c/a\u003e the current software release of C-Gate off the clipsal website and unzipped the files into \u003ccode\u003e/usr/local/bin/cgate.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 4 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e ~\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewget https://updates.clipsal.com/ClipsalSoftwareDownload/mainsite/cis/technical/CGate/cgate-2.11.4_3251.zip  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eunzip cgate-*.zip  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo mv cgate /usr/local/bin\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"running-c-gate-as-service---systemd\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#running-c-gate-as-service---systemd\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Running C-Gate as Service - System.d'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Running C-Gate as Service - System.d\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAdding the following \u0026lsquo;system.d\u0026rsquo; startup script, to have the daemon auto-start with the operating system \u003ccode\u003e/etc/systemd/system/cgate.service\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 14 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eUnit\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDescription\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eClipsal CBUS Gateway\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eAfter\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003esyslog.target network.target\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eService\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eExecStart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/bin/java -Djava.awt.headless\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e -jar -noverify /usr/local/bin/cgate/cgate.jar  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eRestart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003ealways  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eUser\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eroot  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eGroup\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eroot  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eEnvironment\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003ePATH\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/bin:/usr/local/bin  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eWorkingDirectory\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/local/bin/cgate/\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eInstall\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eWantedBy\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003emulti-user.target\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen activate using\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e cgate.service  \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl start cgate.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"c-gate-access-control\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#c-gate-access-control\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'C-Gate Access Control'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    C-Gate Access Control\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWe must configure the C-Gate service to allow remote connections from machines on the network by editing the access control file \u003ccode\u003enano /usr/local/bin/cgate/config/access.txt\u003c/code\u003e; adding a line, providing the ip address of the remote system. In the example I am allowing the network 172.16.0.0/23 or the IP\u0026rsquo;s in the range of 172.16.0.0 to 172.16.255.255\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;remote 172.16.255.255 Program\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u0026gt;\u0026gt; /usr/local/bin/cgate/config/access.tx\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSave, then restart cgate:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl restart cgate.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"c-gate-auto-connect\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#c-gate-auto-connect\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'C-Gate Auto-Connect'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    C-Gate Auto-Connect\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eEdit the file \u003ccode\u003e/usr/local/bin/cgate/config/C-gateConfig.txt\u003c/code\u003e. Set the \u003cstrong\u003eproject.default\u003c/strong\u003e and \u003cstrong\u003eproject.start\u003c/strong\u003e lines to the name of the C-Gate Project.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you do not know your project name, you can interact with C-Gate over telnet\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003etelnet 127.0.0.1 \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20023\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u0026gt; project list\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn my environment, my project is called \u003ccode\u003ehome\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"cgate-mqtt\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  CGate MQTT\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMQTT interface for CBus lighting written in Node.js\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /usr/local/bin\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo git clone https://github.com/the1laz/cgateweb.git\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e cgateweb\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003enpm install\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano settings.js\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePut in your settings.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6a600e2586c215925e6af12b9a6c92c7-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo cp cgateweb.service /etc/systemd/system\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e cgateweb\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl start cgateweb\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAt this point, you should start seeing your MQTT Service update with CBus Lighting application status.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Configure the Azure Application Gateway WAF with PowerShell",
        "date_published" : "2019-10-03T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-10-03T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/configure-the-azure-application-gateway-waf-with-powershell/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/configure-the-azure-application-gateway-waf-with-powershell/",
        "summary": "Microsoft Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 application delivery controller (ADC) offered as a service in Azure. It provides load balancing, SSL termination, end-to-end SSL, URL path-based routing, and basic web application firewall (WAF) functionality.\nWorking with the WAF, I usually build a basic configuration in the Portal before exporting the ARM JSON, which, then becomes my primary method to working on this service.\nWhy JSON you may ask\u0026hellip; One of my biggest gripes with the Azure Firewall solutions currently is based on thier CRUD (Create, Read, Update and Delete) interface. It always results in a workflow from hell, training along the lines of \u0026lsquo;Edit, Save, WAIT,, Edit, Save, WAIT\u0026rsquo; in a painful loop. What should be a fast and straightforward configuration update, typically is a process that must be executed over many hours, preferably on a second screen.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eMicrosoft Azure Application Gateway is a Layer 7 application delivery controller (ADC) offered as a service in Azure. It provides load balancing, SSL termination, end-to-end SSL, URL path-based routing, and basic web application firewall (WAF) functionality.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorking with the WAF, I usually build a basic configuration in the Portal before exporting the ARM JSON, which, then becomes my primary method to working on this service.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"why-json-you-may-ask\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Why JSON you may ask\u0026hellip;\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOne of my biggest gripes with the Azure Firewall solutions currently is based on thier CRUD \u003cem\u003e(Create, Read, Update and Delete)\u003c/em\u003e interface. It always  results in a workflow from hell, training along the lines of \u0026lsquo;\u003cem\u003eEdit, Save,\u003c/em\u003e \u003cem\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWAIT,\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003eEdit, Save,\u003c/em\u003e \u003cem\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWAIT\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u0026rsquo; in a painful loop.  What should be a fast and straightforward configuration update, typically is a process that must be executed over many hours, preferably on a second screen.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"powershell\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Powershell\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile I spend a large amount of my working time sitting in VS code, with a terminal logged into Azure with both Powershell and Azure CLI, I do not every recall trying to work with the Application Gateway from this interface ever!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI was asked to check the HTTP Timeout on one of the Firewalls I have access to, and send the details to a colleague; my first port of call was JSON, and then realized that this is a bit ugly for the request in hand.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA quick PowerShell command should sort this out, which of course has even more Idiosyncrasy.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"working-with-application-gateways-in-powershell\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Working With Application Gateways in PowerShell\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWait for it (Remember my CRUD comment). Well, The PowerShell implementation is restricted by that same API limitations. The first step for updating any existing Gateway is to load the whole gateway configuration from Azure into a PowerShell object.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ep-ap1pub\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-waf01\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom here, all the changes we make are to the PowerShell object \u003ccode\u003e$appGw\u003c/code\u003e until we are ready to commit the gateway back to Azure with the following command:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eSet-AzApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"making-changes\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#making-changes\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Making changes'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Making changes\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUnderstanding that all configurations are going to be applied to our in-memory object \u003ccode\u003e$appGw\u003c/code\u003e; we can use any of the available PowerShell commandlets to alter this object, and once ready to validate we must push these changes back to Azure with the \u003ccode\u003eSet-AzApplicationGateway\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eNow you will understand why I ignore this rubbish and work with the ARM JSON!\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eLet\u0026rsquo;s take a swift tour of working with this object to establish an end-to-end SSL listener, which would be atypical of any implemented configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"backend\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#backend\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Backend'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Backend\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"backend-pool\"\u003eBackend Pool\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#backend-pool\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Backend Pool'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe backend pool for our web servers can be created using FQDNs or IPs; I usually implement this initially using IP addresses.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayBackendAddressPool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPool\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-BackendIPAddresses\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;192.168.####101\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;192.168.1.102\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzApplicationGatewayBackendAddressPool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPool\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"backend-ssl-encryption\"\u003eBackend SSL Encryption\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#backend-ssl-encryption\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Backend SSL Encryption'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFrequently, we establish the connection as a genuine end-to-end encrypted connection; which implies that the Web Application Gateway should have an authentication certificate, so it only forward\u0026rsquo;s traffic to a backend server if it has the expected SSL certificate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo enable this, we must upload the public certificate used by the backend servers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayAuthenticationCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPoolPublicCert\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CertificateFile\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;.\\myAppPublicCertifcate.cer\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPoolCert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzureRmApplicationGatewayAuthenticationCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPoolPublicCert\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"configure-the-backend-service\"\u003eConfigure the Backend Service\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configure-the-backend-service\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Configure the Backend Service'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we can configure the HTTPS Protocol and authentication certificate the WAF will use to validate the backend servers.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayBackendHttpSettings\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPoolHTTPS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Port\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e443\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Protocol\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eHttps\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CookieBasedAffinity\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eEnabled\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-AuthenticationCertificates\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPoolCert\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPoolHTTPS\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzureRmApplicationGatewayBackendHttpSettings\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$AppGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppPoolHTTPS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"frontend\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#frontend\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Frontend'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Frontend\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow we can switch focus on build the frontend configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"a-public-ssl-certificate\"\u003eA public SSL certificate.\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#a-public-ssl-certificate\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'A public SSL certificate.'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe certificate should be in PFX format with a password. We add this to the gateway object as follows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewaySslCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FrontCert\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-CertificateFile\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;.\\myExternalFacingCertWithPrivateKey.pfx\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Password\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;myP@ssw0rd!\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwFrontCert\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzApplicationGatewaySslCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FrontCert\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"https-port-tcp-443\"\u003eHTTPS Port (TCP 443)\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#https-port-tcp-443\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'HTTPS Port (TCP 443)'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eEnsure that we have TCP 443 allowed on our gateway.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayFrontendPort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FrontHTTPS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Port\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e“\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e443\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e”\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwFrontPort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzApplicationGatewayFrontendPort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FrontHTTPS\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"ip-configuration-object\"\u003eIP Configuration Object\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#ip-configuration-object\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'IP Configuration Object'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThe last part of this jigsaw is the Frontend IP Configuration.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwFrontIPConfig\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzApplicationGatewayFrontendIPConfig\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$AppGw\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;FrontIP\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\u003ch4 class=\"heading heading-4\" id=\"my-applications-listener\"\u003eMy Applications Listener\u003c/h4\u003e\u003ca href=\"#my-applications-listener\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'My Applications Listener'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we can combine the parts above to create a listener object.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayHttpListener\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;appListener\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Protocol\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eHttps\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-FrontendIPConfiguration\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwFrontIPConfig\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-FrontendPort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwFrontPort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-HostName\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;fqdn.myapp.site\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-RequireServerNameIndication\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-SslCertificate\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$AppGwFrontCert\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwListener\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eGet-AzureRmApplicationGatewayHttpListener\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;appListener\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"routing-flow\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#routing-flow\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Routing Flow'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Routing Flow\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow we glue these two concepts together and build the route from the listener to the server.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eAdd-AzApplicationGatewayRequestRoutingRule\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGW\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;AppRule\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-RuleType\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ebasic\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-BackendHttpSettings\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPoolHTTPS\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-HttpListener\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwListener\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-BackendAddressPool\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGwBackPool\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"publish\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#publish\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Publish'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Publish\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eThat\u0026rsquo;s - Now we publish and test to see if we got it working, or messed up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eSet-AzApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-ApplicationGateway\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"reporting-configuration\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Reporting Configuration\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOk, Distraction aside, we started this post, as we needed to get a quick report on all the listeners configured, including the associated timeout each has currently defined.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the knowledge of how to work with the App Gateway in PowerShell, this request is indeed trivial to complete\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 6 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-6d5102c1fab8c52f97b24f420d4980d5-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$appGw\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003eBackendHttpSettingsCollection\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e|\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eselect \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ename\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eport\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eprotocol\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003erequesttimeout\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eName\u003c/span\u003e                             \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ePort\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eProtocol\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRequestTimeout\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e----\u003c/span\u003e                             \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e----\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--------\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e--------------\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ehttp_t-www\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003emysite\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e              \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e80\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eHttp\u003c/span\u003e                 \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ehttps_t-www\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003emysite\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"py\"\u003ecom\u003c/span\u003e            \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e443\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eHttps\u003c/span\u003e                \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Install Docker and Docker Compose on a Raspberry Pi (Raspbian Buster)",
        "date_published" : "2019-10-01T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-10-01T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/install-docker-and-docker-compose-on-a-raspberry-pi-raspbian-buster/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/install-docker-and-docker-compose-on-a-raspberry-pi-raspbian-buster/",
        "summary": "Quickly update a new Raspberry Pi, which has an install of Raspbian Buster with Docker and Docker-compose.\nDocker This is simple, as the Docker team have done all the work\nbash ShowHide 2 lines Copy code ⌄ curl -fsSL get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh sh get-docker.sh And, we can add our user to the Docker group so we do not need the sudo every time. I am using the environment variable $USER; which indicates who is logged in currently. In my case this is the user pi.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eQuickly update a new Raspberry Pi, which has an install of Raspbian Buster with Docker and Docker-compose.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"docker\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Docker\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is simple, as the Docker team have done all the work\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecurl -fsSL get.docker.com -o get-docker.sh\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esh get-docker.sh\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd, we can add our user to the Docker group so we do not need the \u003ccode\u003esudo\u003c/code\u003e every time. I am using the environment variable \u003ccode\u003e$USER\u003c/code\u003e; which indicates who is logged in currently. In my case this is the user \u003cem\u003epi\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo usermod -aG docker \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$USER\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRight, that was painful. now reboot the Pi and we are solid.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"docker-compose\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Docker-Compose\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is actually a Python script. Raspbian Buster is shipped with Python 3.6; so we just need to add \u003ccode\u003ePIP3\u003c/code\u003e to install the python packages from \u003cem\u003epypy\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo apt-get install -y python3 python3-pip\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo pip3 install docker-compose\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWow, that was a struggle, lets check we are good\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-f85c7cb115c0162208ad832f7516b5b6-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003edocker-compose --version\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Running FastLED on the Dual-Core ESP32",
        "date_published" : "2019-09-11T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-09-11T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/running-fastled-on-the-dual-core-esp32/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/running-fastled-on-the-dual-core-esp32/",
        "summary": " FastLED Package There are many projects posted over the web which implement the excellent FastLED library on the ESP12 processor; however locating a project which implements this on the more powerful sibling is a lot more difficult.\nSo, with a few failed attempts and a lot of patching samples together; I have a stable running implementation which you can clone or fork to get up and running quickly with your own projects.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"fastled-package\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  FastLED Package\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are many projects posted over the web which implement the excellent FastLED library on the ESP12 processor; however locating a project which implements this on the more powerful sibling is a lot more difficult.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, with a few failed attempts and a lot of patching samples together; I have a stable running implementation which you can clone or fork to get up and running quickly with your own projects.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe sample includes 2 different sequences, a simple moving dot; and a more colorful Cylon effect.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe code is complied within Visual Studio Code; with the Platform.IO environment; and includes a working settings file while will automatically install the required libraries, ready to compile and flash to your device.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCheck out the repo on GitHub @ \u003ca href=\"https://github.com/DamianFlynn/ESP32FastLED\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://github.com/DamianFlynn/ESP32FastLED\u003c/a\u003e; and if you have issues please use the tracker.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnjoy\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "WireGuard on a UniFi USG: Tunnels, Secrets and Firewall",
        "date_published" : "2019-08-17T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-08-17T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/wireguard-on-a-unifi-usg-tunnels-secrets-and-firewall/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/wireguard-on-a-unifi-usg-tunnels-secrets-and-firewall/",
        "summary": " Install the Wireguard Package SSH directly to your USG, and run the following commands:\nbash ShowHide 3 lines Copy code ⌄ curl -L https://github.com/Lochnair/vyatta-wireguard/releases/download/0.0.20190123/wireguard-ugw3-0.0.20190702-1.deb -o /tmp/wireguard.deb dpkg -i /tmp/wireguard.deb Create the Tunnel Secrets To keep stuff private, we will encrypt the traffic using a long password, known as a \u0026lsquo;Key\u0026rsquo;. To make sure this is unique, we will use a tool provided by Wireguard to make a random key for us.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"install-the-wireguard-package\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Install the Wireguard Package\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSSH directly to your USG, and run the following commands:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecurl -L https://github.com/Lochnair/vyatta-wireguard/releases/download/0.0.20190123/wireguard-ugw3-0.0.20190702-1.deb -o /tmp/wireguard.deb\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003edpkg -i /tmp/wireguard.deb\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"create-the-tunnel-secrets\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#create-the-tunnel-secrets\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Create the Tunnel Secrets'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Create the Tunnel Secrets\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eTo keep stuff private, we will encrypt the traffic using a long password, known as a \u0026lsquo;Key\u0026rsquo;. To make sure this is unique, we will use a tool provided by Wireguard to make a random key for us.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 6 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /config/auth\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eumask\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e077\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003emkdir wireguard\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e wireguard\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewg genkey \u0026gt; wg_private.key\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ewg pubkey \u0026lt; wg_private.key \u0026gt; wg_public.key\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"configure--the-tunnels\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configure--the-tunnels\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Configure  the Tunnels'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Configure  the Tunnels\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWhile still connected to the USG, we will now create the Interface which will be our end of the tunnel. If we consider this as a Bridge, then as we configure this interface, we will provide the address for our side and also the address of the far side.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe far side is protected from just anyone connecting to it by using another long password (key) which we need to know before we can complete this process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn this example 192.168.33.1 is assumed to be your network, you should change these to match your network space.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 29 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Set the USG into configuration Mode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003econfigure\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# We start, by creating a new Network space for our side of the VPN\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 address 10.192.10.2/32 \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Configure the Port Wireguard will be listening with\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 listen-port \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e51820\u003c/span\u003e \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Allow this interface to forward the traffic over our tunnel\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 route-allowed-ips \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003etrue\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Now, we need to tell the interface the address of the far side of the bridge\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# And also the password to allow us connect\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 peer \u0026lt;Insert-Public-Key-Of-Peer-Here\u0026gt; endpoint 14.28.207.179:51820\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Now, we will tell the far side of the bridge about our network  \u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# This is to ensure that the far side lets our network get out of the tunnel\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# The sample only allows the IPs 192.168.33.101 to 192.168.33.106 to cross over\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# you can choose to let everything by using the address 0.0.0.0/0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 peer \u0026lt;Insert-Public-Key-Of-Peer-Here\u0026gt; allowed-ips 10.192.10.0/32 \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Lets tell the interface where to find our long password we created earlier\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e interfaces wireguard wg0 private-key /config/auth/wireguard/wg_private.key\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Make the changes active, save them and exit configuration mode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecommit\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esave\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"firewalls-block-traffic\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#firewalls-block-traffic\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Firewalls block traffic'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Firewalls block traffic\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAnd our tunnel is no exception, so we need to allow our new Tunnel Interface to be permitted to let the traffic flow. In this case we need to let the far side of the bridge connect back to us; after all there is no point sending traffic over if nothing can come back !\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 13 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-2c2893b035a3e32814aa87c42bde9183-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Set the USG into configuration Mode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003econfigure\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Configure the firewall\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e firewall name WAN_LOCAL rule \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e action accept\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e firewall name WAN_LOCAL rule \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e protocol udp\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e firewall name WAN_LOCAL rule \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e description \u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;WireGuard\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eset\u003c/span\u003e firewall name WAN_LOCAL rule \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e20\u003c/span\u003e destination port \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e51820\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Make the changes active, save them and exit configuration mode\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003ecommit\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esave\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfterwards dump the \u003ccode\u003econfig.gateway.json\u003c/code\u003e and put it in the controller so it do not get overwritten\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"reconfigure-after-an-update\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#reconfigure-after-an-update\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Reconfigure after an Update'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Reconfigure after an Update\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eCopy your backed up \u003ccode\u003econfig.gateway.json\u003c/code\u003e to \u003ccode\u003e/var/lib/unifi/data/sites/default\u003c/code\u003e on the system running the Controller (which might also be a Cloud Key).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThen through the Controller Web UI navigate to \u003cstrong\u003eDevices\u003c/strong\u003e, click on the \u003cstrong\u003eUSG\u003c/strong\u003e row and then in the \u003cstrong\u003eProperties\u003c/strong\u003e window navigate to \u003cstrong\u003eConfig \u0026gt; Manage Device\u003c/strong\u003e and click \u003cstrong\u003eProvision\u003c/strong\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Updating Pester on Windows 10: The Hard Way",
        "date_published" : "2019-01-29T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-01-29T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/updating-pester-on-windows-10-the-hard-way/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/updating-pester-on-windows-10-the-hard-way/",
        "summary": "I spend the majority of my time working on my Windows machines, and for many scenarios, I find it difficult to complain. However, when Windows decides to dig the boot in and not co-operative; usually is when I grab my Mac Book and get the work done.\nHowever, running aware from the problem rarely is a good fix for the issue; My latest battle has been Pester. The testing framework builds on Powershell, and by the grace of God, now shipped as part of the Windows 10 operating system.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eI spend the majority of my time working on my Windows machines, and for many scenarios, I find it difficult to complain. However, when Windows decides to dig the boot in and not co-operative; usually is when I grab my Mac Book and get the work done.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, running aware from the problem rarely is a good fix for the issue; My latest battle has been Pester. The testing framework builds on Powershell, and by the grace of God, now shipped as part of the Windows 10 operating system.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue is that the included version is 3.4 and at the time of writing the current release is 4.6. Typically, this is a non-issue a directly issuing an \u003ccode\u003eUpdate-Module\u003c/code\u003e command addresses the issue and allow the product to continue.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn the odd case we might need to revert to a push and include the \u003ccode\u003e-Force\u003c/code\u003e switch; but for various reasons, this sometimes also fails; which is the case in this Pester Module scenario\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-hard-way\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The Hard Way\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA little research identifies that over time, a few things have evolved with this module. In our case, the certificate used for signing the modules has changed, and for obvious reasons of security, the normal processes are failing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo accomplish the objective in this case, I have reverted to removing the pre-installed version of pester, and then once a memory; I can proceed to deploy the newest release of this product.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing an administrative PowerShell session, I proceed to issue the following commands; which define where the module in question is residing on my system and then assume ownership of the associated files, which I then delete. After all, Powershell modules are discovered, based on the search folder they have been installed within.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 5 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-c6b85b4d69af2736d0e158f7422240db-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-c6b85b4d69af2736d0e158f7422240db-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;c:\\Program Files\\WindowsPowerShell\\Modules\\Pester\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003etakeown\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eF\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eA\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eR\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eicacls\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ereset\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eicacls\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003egrant\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAdministrators\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s1\"\u003e\u0026#39;F\u0026#39;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003einheritance\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ed\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eT\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eRemove-Item\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Path\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003e$Module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Recurse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Force\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-Confirm:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"vm\"\u003e$false\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow, we can put the hammer away, and proceed to deploy the module we originally required, this time without challange.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-c6b85b4d69af2736d0e158f7422240db-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-c6b85b4d69af2736d0e158f7422240db-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eInstall-Module\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-name\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003epester\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003e-MinimumVersion\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e4.3\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e0\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHappy Testing\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Starting Services at Boot on Linux: rc.local, init.d, systemd and cron",
        "date_published" : "2019-01-14T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-01-14T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/starting-services-at-boot-on-linux-rc.local-init.d-systemd-and-cron/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/starting-services-at-boot-on-linux-rc.local-init.d-systemd-and-cron/",
        "summary": "With a multitude of Raspberry PI\u0026rsquo;s deployed around the house, each taking a dedicated duty in ensuring that services run transparently; It is not uncommon for me to discover the initialization scripts designed to have these services auto start at boot is not working.\nThe content of this post is a reference for different methods which can be employed to resolve these stubborn daemons; which always are to fond of reappearing after an unplanned outage; or what is more commonly referred to as a Power Failure!\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eWith a multitude of Raspberry PI\u0026rsquo;s deployed around the house, each taking a dedicated duty in ensuring that services run transparently; It is not uncommon for me to discover the initialization scripts designed to have these services auto start at boot is not working.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe content of this post is a reference for different methods which can be employed to resolve these stubborn daemons; which always are to fond of reappearing after an unplanned outage; or what is more commonly referred to as a Power Failure!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"rclocal\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  rc.local\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo start a program on your Linux distribution \u003cem\u003e(I am focusing on Raspbian running on a Raspberry Pi)\u003c/em\u003e at start-up, before other services are started, we will use the file \u003ccode\u003erc.local\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"editing-rclocal\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#editing-rclocal\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Editing rc.local'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Editing rc.local\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOn your Pi, using \u003cem\u003enano\u003c/em\u003e or \u003cem\u003evi\u003c/em\u003e which are installed by default, using elevated permissions trough \u003cem\u003esudo\u003c/em\u003e, we will edit the file \u003ccode\u003e/etc/rc.local\u003c/code\u003e:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano /etc/rc.local\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd commands to execute the program, using absolute path references of the file location.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe final command in the file should be \u003ccode\u003eexit 0\u003c/code\u003e to indicate to the OS that we are terminating without error, then save the file and exit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e## Start our Node Application\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003eexit\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eProgram which are not expected to terminate, \u003cem\u003e(runs continuously in an infinite loop)\u003c/em\u003e should be stated as a forked process by adding an ampersand \u003ccode\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/code\u003e to the end of the command. Failure to address this scenario will prevent the OS from completing its boot process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe ampersand allows the command to run in a separate process and continue booting with the main process running.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-2\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-2\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eNote: A script added to  \u003ccode\u003e/etc/rc.local\u003c/code\u003e is added to the OS boot sequence. A bug here will prevent the OS boot sequence progressing. Recommend that the script’s output and error messages are directed to a text file for debugging.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-3\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-3\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e \u0026gt; /var/log/myservice.log 2\u0026gt;\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"bashrc\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  .bashrc\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003e.bashrc\u003c/code\u003e file executes on boot and \u003cem\u003ealso\u003c/em\u003e every time when a new terminal is opened, or when a new SSH connection is made.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNormally, we would spawn our program, by placing the command at the bottom of \u003ccode\u003e/home/pi/.bashrc\u003c/code\u003e file. The program can be aborted with ‘ctrl-c’ while it is running!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-4\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-4\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano /home/pi/.bashrc\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd commands to execute the program, using absolute path references of the file location.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-5\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-5\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eecho\u003c/span\u003e Running at boot \n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe echo statement above is used to show that the commands in \u003ccode\u003e.bashrc\u003c/code\u003e file are executed on bootup as well as connecting to bash console.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"initd-directory\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  init.d directory\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ccode\u003e/etc/init.d\u003c/code\u003e directory contains the scripts which are started during the boot process, and also during the shutdown or reboot process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreate a new file in the \u003ccode\u003e/etc/init.d\u003c/code\u003e directory\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-6\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-6\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ecd\u003c/span\u003e /etc/init.d\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano sample.py\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith the following sample content, we define a \u003cem\u003eLinux Standard Base (LSB)\u003c/em\u003e (A standard for software system structure, including the filesystem hierarchy used in the Linux operating system) \u003cem\u003einit\u003c/em\u003e script.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 10 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-7\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-7\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# /etc/init.d/sample.py\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e### BEGIN INIT INFO\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Provides:          sample.py\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Required-Start:    $remote_fs $syslog\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Required-Stop:     $remote_fs $syslog\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Default-Start:     2 3 4 5\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Default-Stop:      0 1 6\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Short-Description: Start daemon at boot time\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e# Description:       Enable service provided by daemon.\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"c1\"\u003e### END INIT INFO\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003einit.d\u003c/em\u003e scripts require the above runtime dependencies to be documented so that it is possible to verify the current boot order, the order the boot using these dependencies, and run boot scripts in parallel to speed up the boot process.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://wiki.debian.org/LSBInitScripts\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eLSB \u003cem\u003eInit\u003c/em\u003e Scripts guide\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eFinally, the script in the \u003ccode\u003e/etc/init.d\u003c/code\u003e directory should be executable, and added to the init database with the following commands:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-8\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-8\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chmod +x sample.py\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo update-rc.d sample.py defaults\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"systemd\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  SystemD\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003esystemd\u003c/code\u003e provides a standard process for controlling what programs run when a Linux system boots up.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA sample \u003cem\u003eunit\u003c/em\u003e file is provided by default in the OS, located at \u003ccode\u003e/lib/systemd/system/sample.service\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 2 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-9\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-9\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo cp /lib/systemd/system/sample.service /lib/systemd/system/my.service\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano /lib/systemd/system/my.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith a copy of the sample file, we define a new service called \u003cem\u003eSample Service\u003c/em\u003e and we are requesting that it is launched once the multi-user environment is available.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExecStart\u003c/strong\u003e parameter specifies the command we want to run. * \u003cstrong\u003eType\u003c/strong\u003e  set to \u003ccode\u003eidle\u003c/code\u003e to ensure that the \u003cem\u003eExecStart\u003c/em\u003e command is run only when everything else has loaded.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eNote: Paths are absolute and define the complete location of the runtime and any input files\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 10 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-10\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-10\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eUnit\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eDescription\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eMy Sample Service\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eAfter\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003emulti-user.target\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eService\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eType\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003eidle\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eExecStart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/bin/node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003eInstall\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e]\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eWantedBy\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003emulti-user.target\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn order to store the output in a log file you can change the \u003cem\u003eExecStart\u003c/em\u003e as follows:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-11\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-11\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nv\"\u003eExecStart\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"o\"\u003e=\u003c/span\u003e/usr/bin/node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js \u0026gt; /var/log/myservice.log 2\u0026gt;\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe permission on the unit file needs to be set to 644, and then we can tell \u003cem\u003esystemd\u003c/em\u003e to start it during the boot sequence.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-12\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-12\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo chmod \u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e644\u003c/span\u003e /lib/systemd/system/my.service\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl daemon-reload\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo systemctl \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eenable\u003c/span\u003e my.service\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"crontab\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  crontab\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCrontab is a table used by \u003ccode\u003ecron\u003c/code\u003e which is a daemon used to run specific commands at a particular time.  Crontab is very flexible and can also run a program at boot or to repeat a task or program at specific times.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCreate a script to bootstrap our program\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-13\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-13\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo nano /home/pi/.scripts/myProgram.sh\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eand then add the command you wish to execute\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-14\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-14\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e/usr/bin/node /usr/local/bin/cgateweb/index.js \u0026gt; /var/log/myservice.log 2\u0026gt;\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\u0026amp;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"m\"\u003e1\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow open crontab. You most likely will be required to open crontab with elevated permissions.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-15\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-15\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003esudo crontab -e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdd a new entry at the very bottom with \u003ccode\u003e@reboot\u003c/code\u003e to specify that you want to run the command at boot, followed by the command. Here we want to run our bootstrap script\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ecrontab\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-16\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-16\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e@reboot sudo /home/pi/.scripts/myProgram.sh\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNow save the file and exit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhen you restart the pi, the command will be run and we will get the output log file.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBe a bit careful with the permissions and making sure that your program runs properly before you put it on boot: you can waste a lot of time trying to figure out what went wrong!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ebash\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 1 line\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-17\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-7f35a8defbd32d62a4d438ac1ce1fc34-17\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003egrep cron /var/log/syslog\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Cloud Shell in Visual Studio Code: Sign In and Mount the Drive",
        "date_published" : "2019-01-04T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-01-04T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-cloud-shell-in-visual-studio-code-sign-in-and-mount-the-drive/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-cloud-shell-in-visual-studio-code-sign-in-and-mount-the-drive/",
        "summary": "After years living in tools like Visual Studio, and PowerShell; Currently my primary landing ground is Visual Studio Code. With my target audience firmly defined as Azure; In this post I am going to share my notes on how to get these two tools working harmonisly; and to make the experience a little richer, we will also mount the underlying Cloud Drive File Share of the Azure Cloud Shell on our local computer as a PowerShell Drive (PSDrive).\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eAfter years living in tools like Visual Studio, and PowerShell; Currently my primary landing ground is Visual Studio Code. With my target audience firmly defined as Azure; In this post I am going to share my notes on how to get these two tools working harmonisly; and to make the experience a little richer, we will also mount the underlying Cloud Drive File Share of the Azure Cloud Shell on our local computer as a PowerShell Drive (PSDrive).\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure-cloud-shell-in-visual-studio-code\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure Cloud Shell in Visual Studio Code\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn VSCode we will naviagte to the \u003cstrong\u003eExtension\u003c/strong\u003e icon and search for \u003cstrong\u003eAzure Account\u003c/strong\u003e, then install it.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Azure Account extension provides a single Azure sign-in and subscription filtering experience for all other Azure extensions. This extension also exposes the \u003cem\u003eAzure’s Cloud Shell\u003c/em\u003e service in VS Code’s integrated terminal.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce the extension in installed you will see the button to \u003cstrong\u003eReload\u003c/strong\u003e your Visual Studio Code instance, which you must complete before we can proceed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"sign-in-to-azure\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#sign-in-to-azure\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Sign In to Azure'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Sign In to Azure\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, Open the VS Code command palette (using the key sequence \u003cem\u003eCTRL, SHIFT + P\u003c/em\u003e or \u003cem\u003eF1\u003c/em\u003e) and select the option to Sign-in to your Azure Subscription; by typing \u003ccode\u003eAzure: Sign In\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce you click on Sign-in, Visual Studio Code will launch your browser and you will be naviagted to login to your azure account. Select the appropiate account and complete the authentication process. Once authenticated, the browser window will confirm, and tell you to return to VS Code.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAs a confirmation of your autentication state, in the status bar of VS Code a new element which is prefixed with the word \u003cstrong\u003eAzure:\u003c/strong\u003e and postfixed with the account you just authenticated with will be presented.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"cloud-shell-in-vs-code\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#cloud-shell-in-vs-code\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Cloud Shell in VS Code'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Cloud Shell in VS Code\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow that we are signed in, launch the VSCode command palette again (CTRL, SHIFT+P or F1), this time typing \u003ccode\u003eAzure: Open PowerShell in Cloud Shell\u003c/code\u003e or \u003ccode\u003eAzure: Open Bash in Cloud Shell\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cblockquote class=\"blockquote\"\u003e\n    \u003cp\u003eNote: This extension requires \u003cem\u003eNode.JS\u003c/em\u003e; If not found on your system, you will be prompted to remediate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\n\u003c/blockquote\u003e\u003cp\u003eVSCode will update the status bar to indicate it is activating the extenstion, If your account is determined to have access to mulitple Azure AD Directories, you will be prompted to select the directory you wish to work in for this session from the drop down list.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter a few moments you will then observe the \u003cstrong\u003eTerminal\u003c/strong\u003e window launch, and the session will be be entitled as \u003cem\u003ePowerShell in Cloud Shell\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003epowershell\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 12 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-31b4deb9e547f8f38ba72a1f3277af34-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-31b4deb9e547f8f38ba72a1f3277af34-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eSelect \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edirectory\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eRequesting\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003ea\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCloud\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eShell\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eConnecting\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eterminal\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eWelcome\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eto\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCloud\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eShell\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eType \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;az\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eto\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003euse\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eCLI \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"mf\"\u003e2.0\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003eType \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;help\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eto\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003elearn\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eabout\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eCloud\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eShell\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eVERBOSE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAuthenticating\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eto\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eVERBOSE\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eBuilding\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eyour\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003edrive\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e...\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e/\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"nb\"\u003ePS \u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"n\"\u003eAzure\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e\\\u0026gt;\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"mount-azure-cloud-shell-drive-locally\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Mount Azure Cloud Shell drive Locally\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor the best flexability you will regularly have the requirement of interacting with the files in the Cloud Drive, directly from your local working environment.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLaunch your browser, and authenticate to \u003ca href=\"https://portal.azure.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003ehttps://portal.azure.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eLocate the \u003cem\u003eResource Group\u003c/em\u003e which contains the \u003cem\u003eCloud Shell Storage\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOpen the \u003cem\u003eStorage Account\u003c/em\u003e and select the \u003cem\u003eFiles Service\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInspect the names of the presented File Shares, and select the name which contains your chosen authentication account, eg \u003cstrong\u003ecs-technology-damianflynn-com-1001100110011001\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFinally, On the \u003cem\u003eFile share\u003c/em\u003e blade, you will select the \u0026lsquo;Connect\u0026rsquo; button, which will present a new blade to the right of the window.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIn the blade, choose a \u003cstrong\u003eDrive letter\u003c/strong\u003e and then copy the auto-generated PowerShell Commands to map your Cloud Drive.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn a powershell session on your local machine, paste the copied commands; which will automatically mount the cloud drive to your chosen drive letter on your local computer.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFrom here you can now access and interact with the cloud drive, making changes which will appear real time in the Cloud Shell.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Happy New Year 2019: Speaking, Azure and IoT",
        "date_published" : "2019-01-02T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2019-01-02T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/happy-new-year-2019-speaking-azure-and-iot/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/happy-new-year-2019-speaking-azure-and-iot/",
        "summary": "First, allow me to thank all of you that are continuing to read this blog; despite the drought which I am predicting has now passed. I have a long list of topics which I wish to address in detail throughout the year; focused on the areas which I am most passionate.\nSpeaking Last year I had the opportunity to meet a lot of you in various parts of the globe, primarily speaking at some significant events; including the \u0026lsquo;Nordic NIC Conference\u0026rsquo;, \u0026lsquo;Cloud and Datacenter Conference\u0026rsquo;, \u0026lsquo;Tech Camp\u0026rsquo; and \u0026lsquo;Experts Live\u0026rsquo;.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eFirst, allow me to thank all of you that are continuing to read this blog; despite the drought which I am predicting has now passed. I have a long list of topics which I wish to address in detail throughout the year; focused on the areas which I am most passionate.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"speaking\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Speaking\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLast year I had the opportunity to meet a lot of you in various parts of the globe, primarily speaking at some significant events; including the \u0026lsquo;Nordic NIC Conference\u0026rsquo;, \u0026lsquo;Cloud and Datacenter Conference\u0026rsquo;, \u0026lsquo;Tech Camp\u0026rsquo; and \u0026lsquo;Experts Live\u0026rsquo;.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am somewhat disappointed to have learned that after 3 years presenting at the NIC Conference, this year I wont be returning, due to concerns of competition \u003cem\u003e(community spirit?)\u003c/em\u003e as I am involved with the management of the Azure Track for the new \u003cstrong\u003eExperts Live Norway\u003c/strong\u003e event; happening on \u003cem\u003eMay 29th in Oslo\u003c/em\u003e!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI have been accepted to present at some different conferences throughout 2019; most specifics a little later.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"azure\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Azure\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWorking with Azure Infrastructure on a daily basis; I have much to share related to many exciting technologies including \u003cem\u003eTerraform\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003eAzure Resource Manager\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003eDevOps Pipelines\u003c/em\u003e, \u003cem\u003ePolicies\u003c/em\u003e, and \u003cem\u003eGovernance\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"iot\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  IoT\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter much fun during Christmas, I also plan to share some insights into Home Automation and related technologies; Some of these are foundational, and leverage open source offers including \u003cem\u003eOpenHAB\u003c/em\u003e and \u003cem\u003eHome-Assistant\u003c/em\u003e; others integrate directly with Azure to leverage the IoT hub and AI services which it has to offer trough standards like MQTT.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI also anticipate covering some more device-specific technologies; including a standard from my past \u003cem\u003eDMX512\u003c/em\u003e, which has evolved to a new cool standard \u003cem\u003ee1.31\u003c/em\u003e. Hint - From Dj Lights to Christmas Lights; but don\u0026rsquo;t worry; I promise to decrypt is jargon on the way!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"roll-on-2019\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Roll On 2019\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf you have any topics or questions which you believe I should be able to help explain, or should be considered as topics for some posts, presentations or webinars; then please do let me know; either via mail, twitter or comments on this blog.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSlainte!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Calendar Chaos: Syncing Family, Google and Work Calendars",
        "date_published" : "2018-12-18T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2018-12-18T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/calendar-chaos-syncing-family-google-and-work-calendars/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/calendar-chaos-syncing-family-google-and-work-calendars/",
        "summary": "Assumingly I am not alone, when we sit down as a family and talk about our day, and the plan for the next days or the weekend; only to realize that we have some real scheduling issues; because you totally forgot that you would take the children to an event; while your partner had a long-standing appointment with the hairdresser.\nLetting this happen once or twice, is forgivable, but happing on a regular basis; is the recipe for a lousy dispute; that we do not need.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eAssumingly I am not alone, when we sit down as a family and talk about our day, and the plan for the next days or the weekend; only to realize that we have some real scheduling issues; because you totally forgot that you would take the children to an event; while your partner had a long-standing appointment with the hairdresser.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLetting this happen once or twice, is forgivable, but happing on a regular basis; is the recipe for a lousy dispute; that we do not need.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"synchronizing-schedules\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Synchronizing Schedules\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe solution, of course, is simple, We need to share some visibility of our schedules, and of course be consistent in making sure that we record these events in the calendar in the first place.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe problem is, however, what calendar do we use, and NO; a whiteboard stuck to the fridge or some other silly place is not an option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is a digital era, and I need a digital solution; as I can not predict where I might be when I agree with that business trip, or customer call which stomps all over that crucial other thing that I have now entirely forgotten about, and its not possible to run from Oslo to my Fridge door to check!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"environment-survey\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Environment Survey\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFirst, I need to determine what are the artefacts I am dealing with here;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-actors\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-actors\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The Actors'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The Actors\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMy Wife\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eHer Schedule\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMyself\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMy Work Schedule, including Trips, Workshops and Meetings\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMy MVP Schedule, including Product Calls, Meetups, Conferences, Community Time\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e2 Children\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePre-School, Appointments, etc.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFamily Unit\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOutings, Appointments, Events, Games, etc.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-actions\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-actions\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The Actions'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The Actions\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow, Let\u0026rsquo;s consider the unconscious actions we take\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMy Wife\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eiPhone to update her Calender\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eMyself\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOutlook primarily to manage both Work and MVP schedules\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGoogle/Alexa/Siri\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eShout at these devices to update the Family calendar\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-objective\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The Objective\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe vision is simple:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e|Situation| Requirements|\n|||\n|For Work | Ensure my calendar, offers a true representation of when I am available. Assist my colleagues and customers to not inadvertently stomp on time which I planned to use for other activities; for example, that dentist appointment.\n|Personal | Using the digital assistants, phone, watch, etc.; Maintain an up-to-date view of what my day or week truly looks like, including Personal, Family, Work and MVP appointments\n|Wife     | Requires a view of when I might be otherwise busy; so she can plan around me, when and if necessary\n|Family   | Easily setup events, while being aware of any potential conflicts which might arise, and address appropriately.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-approach\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The approach\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"family-calander\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#family-calander\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Family Calander'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Family Calander\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the shared Family calendar features offered by many of the consumer-focused cloud offerings; leverage these services, so that shared appointments are visible; while managing out own independent personal scheduled.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWhile both my wife and I are currently iPhone users; there is no guarantee that this will always be the case; especially looking at the inflation on the newest models. Accessing the iCloud Calendars outside the Apple ecosystem is not a fantastic experience.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCombined with the desire to leverage Siri, Alexa and Google Assistant; my current conclusion is that the best-supported Calander for families, for free is \u003cem\u003eGoogle Calander\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTherefore with existing Gmail accounts, we established a Family relationship and gained the shared family calendar feature.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, we Invited each other to our \u003cem\u003epersonal calendars\u003c/em\u003e so we can see the potential conflicts which may arise\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"my-work-calendars\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#my-work-calendars\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'My Work Calendars'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    My Work Calendars\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOthers essentially manage my Work and MVP Calendars; as they set meetings, appointments and so on, which I usually am obliged to join. I have kept these two environments independent; mainly due to the NDA\u0026rsquo;s which I have signed which results in lots of sensitive emails flowing which I am not comfortable being managed by other mail administrators \u003cem\u003e(I wore that hat long enough to understand the potential access available)\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUsing Microsoft Flow, I created three flows to synchronise these schedules\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSync Work calendar to my Personal Google Calander\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSync MVP calendar to my Personal Google Calander\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSync Family Google Calander appointments to Work Calander \u003cem\u003e[as Time Blockers]\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSync MVP calendar to my Work Calander \u003cem\u003e[as Time Blockers]\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-big-picture\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-big-picture\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The Big Picture'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The Big Picture\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eNow with the boundaries defined, and the flows described, let\u0026rsquo;s visualise this challenge\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"mermaid\"\u003e\ngraph LR\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003esubgraph Google Calanders\nC[\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;My Schedule\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;My Personal\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Google Calander\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;]\nG[\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Wifes Schedule\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Her Personal\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Google Calander\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;]\nD(\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Family\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Shared Family\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Google Calander\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;)\nend\n\n\nsubgraph My Calanders\nA[\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;MVP Calander\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Office 365\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;]\nB[\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Work Calander\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Office 365\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;]\nend\n\nE(\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;My Assistants Profile\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Google/Alexa/Siri\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;)\nF(\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Wife Assistants Profile\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;i\u0026gt;Google/Alexa/Siri\u0026lt;/i\u0026gt;)\n\nA -.-\u0026gt;|Flow\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;MVP Blockers to Work\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;|B\nA --\u0026gt;|Flow\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;MVP to My Schedule\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;|C\nB --\u0026gt;|Flow\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Work to My Schedule\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;|C\n\nC -.- D\nD --\u0026gt;|Flow\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;\u0026lt;b\u0026gt;Family Blockers to Work\u0026lt;/b\u0026gt;| B\nE --\u0026gt;|New Bookings\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Family Calander|D\nC --\u0026gt;|Presented Schedule\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Inc Family Calander| E\n\nG -.- D\nF --\u0026gt;|New Bookings\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Family Calander|D\nG --\u0026gt;|Presented Schedule\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;Inc Family Calander| F\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"setting-up\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Setting Up\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"google-calander\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#google-calander\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Google Calander'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Google Calander\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the existing Google accounts which you may have, establish a \u003cem\u003eFamily\u003c/em\u003e Relationship\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNext, Invite each party in the family to have read access at least to each other\u0026rsquo;s calendar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTurn off notifications on these calendars if they are not your primary calendar. In my scenario I already get notifications from Work and MVP; so do not need duplicate notifications from Google also. My Wife, on the other hand, is using Google as her primary, so does still want notifications.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"configuring-iphone\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#configuring-iphone\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Configuring iPhone'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Configuring iPhone\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eUsing the IOS Settings App, the following is how I set up both our iPhones.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSettings\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ePasswords \u0026amp; Accounts\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAdd Account\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGoogle\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAuthenticate\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSelect Gmail\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnable Calander\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eEnable Contacts\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCalander\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDefault Calendar\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFamily\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eContacts\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eDefault Account\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGmail\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eFor my phone, I use the Outlook App as the owner of both MVP and Work Mail and Calendars; As Siri has no access in here, only the Google Calendars are linked at the OS level, exposing the data to the native Calander app, and therefore Siri.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"google-assistant--alexa\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#google-assistant--alexa\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Google Assistant / Alexa'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Google Assistant / Alexa\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eSet up personal profiles, and then Link to your Personal Gmail Account; this should then expose the shared calendars also.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "My Journey to the Internet of Things: ESP8266, Arduino and PlatformIO",
        "date_published" : "2018-12-06T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2018-12-06T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/my-journey-to-the-internet-of-things-esp8266-arduino-and-platformio/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/my-journey-to-the-internet-of-things-esp8266-arduino-and-platformio/",
        "summary": "In a previous post, I referred to an embedded device which is called a NodeMCU. This device is a developer kit, designed to make it easy to develop and test programs for the embedded ESP8266 System on a Chip. Many manufacturers are offering both developer and production kits which leverage this SoC; including the Wemos D1, Lolin, and in my case the NodeMCU.\nThe function of these developer kits is to add some supporting features, for example, a USB to serial converter which makes programming a lot easier, in addition to a couple of buttons, and maybe an LED or two, for testing some simple scenarios with.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eIn a previous post, I referred to an embedded device which is called a \u003cstrong\u003eNodeMCU\u003c/strong\u003e. This device is a developer kit, designed to make it easy to develop and test programs for the embedded \u003cem\u003eESP8266 System on a Chip\u003c/em\u003e. Many manufacturers are offering both developer and production kits which leverage this SoC; including the Wemos D1, Lolin, and in my case the NodeMCU.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe function of these developer kits is to add some supporting features, for example, a USB to serial converter which makes programming a lot easier, in addition to a couple of buttons, and maybe an LED or two, for testing some simple scenarios with.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"mermaid\"\u003e\ngraph LR\n    A[ESP8266]\n    B[ESP12]\n    C[NodeMCU]\n    C--\u003e|Hosts the\u003cbr\u003emodule| B\n    B--\u003e|Encapsulates\u003cbr\u003ethe SoC| A\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOnce your development efforts are at a stage ready for production, we can implement the \u003cem\u003eESP12\u003c/em\u003e module on custom circuit boards, designed for the specific scenarios you might be addressing. The cost of the models is meager and can be significantly reduced further based on the order size. For a tiny quantity of 10 unit\u0026rsquo;s, we will have change out of €15, after Postage and Packing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe developer board, is a little more expensive, for example you can grab these from many online suppliers including my link to Amazon, which offers two developer boards for €8, seriously not going to burst any banks here.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"some-history\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Some History\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo why am I playing with these devices? I have been working on embedded technologies for over 30 years; starting with my first industrial deploying in a rubber injection moulding company, using a board from an American company called Tern, Inc; developing the code in \u003cem\u003eC\u003c/em\u003e, and running my own communications protocol across an RS485 network! This was way back in 1994! \u003cem\u003eNow, I am showing my age!\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe scenario at the time was to monitor the state of the Moulding press, ensure the safety guards were down while injection was happening, reporting temperature which has been managed by a Siemens PLC, and then using a digital scale, counting the number of rubber parts which were just created and placed in a plastic box.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e30 years later, not a lot has changed, we still use conveyor belts, PLCs, digital scales, thermocouples, and so on; what has changed however\u0026hellip;\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe computers have shrunk considerably\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProtocols are now published and supported with free open-source libraries\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eProjects are shared so development can be accelerated, and new patterns and practices discovered and learnt\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCosts have decreased, while reliability has increased.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eData is preferred to be stored in large pool\u0026rsquo;s; exposing some amazing value attributes.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"learning\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#learning\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Learning'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Learning\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eMy original deployment failed after a few weeks in live production, for reasons which are now very obvious, but at the time were not so transparent. Considering the environment, all the heavy 3-Phase machinery introduced a lot of noise, Not noise as in you should wear ear protection, but electrical noise, Spikes, and drops, which on a network of 2 twisted wires with no error handling; and a rudimentary communications protocol with nothing more than a CRC code for data blocks, resulted in some false data getting stored, or worse lost.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe fix at the time was costly. Firstly, the network required to be insulated; trough both software (firmware) updates to harden the protocol, and better error handling; along with physical shielding from the noise base; In the worst areas of the factory, the copper RS485 network had to be redeployed with optical cables, which transmitted the signal using couplers and decouplers. Very cool stuff back then.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"mermaid\"\u003e\ngraph LR\n    S1[Thermocouple]\n    S2[Light Curtain]\n    S3[Ram Position]\n    S4[Injector Pressure]\n    P1[PLC]\n    C1[Datalogger]\n    N1[RS485 Network]\n    O1[Optic\u003cbr\u003eTx and Rx]\n    O2[Optic\u003cbr\u003eTx and Rx]\n    P2[Data Aggregator]\n    B1[Business\u003cbr\u003ePresentation]\n    E1[Enterprise\u003cbr\u003eResource Planner]\n    subgraph Moulding Press\n        S1 --\u003e P1\n        S2 --\u003e P1\n        S3 --\u003e P1\n        S4 --\u003e P1\n        subgraph Datalogger\n        P1 --\u003e C1\n        S1 -.- C1\n        end\n    end\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003esubgraph RS485 Network\nC1 --\u0026gt; N1\n    subgraph Optic Overlay\n    C1 -.- O1\n    O1 -.- N1\n    N1 -.- O2\n    O2 -.- P2\n    end\nN1 --\u0026gt; P2\nend\n\nsubgraph Resource Planning\nP2 --\u0026gt; B1\nB1 --\u0026gt; E1\nend\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter some painful weeks, the solution was stabilized and happily ran for many years, and well after I had left the company.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"retrospective-thoughts\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#retrospective-thoughts\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Retrospective Thought\u0026rsquo;s'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Retrospective Thought\u0026rsquo;s\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWhile this solution completely changed the efficiency of the production line, and provided end to end visibility of work at all its stages in the manufacturing pipeline; the super important business data was locked tightly behind the code, and only leveraged to illuminate the insights from data which was determined to be of business value in a fixed set of scenarios.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eUpdates were tedious; considering every data collector had to be individually re-flashed with a new firmware in-situ. Considering that every update was guaranteed to change the data payload, as new sensors were introduced or retired; then the only option was to shutdown the complete solution for the duration of the update; followed by a number of test cycles, before finally bringing everything up; which of course had to be in the correct sequence. Oh, and the Plant ran 3 Shifts, each 8 hours, for 5 days a week, and some weekends on a Saturday depending on demand pressures. This of course translated to your truly working a lot of Sunday\u0026rsquo;s, and Early Monday\u0026rsquo;s for the first shift to commence\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn today\u0026rsquo;s world the architecture would be much more modular, with the data been deposited into a large pool; and interrogated by subject matter experts to gain insights which are relevant to a particular business scenario, or process. However when a new perspective on a situation might be required; then with open access to all the data points, that subject matter expert can dip into the pool, and evaluate the data to expose the results specific to their case.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAttempting to achieve this at the time would, well, likely have cost more than one of those moulding presses; and require that all the operators had degrees in computer science related fields.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"the-iot-approach\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#the-iot-approach\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'The IoT Approach'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    The IoT Approach\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eIf we were challenged with this sample problem 30 years on, how would we approach the project?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eI certainly promise, I will not be writing my own communication Protocols again; there is no requirement to reinvent the wheel.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eData collectors have not changed a lot. Of course, they will be faster and more accurate, but a thermocouple is still a thermocouple.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNew collectors types with much richer data, cameras for example; including heat, night vision, spectral, high speed, high resolution and so on.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eInteracting with the collectors, is essentially reduced to a single line of code, thanks to the ecosystem of libraries.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eData would be all pooled securely, enabling the correct people, services and technologies access, to build new business models.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eData models packaged into light payloads, JSON, MQTT, etc.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eNo more nightmares of In-Situ updates; Over the Air, self applying firmwares\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSecure Data communications, shielding and transports\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eStaggered updates; with no system wide downtime, or sensitive startup dependencies\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eScale, Scale, Scale\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFail Fast\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eChange Management and DevOps\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eAnd so on\u0026hellip;\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe evolution is real, yet so much is still very familiar.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBusiness logic Encapsulated as separate and distinct micro-services, ensuring a platform that can scale, while leveraging the correct tools at any point in time to address a scenario; enabling new and old approaches to be conducted in parallel, risk-free\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"mermaid\"\u003e\ngraph LR\n    S1[Thermocouple]\n    S2[Light Curtain]\n    S3[Ram Position]\n    S4[Injector Pressure]\n    S5[Cameara]\n    P1[PLC]\n    IOT1[IoT Device]\n    IOT2[IoT Edge\u003cbr\u003eDevice]\n    N1[Network\u003cbr\u003eCloud]\n    P2[Data Aggregator\u003cbr\u003eStream Hub]\n    B1[Stream\u003cbr\u003eAnalytics]\n    B2[Event\u003cbr\u003eHubs]\n    B3[Data Lake]\n    E1[Enterprise\u003cbr\u003eResource Planner]\n    subgraph Moulding Press\n    S1 --\u003e IOT1\n    S2 --\u003e IOT1\n    S3 --\u003e IOT1\n    S4 --\u003e IOT2\n    S5 --\u003e IOT2\n    P1 --\u003e IOT2\n    end\n\u003cpre\u003e\u003ccode\u003esubgraph Network\nIOT1 --\u0026gt;|IoT\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;communcations| N1\nIOT2 --\u0026gt;|Edge\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;processing| N1\nN1 --\u0026gt;|Data Stream\u0026lt;br\u0026gt;MQTT Hub| P2\nend\n\nsubgraph Business Logic\nP2 --\u0026gt; B1\nB1 -.- E1\nP2 --\u0026gt; B2\nP2 --\u0026gt; B3\nend\n\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"tooling-up\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Tooling Up\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTaking a leave from my beloved memories of \u003cem\u003eBorland\u0026rsquo;s Turbo C\u003c/em\u003e IDE and compiler; \u003cem\u003e(Which, I still have in my display cabinet,)\u003c/em\u003e accompanied with its collection of 2 3.5\u0026quot; floppy disks, and the now almost defunct RS232 serial cable behind, how do we approach these new developer kits for embedded IoT devices?\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePretty simple actually. Regardless of your OS platform, you can now leverage the rich ecosystems which these kits have established; you simply need to decide on what environment you wish to leverage and get started.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBut be warned, when I started with the \u003cem\u003eTern, Inc.\u003c/em\u003e boards, there was only \u003cstrong\u003eone\u003c/strong\u003e choice, the SDK was licensed for use with the specific board; today, however, this is not the case, and before you start on your first line of code, you can easily be overwhelmed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"hardware\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#hardware\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Hardware'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Hardware\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eOver the years a number of different standards have developed and evolved. One of the richest and possibly best know is that of \u003cstrong\u003eArduino\u003c/strong\u003e; which is a family of boards with an amazing eco-system of supporting libraries; shapes, sizes, and purposes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, Prior to spending time with this family, I actually went \u003cem\u003e100% Nerd\u003c/em\u003e, and choose to develop on the \u003cstrong\u003eMicroChip PIC\u003c/strong\u003e series CPUs; which were 100% chips, and required a special programmer to flash the chip, in my real early days these were based on EPROMS (which could only be reset, by playing them in a special UV drawer), and later the cooler EEPROMS which had an Electronic Erase option on the Programable Read Only Memory. Debugging was a different story; in this case I had a RICE Device, which was an expensive \u0026rsquo;thing\u0026rsquo; that enabled step by step debugging of the code been flashed; however most of the time, this was totally without any of the real inputs which would ultimately be connected to the circuit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThere are other boards, which I will take a closer look at on this journey; including the \u003cem\u003eMicrosoft IoT SDK board\u003c/em\u003e, which is known as the \u003cstrong\u003eMX Chip\u003c/strong\u003e, essentially also a developer board, but with a boot load of additional inputs and outputs.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd of course, the board which I am still waiting patiently to arrive, the \u003cem\u003eMicrosoft Azure Sphere board\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"development-environments\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#development-environments\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Development Environments'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Development Environments\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eWhen I first started playing with these \u003cstrong\u003eArduino\u003c/strong\u003e based systems, I of course made the default choice of development tools, and embraced the cumbersome Arduino IDE; which in many ways is still far less flexible than my fond memories of Borland\u0026rsquo;s IDE.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI quickly focused on VS Code, to use its extension for the Arduino IDE; which in all due respect is a really fantastic effort, and a revolutionary step forward, but due to its total dependency on the Arduino IDE been still installed, there are still a lot of irritable behaviors.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"platformio\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#platformio\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'PlatformIO'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    PlatformIO\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eHowever, I finally saw the light, and one day in pure anger, uninstalled the Ardunio Extension and IDE from my system, and added PlatformIO as an alternative. At that time, I also had a copy of Atom installed, as I had embraced it long before VS Code; and what a change this was.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eToday however, I am working primary in VS Code for all my work; and adding PlatformIO extensions turns development for these boards into a total dream.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"summary\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Summary\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo, after a long story, lets simply this; If you are working on, or considering to get hands dirty on your first IoT project; then allow me to suggest that you can save a ton of time and confusion by simply taking the following path:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIDE: VS Code with PlatformIO Extension\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eSDK: Start with Arduino as its an enormous community\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBoard: NodeMCU 1.0, Wemos 1D Mini, Lolin v3\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAnd all you need to plan for, is what project your going to build. It\u0026rsquo;s Christmas time, and I love lights; so join me on next posts, as I dress the house for the holidays!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003chr\u003e\n\u003c!-- enrich:containment --\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003ePart of: damianflynn\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n",
        "language": "en"
    },
    {
        "title" : "Azure Policy as Code: Escaping Quotes in ARM Templates",
        "date_published" : "2018-11-20T00:00:00Z",
        "date_modified" : "2018-11-20T00:00:00Z",
        "id" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-policy-as-code-escaping-quotes-in-arm-templates/",
        "url" : "https://damianflynn.github.io/posts/azure-policy-as-code-escaping-quotes-in-arm-templates/",
        "summary": "My colleagues and friends Tao Yang , and Stanislav Zhelyazkov have both recently posts interesting topics on how to implement your Azure Policy as Code which I strongly recommend you take a few moments to review\nUsing ARM Templates to deploy azure policy definitions that require input parameters Defining input parameters for policy definitions in ARM Templates Improving Readability Both of these topics address the core of the challenges we face when approaching policy as an Infrastructure as Code problem. However, one of the things that is lost in the translation is the readability of the templates which they are deploying.\n",
        "author" : {
          "name" : "damian"
        },
        "content_html" : "\u003cp\u003eMy colleagues and friends \u003ca href=\"https://blog.tyang.org/2018/06/06/using-arm-templates-to-deploying-azure-policy-definitions-that-requires-input-parameters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eTao Yang\u003c/a\u003e , and \u003ca href=\"https://cloudadministrator.net/2018/07/17/defining-input-parameters-for-policy-definitions-in-arm-template/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eStanislav Zhelyazkov\u003c/a\u003e have both recently posts interesting topics on how to implement your Azure Policy as Code which I strongly recommend you take a few moments to review\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://blog.tyang.org/2018/06/06/using-arm-templates-to-deploying-azure-policy-definitions-that-requires-input-parameters/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eUsing ARM Templates to deploy azure policy definitions that require input parameters\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://cloudadministrator.net/2018/07/17/defining-input-parameters-for-policy-definitions-in-arm-template/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"\u003eDefining input parameters for policy definitions in ARM Templates\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"improving-readability\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  Improving Readability\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eBoth of these topics address the core of the challenges we face when approaching policy as an Infrastructure as Code problem. However, one of the things that is lost in the translation is the readability of the templates which they are  deploying.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNot to reinvent the wheel, I am going to use the same template which Stan presented in his post, and make a small tweak to the process which he has employed to deal with the \u003ccode\u003e'\u003c/code\u003e \u003cem\u003esingle quote\u003c/em\u003e problem!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eARM follows most of the standard JSON escape sequences, therefore the following examples are quite useful\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"escaping-a-single-quote\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#escaping-a-single-quote\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Escaping a Single quote'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Escaping a Single quote\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eAzure ARM behaves nicely with a simply doubling the single quote characters; just as we apply in Visual Basic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[concat('This is a ''quoted'' word.')]\u003c/code\u003e which then provides the output of \u003ccode\u003eThis is a 'quoted' word.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3 class=\"text-xl font-bold text-secondary-500 leading-tight mb-2\" id=\"escaping-a-double-quote\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"#escaping-a-double-quote\" class=\"header-mark\" aria-label=\"Header mark for 'Escaping a Double quote'\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\n    Escaping a Double quote\n\u003c/h3\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eFor the Double quotes, we use the normal escape character \u003ccode\u003e/\u003c/code\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003ccode\u003e[concat('''single'' and \\\u0026quot;double\\\u0026quot; quotes.')]\u003c/code\u003e will render the output as follows \u003ccode\u003e'single' and \u0026quot;double\u0026quot; quotes.\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch2 class=\"relative text-3xl font-bold leading-tight text-secondary-500 mb-2 mt-12 -ml-px\"\u003e\n  \u003cdiv id=\"the-solution\" class=\"absolute -top-28\"\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\n  The Solution\n\u003c/h2\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWith this simple trick, we can replace the \u003cem\u003evariables\u003c/em\u003e definition which the guys used with the following snippet:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\" open\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 3 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-daddccdc2a2af5459502fc5ba30ac968-0\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-daddccdc2a2af5459502fc5ba30ac968-0\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"err\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;filterVNetId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[ concat( \u0026#39;[concat(parameters(\u0026#39;\u0026#39;virtualNetworkId\u0026#39;\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;\u0026#39;*\u0026#39;\u0026#39;)]\u0026#39; ) ]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/code\u003e\u003c/pre\u003e\n  \u003c/details\u003e\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am sure that this is a lot easier to read, and therefor debug; So the full template would look as follows\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cdiv class=\"code-block highlight show-line-numbers  my-2\"\u003e\n  \u003cdetails class=\"code-block-details\"\u003e\n    \u003csummary class=\"code-block-title \"\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-label\"\u003ejson\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-toggle\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-show\"\u003eShow\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"code-block-hide\"\u003eHide\u003c/span\u003e 81 lines\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-status\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\"\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\n      \u003cbutton type=\"button\" class=\"code-block-copy\" data-code-target=\"codeblock-id-daddccdc2a2af5459502fc5ba30ac968-1\" hidden\u003eCopy code\u003c/button\u003e\n      \u003cspan class=\"code-block-chevron\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e⌄\u003c/span\u003e\n    \u003c/summary\u003e\n    \u003cpre style=\"counter-reset: codeblock;\" class=\"block\"\u003e\u003ccode\n      id=\"codeblock-id-daddccdc2a2af5459502fc5ba30ac968-1\"\n      class=\"chroma block code-block-content ease-in-out\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;$schema\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2018-05-01/subscriptionDeploymentTemplate.json\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;contentVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;1.0.0.0\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;parameters\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;vNetId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;string\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;defaultValue\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;ScreenConnect\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e}\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;variables\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;filterVNetId\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;[ concat( \u0026#39;[concat(parameters(\u0026#39;\u0026#39;virtualNetworkId\u0026#39;\u0026#39;),\u0026#39;\u0026#39;*\u0026#39;\u0026#39;)]\u0026#39; ) ]\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e},\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e  \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;resources\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e[\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e      \u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e{\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;name\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;vm-creation-in-approved-vnet-definition\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;type\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;Microsoft.Authorization/policyDefinitions\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;apiVersion\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e:\u003c/span\u003e \u003cspan class=\"s2\"\u003e\u0026#34;2018-03-01\u0026#34;\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"p\"\u003e,\u003c/span\u003e\n\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"line\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"cl\"\u003e          \u003cspan class=\"nt\"\u003e\u0026#34;properties\u00